hadiths[1216]{hadithnumber,text}:
"14158","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Jafar ibn Hamdan ibn Malik al-Qatii narrated to us, Abu Amir Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Zayd, meaning Ibn Aslam, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah, the Exalted, be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked over a cleft of the lava field while we were with him and said: How good is the land Madinah when the Dajjal comes out; upon every pass of its passes is an angel, and he will not enter it. When it is so, Madinah will shake its people with three shakings; no hypocrite man or hypocrite woman will remain except that he will go out to him, and most, meaning of those who go out to him, will be women. That is the day of purification, the day Madinah expels impurity as the bellows expels the impurity of iron. With him will be seventy thousand of the Jews, upon each man of them a cloak and an adorned sword. His neck will be struck at this striking place at the meeting of the streams. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There was no trial, nor will there be until the Hour comes, greater than the trial of the Dajjal, and there is no prophet except that he warned his nation, and I shall inform you of something no prophet informed his nation before me. Then he placed his hand upon his eye, then said: I testify that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is not one-eyed."
"14159","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Hisham, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ubaydullah ibn Miqsam, he said: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad asked Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah, the Exalted, be pleased with them both, about washing from janabah. He said: Wet the hair and wash the skin. He said: How did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wash? He said: He used to pour over his head three times. He said: My head has much hair. He said: The head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had more than your head, and was better."
"14160","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah informed us, from Abu Bishr, from Sulayman ibn Qays, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: We pledged to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of al-Hudaybiyah not to flee."
"14161","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Nubayh al-Anazi, that Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: We raided or traveled with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when we were that day a little over two hundred and ten. Prayer came, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is there water among the people? A man came hurrying with a waterskin in which was some water. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poured it into a cup. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and performed it well, then turned away and left the cup. The people crowded upon the cup, wiping and wiping. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take it easy, when he heard them saying that. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his palm in the water and the cup, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In the name of Allah, then said: Perform ablution fully. By Him who afflicted me with my sight, I saw the springs, the springs of water that day, coming out from between the fingers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until you all performed ablution."
"14162","Yahya ibn Adam and Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, they said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah, the Exalted, be pleased with them both, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) calling the talbiyah for Hajj, with us women and children. When we arrived at Makkah, we circumambulated the House and al-Safa and al-Marwah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him, let him end ihram. We said: Which ending? He said: The complete ending. He said: We went to women and wore clothes and touched perfume. When it was the day of al-Tarwiyah, we entered ihram for Hajj, and the first circumambulation between al-Safa and al-Marwah sufficed us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to share in camels and cattle, every seven of us in a camel. Suraqah ibn Malik ibn Jushum came and said: O Messenger of Allah, clarify our religion for us, as if we were just created now. Tell us: Is this Umrah of ours for this year only or forever? He said: No, rather forever. He said: O Messenger of Allah, clarify our religion for us, as if we were just created now. In what is deed today: Is it in what the pens have dried upon and the decrees have run with, or in what we meet anew? He said: No, rather in what the pens have dried upon and the decrees have run with. He said: Then in what is deed? Abu al-Nadr said in his hadith: I heard one who heard from Abu al-Zubayr say, he said: Act, for each is made easy. Hasan said: Zuhayr said: I asked Yasin what he said. He said: Then I did not understand words spoken by Abu al-Zubayr, so I asked a man and said: How did Abu al-Zubayr say in this place? He said: I heard him say: Act, for each is made easy."
"14163","Yahya ibn Adam and Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, they said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No contagion, no bad omen, and no ghoul."
"14164","Yahya ibn Adam and Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, they said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, Yahya said in his hadith, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the strap of one of you breaks, let him not walk in one sandal until he repairs his strap, and let him not walk in one sock, and let him not eat with his left, and let him not sit with one garment wrapped, and let him not wrap in one garment covering the body with no opening."
"14165","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Abi Karib, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to preach leaning to a piece of wood. When a pulpit was made, it moaned with the moaning of a she-camel to its young. He came to it and placed his hand upon it, and it became still."
"14166","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in one garment."
"14167","Yahya narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to eat with his left, or to walk in one sandal, or to sit wrapped in one garment, or to wrap the body in one garment with no opening."
"14168","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, he said: I saw Ashath ibn Sawwar standing with Abu al-Zubayr, saying: How did he say, and what did he say?"
"14169","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best rows of men are the front, and the worst of them are the back, and the worst rows of women are the front, and the best of them are the back. Then he said: O assembly of women, when men prostrate, lower your gazes; do not see the private parts of men because of the tightness of waist-wrappers."
"14170","Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, Abu Hani informed me that he heard Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli say that Jabir ibn Abdullah al-Ansari was brought to his knees by a camel that had become exhausted under him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by him and said to him: What is the matter with you, O Jabir? He informed him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dismounted to the camel, then said: Ride, O Jabir. He said: O Messenger of Allah, it will not stand. He said to him: Ride. Jabir rode the camel, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck the camel with his foot, and the camel leapt a leap such that had Jabir not clung to the camel he would have fallen from atop it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Jabir: Go ahead now to your family, Allah the Exalted willing, you will find them to have prepared for you such-and-such, until he mentioned bedding. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A bed for the man, a bed for his wife, a third for the guest, and a fourth for Satan."
"14171","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) three days before his death say: Let none of you die except while thinking well of Allah."
"14172","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep your properties to yourselves and do not give them to anyone; whoever is given something for life, it is his."
"14173","Abd al-Razzaq and Rawh narrated to us, they said: Malik narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: We sacrificed at al-Hudaybiyah with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a camel for seven and a cow for seven."
"14174","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you cleans with stones, let him use an odd number."
"14175","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ata, that he heard the two sons of Jabir narrate from their father, he said: While the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting with his Companions, he tore his shirt until he came out of it. It was said to him. He said: I promised them that they would mark sacrificial animals today, so I forgot."
"14176","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with us on the day of sacrifice in Madinah. Men went ahead and sacrificed, thinking that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had sacrificed. He commanded whoever had sacrificed before him to repeat with another sacrifice, and none should sacrifice until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrifices."
"14177","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The life-grant which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allowed is that one says: It is yours and for your descendants. As for when he says: It is yours as long as you live, it returns to its owner."
"14178","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have you married? I said: Yes. He said: A virgin or a previously married woman? I said: No, rather a previously married woman; I have sisters and paternal aunts, so I disliked to bring to them a foolish one like them. He said: Why not a virgin whom you sport with? He said: Will you have carpets? I said: O Messenger of Allah, how could we? He said: Wait, you shall have carpets. I today say to my wife: Remove your carpets from me. She says: Yes indeed, did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not say: You shall have carpets? So I leave them."
"14179","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Amr ibn Dinar informed us that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: A man on the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed a slave boy of his who was his only property, freeing him after his death. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will buy him from me? Nuaym ibn Abdullah said: I will buy him. So he bought him. Amr said: Jabir said: A Coptic boy, and he died in the first year. Abu al-Zubayr added in it: He was called Yaqub."
"14180","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, and Rawh said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Ata said, and Rawh said in his hadith, he said: Ata said to me: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not combine fresh dates and unripe dates, and raisins and dates, as nabidh."
"14181","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Aqil ibn Maqil narrated to us, I heard Wahb ibn Munabbih narrate from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the nushrah, and he said: It is from the work of Satan."
"14182","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, and Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in one garment wrapped around him. Abu al-Zubayr said: And I saw Jabir praying in one garment wrapped around him. Abu Nuaym said in his hadith: And I saw Jabir praying, and he did not name Abu al-Zubayr."
"14183","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, and Abu Nuaym said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: Abu Humayd al-Ansari came with a vessel of milk by day to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at al-Baqi. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you not cover it, even by placing a stick across it?"
"14184","Aqil ibn Maqil, he is Abu Ibrahim ibn Aqil, narrated to us, he said: I went to Ibrahim ibn Aqil, and he was difficult, not reachable. I stayed at his door in Yemen a day or two until I reached him. He narrated to me two hadiths, and with him were the hadiths of Wahb from Jabir, but I could not hear them because of his difficulty, and Ismail ibn Abd al-Karim did not narrate them to us because he was alive; so I did not hear them from any other."
"14185","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated, he kept apart until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen."
"14186","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed at Tabuk twenty days shortening the prayer."
"14187","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Amr ibn Dinar informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: When the Kabah was built, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abbas went carrying stones. Abbas said: Put your waist-wrapper upon your neck against the stones. He did so, then fell to the ground and his eyes turned toward the sky. Then he stood and said: My waist-wrapper, my waist-wrapper. His waist-wrapper was tied upon him."
"14188","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah. When they do that, they protect their blood and their property except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah."
"14189","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preached, he leaned upon a palm trunk of the pillars of the mosque. When his pulpit was made for him and he stood upon it, that pillar shook like the moaning of a she-camel until the people of the mosque heard it, until he came down to it and embraced it, and it became still. Rawh said: And it fell silent. Ibn Bakr said: That pillar shook. Rawh said: It shook like moaning."
"14190","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Sulayman ibn Musa informed us, Jabir informed us, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you make his brother stand on Friday then sit in his seat, but let him say: Make room."
"14191","Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Sulayman ibn Musa informed me, he said: Jabir informed me, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you make his brother stand on Friday, but let him say: Make room."
"14192","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu al-Zubayr informed us that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he preached one day and mentioned a man of his Companions who had died and was shrouded in an inadequate shroud and buried at night. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rebuked that a man be buried at night until prayer is made over him, unless a person is compelled to that. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you shrouds his brother, let him make his shroud good."
"14193","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Sulayman ibn Musa said: Jabir was asked about the shroud, and he informed that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preached one day and mentioned a man who had died and was shrouded in an inadequate shroud, and he mentioned the like of it."
"14194","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu al-Zubayr informed us that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood for a funeral that passed by him until it disappeared. He said: Abu al-Zubayr also informed me that he heard Jabir say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions stood for the funeral of a Jew until it disappeared."
"14195","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid sitting upon the grave, and plastering it or building upon it."
"14196","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Musa said, he said: Jabir said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid a man to sit upon the grave, and plastering it or building upon it."
"14197","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ata informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Today a righteous man of Abyssinia has died; come, form rows. He said: We formed rows, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over him while we were behind him."
"14198","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Ata, from Jabir, then he mentioned the hadith, and said: The name of the Negus is Ashamah."
"14199","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered one day a palm grove of Banu al-Najjar and heard the voices of men of Banu al-Najjar who had died in ignorance being punished in their graves. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out frightened and commanded his Companions to seek refuge from the punishment of the grave."
"14200","He also informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, while the funeral of Sad ibn Muadh was placed before them: The Throne of the Most Merciful shook for it."
"14201","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Jubayr informed me that Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Jafar informed him that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari while he was circumambulating the House: Did you hear the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbid fasting on Friday. He said: Yes, by the Lord of this House."
"14202","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, rebuked a woman joining anything to her head."
"14203","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: I saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying the supererogatory prayers while he was upon his mount in every direction, but he lowered the prostration below the bowing and gestured with a gesture."
"14204","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us from al-Zuhri from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, established preemption only in every property that has not been divided, so when the boundaries fall and the roads are arranged, there is no preemption."
"14205","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us from Mamar from al-Zuhri concerning His saying, mighty and majestic: The Prophet is closer to the believers than their own selves, from Abu Salama from Jabir from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he used to say: I am closer to every believer than his own self, so whichever man dies and leaves a debt, it is to me, and whoever leaves wealth, it is for his heirs."
"14206","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would not pray over a man who owed a debt, so a dead man was brought and he asked: Is there a debt upon him. They said: Yes, two dinars. He said: Pray over your companion. Then Abu Qatada said: They are upon me, O Messenger of Allah. So he prayed over him, then when Allah, mighty and majestic, granted conquests to His Messenger, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: I am closer to every believer than his own self, so whoever leaves a debt, it is upon me, and whoever leaves wealth, it is for his heirs."
"14207","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by al-Hijr, he said: Do not ask for signs, and the people of Salih had asked for them, and it used to come from this pass and go out from this pass, then they rebelled against the command of their Lord and hamstrung it, and it used to drink their water one day and they used to drink its milk one day, then they hamstrung it, so a blast seized them and Allah, mighty and majestic, destroyed everyone under the surface of the sky among them except one man who was in the sanctuary of Allah, mighty and majestic. It was said: Who is he, O Messenger of Allah. He said: He is Abu Righal, then when he left the sanctuary, what befell his people befell him."
"14208","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: Ibn Rawaha estimated it at forty thousand wasqs, and he claimed that the Jews, when Ibn Rawaha gave them the choice, took the fruit while twenty thousand wasqs were due upon them."
"14209","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim informed us from Amr ibn Dinar from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no charity due on less than five uqiyas, nor on less than five awsuq, nor on less than five dhawd."
"14210","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ata informed us from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: I heard him say: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood on the day of al-Fitr and began with the prayer before the sermon, then he addressed the people, then when the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, finished, he came down and went to the women and reminded them while he was leaning upon the hand of Bilal, and Bilal was spreading his garment into which the women were throwing charity. He said: A woman throws her ring, and they throw. Ibn Bakr said: her ring."
"14211","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw a donkey that had been branded on its face, so he said: May Allah curse whoever did this."
"14212","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us from Ismail ibn Umayya, Abd Allah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr informed me that Abd al-Rahman ibn Ubayd Allah, or Abd Allah, Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I doubt, informed him, he said: I asked Jabir ibn Abd Allah about the hyena, and he said: It is lawful. I said: From the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Yes."
"14213","Abd Allah narrated to us, my father and Yahya ibn Main said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Umar ibn Zayd al-Sanani narrated to us that he heard Abu al-Zubayr al-Makki from Jabir that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the price of the cat."
"14214","Abd al-Razzaq and Muhammad ibn Bakr said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, and Sulayman ibn Musa said: Jabir said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no fulfillment of a vow involving disobedience to Allah, mighty and majestic."
"14215","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: There is no fulfillment of a vow involving disobedience to Allah, mighty and majestic, and they did not raise it."
"14216","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us from al-Aswad ibn Qays from Nubayh from Jabir that the slain of Uhud were carried from their place, then a caller of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called out: Return the slain to their resting places."
"14217","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us from al-Aswad ibn Qays from Nubayh from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: I set out to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning a debt that was upon my father, and I came to him as if in haste. Abd Allah said: Yahya ibn Main said: Abd al-Razzaq said to me: Write from me even a single hadith without a book. So I said: No, not even a letter."
"14218","He said: I heard Sufyan ibn Waki say: I heard my father, and he mentioned Abd al-Razzaq, and he said: He resembles the men of the people of Iraq."
"14219","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: And I heard my father say: There was no well in the village of Abd al-Razzaq, so we used to go early for two miles to perform ablution and carry water with us."
"14220","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us, and Rawh and Abd al-Wahhab narrated from Said from al-Walid Abu Bishr from Talha, Abd al-Wahhab al-Iskaf said: that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah narrate that Sulayk came while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was preaching, then he sat down, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered him to pray two rakas. Muhammad said in his hadith: Then he turned to the people and said: When one of you comes while the imam is preaching, let him pray two rakas and make them brief."
"14221","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us from Qatada from Ata from Jabir ibn Abd Allah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The life-grant is permissible for its people, or an inheritance for its people."
"14222","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us that Muhammad narrated that Dhakwan Abu Salih narrated from Abu Said al-Khudri and Jabir ibn Abd Allah and Abu Hurayra that they forbade money exchange, and two men among them raised it."
"14223","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us from Qatada, he said: I heard Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrate from Jabir ibn Abd Allah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: The life-grant is permissible."
"14224","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatada from Ata ibn Abi Rabah from Jabir ibn Abd Allah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: The life-grant is permissible."
"14225","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: I heard Shuba narrate more than once from Muharib ibn Dithar, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: I married a previously married woman, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: What is the matter with you and the virgins and their play."
"14226","Hajjaj narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, Abu al-Zubayr informed me from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: War is deceit."
"14227","Hajjaj and Rawh narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not walk in one sandal, and do not sit wrapped in a single waist-wrapper, and do not eat with your left hand, and do not wrap with the samma wrapping, and do not place one of your feet over the other when you lie on your back. I said to Abu al-Zubayr: Placing his foot upon the knee while lying on his back. He said: Yes. He said: As for the samma, it is one of the two garments: you place the inside of your waist-wrapper and its outside upon one of your shoulders. I said to Abu al-Zubayr: They say one should not sit wrapped in a single waist-wrapper with the private parts exposed. He said: Thus I heard Jabir say: One should not sit wrapped in a single waist-wrapper. Hajjaj said from Ibn Jurayj: Amr said to me: with the private parts exposed."
"14228","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Said narrated to us from Matar from Muhammad ibn Sirin that Dhakwan Abu Salih, and he praised him highly, narrates from Jabir ibn Abd Allah and Abu Said and Abu Hurayra that they forbade money exchange; two men among them raised it to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"14229","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us from al-Hakam from Yazid al-Faqir from Jabir ibn Abd Allah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with them the fear prayer: a row stood in front of him and a row behind him, so he prayed with those behind him one raka and two prostrations, then these advanced until they stood in the station of their companions, and those came until they stood in the station of these, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with them one raka and two prostrations, then he gave salam, so it was for the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, two rakas, and for them one raka."
"14230","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us from Amr ibn Murra from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, he said: I asked Jabir ibn Abd Allah about the people of the tree, so he said: Had we been a hundred thousand, it would have sufficed us; we were one thousand five hundred."
"14231","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shuba narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatada narrate from Abu Nadra, Hajjaj said in his hadith: I heard Abu Nadra, he said: That was mentioned to Jabir ibn Abd Allah, so he said: The hadith circulated at my hands: We performed tamattu with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"14232","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shuba narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatada narrate from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, Hajjaj said in his hadith: He said: I heard Salim from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari that a man of the Ansar had a boy born to him and wanted to name him Muhammad, so he came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and asked him, and he said: The Ansar did well: Name yourselves with my name and do not use my kunya."
"14233","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us from Sayyar from al-Shabi from Jabir ibn Abd Allah that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: When you enter at night, do not enter upon your family until the woman whose husband is absent shaves and the disheveled woman combs. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you enter, upon you is prudence and prudence."
"14234","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj said: Shuba narrated to us from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: I asked permission of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Who is this. So I said: Me. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Me, me. Muhammad said: As if he disliked his saying: Me."
"14235","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, and Hajjaj informed us, Shuba said: I heard Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to me while I was ill and unconscious. He said: So he performed ablution then poured upon me, or he said: Pour upon him, then I regained consciousness, and I said: None shall inherit me except kalala, so how is the inheritance. He said: Then the verse of the obligation came down."
"14236","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj said: Shuba narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: When my father was killed, he said: I began to uncover the garment from his face. He said: The people began to forbid me while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not forbid me. He said: My paternal aunt Fatima bint Amr began to weep, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do you weep or do you not weep, the angels did not cease to shade him with their wings until you lifted him. Hajjaj said in his hadith: shade him."
"14237","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us from Mikhwal from Muhammad ibn Ali from Jabir ibn Abd Allah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pour three handfuls over his head. Shuba said: I think it was concerning washing from major impurity. Then a man of Banu Hashim said: My hair is abundant. Then Jabir said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had more abundant hair than you and better."
"14238","Muhammad, meaning Ibn Jafar, narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, I heard Abd Rabbih narrate from al-Zuhri from Ibn Jabir from Jabir ibn Abd Allah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said concerning the slain of Uhud: Do not wash them, for every wound or every blood will emit musk on the Day of Resurrection, and he did not pray over them."
"14239","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj said: Shuba narrated to us from Muharib ibn Dithar, I heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, he said: A man of the Ansar came with his two water-camels while the sun had declined and Muadh was praying Maghrib, so he entered the prayer with him, then Muadh began with al-Baqara or al-Nisa, Muharib is the one who doubts, then when the man saw that, he prayed then left. He said: It reached him that Muadh spoke ill of him. Hajjaj said: speaks ill of him. He said: He mentioned that to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: Are you a trial, O Muadh, are you a trial, O Muadh, or a tempter, tempter, tempter. And Hajjaj said: Are you a tempter, are you a tempter, are you a tempter. Why did you not recite: Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High, and By the sun and its brightness, for the old and the needy and the weak pray behind you; I think Muharib is the one who doubts concerning the weak."
"14240","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj said: Shuba narrated to us from Muharib ibn Dithar, I heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah, and Affan narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, Muharib ibn Dithar informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, disliked that a man come to his family by night unannounced, or he said: He disliked that a man come to his family by night unannounced."
"14241","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us from Muharib, I heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: I sold to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a camel of mine on a journey, then when we came to Medina, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Come to the mosque and pray two rakas. Then he weighed out for me. Shuba said: Or he ordered and it was weighed out for me, and he gave me extra, and something of it remained with me until the people of Sham seized it on the day of al-Harra."
"14242","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad ibn Zurara al-Ansari from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, Abu al-Nadr, meaning Hashim, in a journey, Yazid, meaning Ibn Harun, said: While the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was on a journey, he saw a man around whom the people had gathered and who had been shaded. They said: This is a fasting man. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Righteousness is not that you fast while traveling."
"14243","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us from al-Aswad ibn Qays from Nubayh al-Anazi from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you enter at night, let none of you come to his family unannounced. Then Jabir said: By Allah, we did come to them unannounced afterwards."
"14244","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Zakariyya, Amir narrated to me from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: I was traveling upon a camel of mine and it became exhausted, so I wanted to let it go. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, caught up with me and struck it with his foot and supplicated for it, so it walked a pace the like of which it had not walked, and he said: Sell it to me for an uqiyya. And I disliked selling it. He said: Sell it to me. So I sold it to him and stipulated carrying me upon it to my family, then when we arrived, I brought him the camel, so he said: Did you think when I haggled with you that I would take your camel. Take your camel and its price; both are yours."
"14245","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, I heard al-Shabi, he said: Jabir ibn Abd Allah narrated to me that he was traveling upon a camel, and he mentioned its meaning, and he said: I excepted carrying me upon it to my family."
"14246","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Sufyan, Humayd narrated to me, and Rawh said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us from Humayd ibn Qays al-Araj from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim from Jabir ibn Abd Allah that a man of the Ansar gave his mother a garden of date-palms for her lifetime, then she died, so his brothers came and said: We share equally in it. But he refused, so they disputed to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he divided it among them as inheritance."
"14247","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Ubayd Allah ibn al-Akhnas from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When one of you sits or lies on his back, let him not place one of his feet over the other."
"14248","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, Ata informed me from Jabir ibn Abd Allah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he forbade ripe dates and unripe dates, and dates and raisins."
"14249","Waki narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us from Uthman ibn Abd Allah ibn Suraqa from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying upon his mount toward the east during the expedition of Anmar."
"14250","Waki narrated to us from Hammad ibn Salama from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade that a sword be handed over unsheathed."
"14251","Waki narrated to us from Sufyan from Muharib ibn Dithar from Jabir that Muadh prayed with his companions and recited al-Baqara in Fajr. Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi, said: Maghrib. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Are you a trial, are you a trial."
"14252","Waki and Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying in a single garment wrapped around himself."
"14253","Waki narrated to us from Ibn Abi Dhib from Shurahbil ibn Sad from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: I asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about wiping the pebbles, and he said: Once, and if you refrain from it, it is better for you than a hundred camels, all of them black-eyed."
"14254","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was thrown from a horse onto a palm trunk and his foot was dislocated, so we came to him visiting him and found him praying, so we prayed with his prayer while we were standing, then when he prayed, he said: The imam has only been made to be followed, so if he prays standing, pray standing, and if he prays sitting, pray sitting, and do not stand while he is sitting as the people of Persia do with their chiefs."
"14255","Waki narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ayman narrated to us from his father from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to preach leaning against a palm trunk. He said: A woman of the Ansar who had a carpenter boy said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a carpenter boy; shall I order him to make for you a minbar upon which you preach. He said: Yes. He said: So he made a minbar for him. He said: Then when Friday came, he preached upon the minbar. He said: Then the trunk against which he used to stand moaned as a boy moans. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: This wept for what it missed of the remembrance."
"14256","Waki narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever among you thinks he will not wake at the end, let him perform witr at the beginning, and whoever among you thinks he will wake at the end, let him perform witr at the end, for the prayer at the end of the night is witnessed, and it is better."
"14257","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You left behind in Medina men; you traversed no valley nor traveled any road but they shared with you in the reward; illness detained them."
"14258","Waki narrated to us from Sufyan, and Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I have been ordered to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah, so when they say it, they protect from me thereby their blood and their wealth except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah. Then he recited: Remind, for you are only a reminder; you are not a controller over them."
"14259","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, which jihad is best. He said: One whose horse is hamstrung and whose blood is shed."
"14260","Waki narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ayman narrated to us from his father from Jabir, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and his companions remained while they were digging the trench for three days without tasting food. So they said: O Messenger of Allah, here is a hard rock of the mountain. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Sprinkle it with water. So they sprinkled it, then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came and took the pickaxe or the spade, then said: In the name of Allah, and struck three times, so it became a heap of pourable sand. Jabir said: I glanced aside, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had bound a stone upon his belly."
"14261","Waki narrated to us, Hasan narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whichever slave marries without the permission of his masters or his family, he is a fornicator."
"14262","Waki narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us from Muharib ibn Dithar from Jabir that when the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, arrived in Medina, they slaughtered a camel or a cow. And he once said: I slaughtered a camel or a cow."
"14263","Waki and Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Salama ibn Kuhayl from one who heard, Abd al-Rahman said: One who heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah narrated to me, saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever sells a slave who has wealth, his wealth belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates."
"14264","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sold the mudabbar."
"14265","Waki narrated to us, Ibn Abi Khalid and Sufyan narrated to us from Salama ibn Kuhayl from Ata from Jabir that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sold the mudabbar."
"14266","Abd Allah said: Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi and Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, they said: Sharik narrated to us from Salama ibn Kuhayl from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sold the mudabbar."
"14267","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, hastened in the valley of Muhassir."
"14268","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let my nation take their rites, and throw with pebbles like the pebbles of khadhf."
"14269","Waki narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ayman narrated to us from his father from Jabir, he said: When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and his companions dug the trench, severe hardship befell them until the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, bound a stone upon his belly from hunger."
"14270","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, and Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Sufyan from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you eats food, let him not wipe his hand with a cloth until he licks it or has it licked, for he does not know in which of his food the blessing lies."
"14271","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, and Abd al-Rahman from Sufyan from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The food of one suffices two, and the food of two suffices four, and the food of four suffices eight."
"14272","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan informed us from al-Amash from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, the like of it."
"14273","Waki narrated to us from Sufyan, and Abd al-Razzaq said: Sufyan informed us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the morsel of one of you falls, let him remove what harm is on it and eat it, and not leave it for Satan."
"14274","Waki narrated to us from al-Muthanna ibn Said from Abu Sufyan Talha ibn Nafi from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What an excellent condiment is vinegar."
"14275","Waki narrated to us from Sufyan from Ibn al-Munkadir from Jabir, he said: When I married, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Have you taken patterned coverings. He said: I said: How should we have patterned coverings. He said: It shall indeed be. And I say to my wife: Keep your covering away from me, so she says: Did not the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: It shall indeed be."
"14276","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Name yourselves with my name and do not use my kunya, for I am Abu al-Qasim dividing among you."
"14277","Waki narrated to us from Fitr from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Close your doors, and cover your vessels, and extinguish your lamps, and tie your waterskins, for Satan does not open a closed door, nor uncover a cover, nor untie a knot, and the little wicked one burns the house upon its people, meaning the mouse."
"14278","Waki narrated to us, Azra ibn Thabit narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: We performed pilgrimage with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and we sacrificed a camel for seven and a cow for seven."
"14279","Waki narrated to us from Sufyan from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Keep your wealth to yourselves and do not grant it as life-grants, for whoever is granted a life-grant, it goes the course of inheritance."
"14280","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: My maternal uncle used to charm against the scorpion, then when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade charms, he came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, you forbade charms, yet I charm against the scorpion. So he said: Whoever is able to benefit his brother, let him do so."
"14281","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Muharib from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade that a man come to his family by night to betray them or seek their faults."
"14282","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked: Which jihad is best. He said: One whose horse is hamstrung and whose blood is shed. He said: And he was asked: Which prayer is best. He said: Length of standing."
"14283","Waki narrated to us from Shuba from Muharib ibn Dithar from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, bought a camel from me and weighed out its price for me and gave me extra. He said: Then he said to me: Have you prayed. Pray two rakas."
"14284","Waki narrated to us, Misar narrated to us from Muharib ibn Dithar from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, owed me a debt, so he repaid me and increased me."
"14285","Waki narrated to us from Sufyan from al-Aswad ibn Qays from Nubayh from Jabir, he said: The companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to walk in front of him when he went out and leave his back for the angels."
"14286","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Abd al-Malik, and Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq narrated to us, Abd al-Malik narrated to us from Ata from Jabir, he said: I married a woman at the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: O Jabir, have you married. He said: I said: Yes. He said: A virgin or a previously married woman. He said: I said: A previously married woman. He said: Why not a virgin whom you play with. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I had sisters, so I feared she would come between me and them. So he said: A woman is married for her religion and her wealth and her beauty, so take the religious one, may your hands be dusty."
"14287","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Abd al-Malik from Ata from Jabir, he said: We arrived with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with four days passed of Dhu al-Hijja while we were in ihram for hajj, so he ordered us to make it umra, and our breasts were constricted thereby and it weighed heavily upon us, then that reached him, so he said: O people, release yourselves, for were it not for the sacrificial animal with me, I would have done as you do. So we did until we approached women as the lawful does, until when it was the evening of al-Tarwiya or the day of al-Tarwiya, we put Mecca behind our backs and called out for hajj."
"14288","Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Malik narrated to us from Ata from Jabir, he said: We arrived with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in ihram for hajj, and he mentioned the like of it, and he said: Then when it was the day of al-Tarwiya and we put Mecca behind our backs, we called out for hajj."
"14289","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Jarir ibn Hazim, he said: I heard Ata, he said: Jabir narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade dates and unripe dates, and raisins and dates, that they be steeped together."
"14290","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan, Ubayd Allah ibn Miqsam narrated to me from Jabir ibn Abd Allah that Muadh ibn Jabal used to pray Isha with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then come to his people and pray that prayer with them."
"14291","Yahya narrated to us from Abd al-Malik, Ata narrated to us from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever has land, let him cultivate it, and if he cannot or is unable, let him grant it to his brother and not rent it out."
"14292","Yahya narrated to us from Hisham from Yahya from Abu Salama from Jabir from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The life-grant belongs to the one to whom it was granted."
"14293","And Abu Dawud narrated it to us from Sufyan, the like of it."
"14294","Yahya narrated to us from Sufyan from Mansur from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade vessels, the Ansar said: We cannot do without them. He said: Then no harm then."
"14295","Waki narrated to us from Sufyan from al-Aswad ibn Qays from Nubayh from Jabir, he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seeking his help concerning a debt that was upon my father. He said: So he said: I shall come to you. He said: So I returned and said to the wife: Do not speak to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, nor ask him. He said: So he came to us and we slaughtered for him a domestic bird that we had. Then he said: O Jabir, as if you knew our love of meat. He said: Then when he left, the wife said to him: Pray for me and my husband, or pray for us. He said: So he said: O Allah, bless them. He said: So I said to her: Did I not forbid you. She said: Do you see the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entering upon us and not supplicating for us."
"14296","Waki narrated to us from Sufyan from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil from Jabir, he said: Dhuhr is as its name, and Asr is white and alive, and Maghrib is as its name, and we used to pray Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then come to our dwellings which were about a mile away and see the marks of the arrows, and he used to hasten Isha and delay, and Fajr is as its name, and he used to pray it in the darkness before dawn."
"14297","Hushaym narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, Jabir, meaning Ibn Abd Allah, narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever has three daughters whom he shelters and shows mercy to and maintains, Paradise becomes obligatory for him, certainly. He said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, and if they are two. He said: Even if they are two. He said: Some of the people thought that had they said to him: One, he would have said: One."
"14298","Hushaym narrated to us, Sayyar informed us from al-Shabi from Jabir, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey, then when we returned, we went to enter, so he said: Wait until we enter at night, that is, in the evening, so that the disheveled woman may comb and the woman whose husband is absent may shave."
"14299","Hushaym narrated to us from Husayn from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: A boy was born to a man of us and he named him al-Qasim, so we said: We shall not call you by it until we ask the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so we mentioned it to him, and he said: Name yourselves with my name and do not use my kunya, for I was only sent as a divider among you."
"14300","Hushaym narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad informed us from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to wash with a sa and perform ablution with a mudd."
"14301","Hushaym narrated to us, Sayyar informed us, from Abu Hubayrah, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey, and he bought a camel from me, and he allowed me its back until I would arrive at Madinah. When I arrived, I brought him the camel and handed it to him, and he ordered the price for me. Then I left, and suddenly the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, caught up with me. He said: I said: It has occurred to him. He said: When I came to him, he handed the camel to me and said: It is yours. Then I passed by a Jewish man and informed him. He said: He began to marvel. He said: He said: He bought the camel from you and paid you the price and gave it to you as a gift? He said: I said: Yes."
"14302","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Al-Amash informed us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: Ubayy ibn Kab was shot on the day of Uhud with an arrow, and it struck his akhal vein. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered, and he was cauterized over his akhal vein."
"14303","Hushaym narrated to us, Abd al-Malik informed us, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The neighbor is most entitled to the preemption of his neighbor; it is awaited for him even if he is absent, when their road is one."
"14304","Hushaym narrated to us, Dawud informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Umra is valid for its people, and ruqba is valid for its people."
"14305","Hushaym narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"14306","Hushaym narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed us, from Jabir, who said: We were with Abu Ubaydah; the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent us with him on a journey, and our provisions ran out. We passed by a fish cast up by the sea, and we wanted to eat from it, but Abu Ubaydah prevented us. Then he said afterwards: We are the messengers of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and in the path of Allah; eat. He said: So we ate from it for days. When we arrived, we mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: If anything of it remains with you, send it to us."
"14307","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, I heard Sulayman, I heard Abu Sufyan, he said: I heard Jabir, and he mentioned the hadith, except that he said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cauterized him with his hand."
"14308","Hushaym narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, that Suraqah ibn Malik said: O Messenger of Allah, concerning deeds, is it regarding something already completed or something we newly begin? He said: Rather regarding something already completed. He said: Then why deeds? He said: Act, for each is facilitated to that for which he was created."
"14309","Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about washing from janabah, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: As for me, I pour over my head three times."
"14310","Hushaym narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar, from Umar ibn al-Hakam ibn Thawban, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever visits a sick person remains wading in mercy until he sits, and when he sits he is immersed in it."
"14311","Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What an excellent condiment vinegar is."
"14312","Hushaym narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, who said: I ate with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr and Umar, bread and meat, and they prayed and did not perform ablution."
"14313","Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed the eater of usury and its giver and its two witnesses and its writer."
"14314","Hushaym narrated to us, Sayyar informed us, from Yazid al-Faqir, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I was given five that no one before me was given: I was sent to the red and the black, while a prophet was only sent to his people specifically, and I was sent to mankind generally; spoils were made lawful for me and were not made lawful for anyone before me; I was aided with terror from a distance of a month; the earth was made for me pure and a mosque, so whenever prayer overtakes a man, let him pray wherever it overtakes him."
"14315","Hushaym narrated to us, Abd al-Malik informed us, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: We used to perform tamattu in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, slaughtering a cow on behalf of seven, sharing in it."
"14316","Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, from Dawud, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Upon every Muslim is a washing in seven days, every Friday."
"14317","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: Nabidh was made for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a waterskin, and if there was no waterskin, it was made for him in a stone vessel."
"14318","He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade dubba and naqir and jarr and muzaffat."
"14319","Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: We used to perform tamattu in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, until Umar forbade us at the end, meaning women."
"14320","Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever has land, let him cultivate it; if he cannot cultivate it or is unable, let him grant it to his Muslim brother, and let him not rent it out."
"14321","Ishaq narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Umra belongs to the one to whom it was gifted."
"14322","Abbad ibn Abbad al-Muhallabi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever revives a dead land, for him is from it, meaning a reward, and whatever wild creatures eat from it is charity for him."
"14323","Ismail, meaning Ibn Ulayyah, narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray on his mount toward the east, and when he wanted to pray the prescribed prayer, he descended and faced the qiblah."
"14324","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that a man from the Ansar called Abu Madhkur freed a slave boy of his called Yaqub after his death, and he had no wealth other than him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called for him and said: Who will buy him, who will buy him? So Nuaym ibn Abd Allah al-Nahham bought him for eight hundred dirhams and paid it to him, and said: When one of you is poor, let him begin with himself, and if there is surplus, then upon his dependents, and if there is surplus, then upon his near relatives, or he said: upon his kin, and if there is surplus, then here and here."
"14325","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, al-Ajlah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, left Makkah at sunset and did not pray until he came to Sarif, which is nine miles from Makkah."
"14326","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The parable of the five prescribed prayers is like a flowing river at the door of one of you; he bathes from it every day five times."
"14327","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you prays, let him not spread his forearms as a dog spreads."
"14328","Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham, from al-Hasan, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you travel in fertile land, give the mounts their share of grazing and do not pass beyond stopping places, and when you travel in drought, hasten, and upon you is night travel, for the earth is folded at night. If ghouls appear to you, call the adhan. Beware of praying on the main roads and alighting upon them, for they are shelter of snakes and beasts, and of relieving oneself, for they are places of curse."
"14329","Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Jafar, from his father, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judged by an oath with a witness. Jafar said: My father said: And Ali judged by it in Iraq. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: My father had crossed out this hadith. He said: No one agreed with al-Thaqafi on Jabir, and I kept urging him until he read it to me, and he wrote upon it: it is sahih."
"14330","Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Habib, meaning al-Muallim, narrated to us, from Ata, Jabir narrated to me, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered ihram with Hajj, he and his companions, and none of them that day had sacrificial animals except the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Talhah. Ali had arrived from Yemen with sacrificial animals, and he said: I entered ihram with what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered ihram with. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered his companions to make it Umrah and to circumambulate, then shorten and exit ihram, except whoever had sacrificial animals with him. They said: We go to Mina while the private part of one of us drips? It reached the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Had I faced of my affair what I now know, I would not have brought sacrificial animals, and were it not that sacrificial animals are with me, I would have exited ihram. Aishah menstruated and performed all rites except that she did not circumambulate the House. When she became pure, she circumambulated. She said: O Messenger of Allah, will you go with Hajj and Umrah while I go with Hajj? So he ordered Abd al-Rahman to go out with her to al-Tanim, and she performed Umrah after Hajj in Dhu al-Hijjah. Suraqah ibn Malik ibn Jushum met the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at al-Aqabah while he was stoning it, and said: Is this for you specifically, O Messenger of Allah? He said: No, rather forever."
"14331","Abu Qatan and Rawh narrated to us, they said: Hisham narrated to us, Rawh said: Ibn Abi Abd Allah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was cupped while in ihram due to a sprain in his hip or his back."
"14332","Muhammad ibn Abi Adiyy narrated to us, from Sulayman, meaning al-Taymi, from Abu Nadrah, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said shortly before his death, or by a month: There is no living soul, or: there is none among you today a living soul, over whom a hundred years will pass while it is alive that day."
"14333","Muhammad ibn Abi Adiyy narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu Nadrah, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to stand at the base of a tree, or he said: at a trunk, then he took a minbar. He said: So the trunk moaned. Jabir said: Until the people of the mosque heard it, until the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to it and wiped it, and it calmed. Some of them said: Had he not come to it, it would have moaned forever until the Day of Resurrection."
"14334","Muhammad ibn Abi Adiyy narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, and Yazid said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, the meaning, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, Yazid said in his hadith: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: When you hear the barking of dogs and the braying of donkeys at night, seek refuge with Allah, for they see what you do not see. Lessen going out when movement quiets, for Allah Almighty spreads in His night of His creation what He wills. Shut the doors and mention the name of Allah over them, for Satan does not open a shut door over which the name of Allah was mentioned. Tie the waterskins and cover the jars and overturn the vessels. Yazid said: And tie the waterskins."
"14335","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, I heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: A Bedouin came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and pledged to him upon Islam, then he fell ill. He came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Release me, but he refused. Then he came to him and he refused. He said: Release me, but he refused. He asked about him, and they said: He left. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Madinah is like the bellows; it expels its dross and purifies its good."
"14336","Muhammad ibn Abi Adiyy narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Jabir, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever has three children die and seeks reward for them will enter Paradise. He said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, and two? He said: And two. Mahmud said: So I said to Jabir: I see that had you said: and one, he would have said: and one. He said: And I, by Allah, think that."
"14337","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Malik, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he informed him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent an expedition of three hundred and appointed over them Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah. Our provisions ran out, so Abu Ubaydah gathered their provisions and placed them in a bag, and he sustained us until each day a date would reach us. A man said to him: O Abu Abd Allah, what would a date avail you? He said: We found its loss when it was gone. Until we reached the coast, and there was a fish like a great hill. He said: That army ate from it eighteen nights. Then Abu Ubaydah took two ribs from its ribs and erected them, then ordered his mount to be saddled, and it passed beneath them without touching anything."
"14338","Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, that he heard Yahya, and Waki, Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, the meaning, he said: I asked Abu Salamah which Quran was revealed first, and he said: O you wrapped up. Yahya said: So I said to Abu Salamah: Or Read? He said: I asked Jabir which Quran was revealed first, and he said: O you wrapped up. I said: Or Read? Jabir said: I narrate to you what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrated to us. He said: I secluded in Hira for a month, and when I completed my seclusion, I descended and reached the interior of the valley, and I was called. I looked before me and behind me and to my right and to my left, and I saw no one. Then I was called, and I looked and saw no one. Then I was called, al-Walid said in his hadith: So I raised my head, and there he was upon the throne in the air, and intense trembling seized me. And both said in their hadith: So I came to Khadijah and said: Wrap me, so they wrapped me and poured water over me, and Allah Almighty revealed: O you wrapped up, arise and warn, and your Lord magnify, and your garments purify."
"14339","Affan narrated to us, Aban al-Attar informed us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, he said: I asked Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman which Quran was revealed first, and he said: O you wrapped up. Then he mentioned the hadith, except that he said: When I completed my seclusion, I descended and reached the interior of the valley, and I was called, and he also mentioned. He said: So I looked above me, and there he was seated upon a throne between heaven and earth, and I was terrified of him. So I came to the house of Khadijah and said: Wrap me, and he mentioned the hadith."
"14340","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, he heard it from Jabir: Nabidh was made for the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a waterskin, and if there was no waterskin, then a vessel of stone."
"14341","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about the earnings of the cupper, and he said: Feed it to your water-carrying camel."
"14342","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let no townsman sell for a Bedouin; leave people, Allah provides some of them from others."
"14343","Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Whoever of you has land or date-palms, let him not sell it until he offers it to his partner."
"14344","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I saw as if my neck was struck. He said: Why does one of you narrate the play of Satan."
"14345","Sufyan narrated to us, Ibn al-Munkadir said: I heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was never asked for anything at all and said: No."
"14346","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn al-Munkadir, that he heard Jabir say: My father was brought on the day of Uhud and placed before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, covered. I began wanting to uncover his face, while my people forbade me. He heard a weeping woman, and he said once: The voice of a wailing woman. He said: So he said: Who is this? They said: The daughter of Amr or the sister of Amr. He said: Why do you weep, or he said: Do you weep? The angels kept shading him with their wings until he was lifted."
"14347","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn al-Munkadir, he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: A boy was born to a man among us, and he named him al-Qasim. We said: We will not give you the kunyah Abu al-Qasim, nor gratify you. So he came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned that to him, and he said: Name your son Abd al-Rahman."
"14348","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn al-Munkadir, he heard Jabir say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called the people on the day of al-Khandaq, and al-Zubayr responded. Then he called the people, and al-Zubayr responded. Then he called the people, and al-Zubayr responded. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is al-Zubayr. Sufyan said: I heard it from Ibn al-Munkadir in this mosque."
"14349","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn al-Munkadir, that he heard Jabir say: I fell ill, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to visit me, he and Abu Bakr walking, while I had fainted and did not speak to him. He performed ablution and poured it over me, and I awoke. I said: O Messenger of Allah, how shall I deal with my wealth, while I have sisters? He said: So the verse of inheritance was revealed: They ask you; say: Allah gives you a ruling about kalalah; if a man perishes having no child but having sisters; if a man dies having no child but having a sister."
"14350","Sufyan narrated to us, I heard Ibn al-Munkadir more than once say, from Jabir, and as if I heard him once say: One who heard Jabir informed me, and I thought he heard it from Ibn al-Munkadir, and Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ate meat then prayed and did not perform ablution, and that Abu Bakr ate meat then prayed and did not perform ablution, and that Umar ate meat then prayed and did not perform ablution."
"14351","Sufyan narrated to us, Ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir say: A Bedouin man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and embraced Islam and pledged to him upon migration. It was not long before he came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Release me. He said: I will not release you. Then he came to him and said: Release me. He said: I will not release you. Then he came to him and said: Release me. He said: No. So he fled. He said: Madinah is like the bellows; it expels its dross and purifies its good."
"14352","Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Munkadir heard Jabir say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Had the wealth of Bahrain come, I would have given you thus and thus and thus. He said: When the wealth of Bahrain came after the death of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, Abu Bakr said: Whoever had a debt or a promise from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, let him come to me. He said: So I came. He said: So I said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Had the wealth of Bahrain come, I would have given you thus and thus, three times. He said: So take. He said: So I took. One who heard him said: So I found it five hundred. Then I took. Then I came to him and he did not give me. Then I came to him and he did not give me. Then I came to him a third time and he did not give me. So I said: Either you give me or you are miserly toward me. He said: Did you say: miserly toward me? What disease is worse than miserliness? You never asked me once but that I intended to give you."
"14353","Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Said, meaning Ibn Abi Ayyub, narrated to us, Amr ibn Jabir al-Hadrami narrated to me, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever fasts Ramadan and six from Shawwal, it is as if he fasted the whole year."
"14354","Al-Hasan narrated it to us, Ibn Lahiah informed us, Amr ibn Jabir al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say, and he mentioned its meaning."
"14355","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Aswad, from Nubayh, from Jabir: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade us to come to women at night, then we came to them afterwards."
"14356","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Aswad, from Nubayh, from Jabir, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered that the slain of Uhud be returned to their places of falling."
"14357","Sufyan narrated to us, Amr said: I heard Jabir say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Have you married? I said: Yes. He said: A virgin or previously married? I said: Previously married. He said: Why not a virgin whom you play with and who plays with you? I said: O Messenger of Allah, my father was killed on the day of Uhud and left seven daughters, and I disliked to bring to them one ignorant like them, but a woman who combs them and cares for them. He said: You did right."
"14358","Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, he heard it from Jabir: Muadh used to pray with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then return and lead us. And he said once: Then he would return and pray with his people. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, delayed prayer one night, and he said once: Isha. Muadh prayed with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then came to his people and recited al-Baqarah. A man from the people withdrew and prayed, and it was said: You have been hypocritical, O so-and-so. He said: I have not been hypocritical. He came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Muadh prays with you then returns and leads us. O Messenger of Allah, we are owners of water-carrying camels and work with our hands, and he came to lead us and recited Surah al-Baqarah. He said: O Muadh, are you a tempter, are you a tempter? Recite with such and such. Abu al-Zubayr said: With Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High, and By the night when it covers. We mentioned it to Amr, and he said: I think he mentioned it."
"14359","Sufyan narrated to us, Amr heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah, and he said once: Amr heard it from Jabir, say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: War is deception."
"14360","Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, he heard Jabir: A man entered on Friday while the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was preaching, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Have you prayed? He said: No. He said: Pray two rakahs."
"14361","Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I said to Amr: Did you hear Jabir say: A man passed in the mosque with arrows, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Hold their blades? He said: Yes."
"14362","Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, he heard Jabir: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sold a mudabbar slave, and Ibn al-Nahham bought him, a Coptic slave who died in the first year during the rule of Ibn al-Zubayr; a man from the Ansar had made him mudabbar and had no wealth other than him."
"14363","Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Allah Almighty will bring out from the Fire a people and admit them to Paradise."
"14364","Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, I heard Jabir say: We were on the day of al-Hudaybiyah one thousand four hundred, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to us: You today are the best people on earth."
"14365","Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, I heard Jabir say: A man said on the day of Uhud to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: If I am killed, where am I? He said: In Paradise. So he threw dates that were in his hand and fought until he was killed. And other than Amr said: And he freed himself from the food of this world."
"14366","Sufyan narrated to us, Amr heard Jabir say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent us with three hundred riders, our commander Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah. We stayed on the coast until our provisions ran out, until we ate khabat. Then the sea cast up a beast called amber, and we ate from it half a month until our bodies recovered. Abu Ubaydah took a rib from its ribs and erected it, and looked at the tallest camel, and it passed beneath it. A man slaughtered three camels, then three camels, then three camels, and Abu Ubaydah forbade him."
"14367","Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah: When: He is able to send punishment upon you from above you was revealed, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I seek refuge in Your Face. When: Or from beneath your feet was revealed, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I seek refuge in Your Face. When: Or clothe you in factions and taste some of you the violence of others was revealed, he said: This is lighter and easier."
"14368","Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, and they mentioned a man entering ihram for Umrah then becoming lawful, may he approach before circumambulating between al-Safa and al-Marwah? So I asked Jabir ibn Abd Allah, and he said: No, until he circumambulates between al-Safa and al-Marwah. I asked Ibn Umar, and he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, arrived and circumambulated the House seven times and prayed two rakahs behind the Maqam and ran between al-Safa and al-Marwah, then said: In the Messenger of Allah you have a good example."
"14369","Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir: We practiced withdrawal during the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while the Quran was being revealed."
"14370","Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Ata, from Jabir: We used to carry sacrificial meat as provision to Madinah during the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"14371","Sufyan narrated to us, from Humayd al-Araj, from Sulayman ibn Atiq, a Makkan, from Jabir, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the sale of years and remitted calamities."
"14372","Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr and Ibn al-Munkadir, they heard Jabir, one adding over the other, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I entered Paradise and saw in it a palace, or a house, and heard in it a voice. I said: Whose is this? It was said: Umar's. I wanted to enter it, but I remembered your jealousy, O Abu Hafs. Umar wept, and once he informed Umar of it, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, would jealousy be shown toward you? Sufyan said: I heard it from Ibn al-Munkadir and Amr; they heard Jabir. Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: I found these hadiths in my father's book in his handwriting, up to the end of the hadith of al-Hakam ibn Musa."
"14373","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu al-Zubayr informed us, that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon Aishah while she was weeping, and said: What is with you that you weep? She said: I weep that people exited ihram and I did not exit, and they circumambulated the House and I did not circumambulate, and this Hajj has come. He said: This is a matter Allah decreed for the daughters of Adam, so bathe and enter ihram for Hajj and perform Hajj. She said: So I did that. When I became pure, he said: Circumambulate the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah, then you have exited from your Hajj and your Umrah. She said: O Messenger of Allah, I feel in myself about my Umrah that I did not circumambulate until I performed Hajj. He said: Take her, O Abd al-Rahman, and make her perform Umrah from al-Tanim."
"14374","Abd Allah said: I found in my father's book: Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Abu Bakr: When do you perform witr? He said: At the beginning of the night after atamah. He said: And you, O Umar? He said: At the end of the night. He said: As for you, O Abu Bakr, you took with caution, and as for you, O Umar, you took with strength."
"14375","He said: I found in my father's book: Al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, and I heard it from al-Hakam ibn Musa, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, al-Mujalid ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to us: Do not enter upon absent wives, for Satan flows from one of you as blood flows. We said: And from you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: And from me, but Allah aided me over him, so he submitted."
"14376","Abd Allah said: I found in my father's book: Al-Hakam ibn Musa informed us, Abd Allah said: And al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated it to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from Abu Wahb, from Sulayman ibn Musa, that Nafi narrated to him, from Abd Allah ibn Umar and Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever sells a slave who has wealth, his wealth belongs to him and his debt is upon him, unless the buyer stipulates. Abd Allah said: Up to here I found in my father's book, and the rest is direct hearing."
"14377","Ziyad ibn Abd Allah al-Bakkai narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whatever people among whom is undivided property or a house, and one of them wants to sell his share, let him offer it to his partners; if they take it, they are most entitled to it for the price."
"14378","Nasr ibn Bab narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade a man to come to his family at night."
"14379","Nasr ibn Bab narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said to me: O Jabir, had wealth come to us, I would have scooped for you, then scooped for you. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died before fulfilling that promise for me. I came to Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, and informed him, and Abu Bakr said: And we, had anything come to us, would have scooped for you, then scooped for you, then scooped for you. He said: So wealth came to him, and he scooped for me a handful, then a handful, then said: There is no charity upon you therein until a year passes. He said: So I weighed it, and it was one thousand five hundred."
"14380","Nasr ibn Bab narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led us in the two Eids without adhan or iqamah, then addressed us, then descended and walked to the women with Bilal, none other with him, and ordered them to give charity. A woman began throwing her earring and her ring to Bilal."
"14381","Nasr ibn Bab narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from al-Dhayyal ibn Harmalah, who said: I asked Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with them both: How many were you on the day of the tree? He said: We were one thousand four hundred. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to raise his hands in every takbir of prayer."
"14382","Nasr ibn Bab narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the sale of an animal for an animal on credit, two for one, and there is no harm in it hand to hand."
"14383","Abd Allah narrated to us: I said to my father: I heard Abu Khaythamah say: Nasr ibn Bab is a liar. He said: I seek Allah's forgiveness; a liar? They only faulted him that he narrated from Ibrahim al-Saigh, and Ibrahim al-Saigh is from his town, so it is not denied that he heard from him."
"14384","Rawh narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, I heard Jabir narrate, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to carry with them the stones of the Kabah wearing his izar. Al-Abbas, his uncle, said to him: O son of my brother, had you loosened your izar and placed it upon your shoulders beneath the stones. He said: So he loosened it and placed it upon his shoulders, and fell unconscious. He was never seen naked after that day."
"14385","Musab ibn Sallam narrated to us, I heard it from his father twice, al-Ajlah narrated to us, from al-Dhayyal ibn Harmalah, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, who said: We came with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from a journey, until we reached a wall of the walls of Banu al-Najjar, and in it was a camel; no one entered the wall but it charged at him. He said: They mentioned that to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he came until he reached the wall and called the camel. It came placing its muzzle to the ground until it knelt before him. He said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Bring a bridle. So he bridled it and handed it to its owner. He said: Then he turned to the people. He said: There is nothing between heaven and earth but knows that I am the Messenger of Allah, except the disobedient of jinn and men."
"14386","Musab ibn Sallam narrated to us, Jafar narrated to us, from his father, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed us, praised Allah and extolled Him as He deserves, then said: To proceed, the truest speech is the Book of Allah, the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad, the worst matters are invented ones, and every innovation is misguidance. Then he raised his voice and his cheeks reddened and his anger intensified when he mentioned the Hour, as if a warner of an army. He said: Then he says: The Hour has come to you; I was sent, I and the Hour, like this, and he pointed with his two fingers, the index and the middle. The Hour has overtaken you in the morning and in the evening. Whoever leaves wealth, it is for his family, and whoever leaves debt or loss, it is to me and upon me, and loss means his helpless poor children."
"14387","Abd Allah said: I found this hadith in my father's book in his handwriting, and I heard it elsewhere: Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Shuayb informed me, from al-Zuhri, Sinan ibn Abi Sinan al-Duali and Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, that Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, and he was among the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informed that he raided with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a raid toward Najd. When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, returned, he returned with them, and midday overtook them one day in a valley of abundant thorn trees. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, descended, and the people scattered among the thorn trees seeking shade under trees, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, descended seeking shade under a tree and hung his sword upon it. Jabir said: We slept there a sleep. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called us, and we came to him, and there was a Bedouin seated with him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: This one drew my sword while I was asleep, and I awoke while it was in his hand unsheathed. He said: Who protects you from me? I said: Allah. He said: Who protects you from me? I said: Allah. So he sheathed the sword and sat, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not punish him after he did that."
"14388","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Amr ibn Dinar informed me, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: We raided the Khabat army, our commander Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah. We hungered severely, and the sea cast for us a fish the like of which we had not seen, called amber. We ate from it half a month, and Abu Ubaydah took a bone from its bones, and a rider would pass beneath it."
"14389","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me, that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah inform similar to this report of Amr, and he added therein. He said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, provisioned us with a bag of dates, and he would grasp for us a handful, a handful, then a date, a date. We chewed them and drank water over them until night. Then what was in the bag ran out, and we gathered khabat with our bows. We hungered severely, and the sea cast for us a dead fish. Abu Ubaydah said: Raiders and hungry, so eat. So we ate. Abu Ubaydah would erect a rib from its ribs, and a rider would pass on his camel beneath it, and five men would sit in the place of its eye. We ate from it and oiled until our bodies recovered and our appearances improved. He said: When we arrived at Madinah, Jabir said: So we mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: A provision Allah brought out for you; if anything of it is with you, feed us. He said: Something of it was with us, and some of the people sent it to him, and he ate from it."
"14390","Hashim ibn al-Qasim and Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, they said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent us and appointed over us Abu Ubaydah to meet a caravan of Quraysh, and provisioned us with a bag of dates, finding nothing else for us. He said: Abu Ubaydah would give us a date, a date. He said: I said: How did you do with it? He said: We sucked it as a boy sucks, then drank water over it, and it sufficed us our day until night. He said: We would beat with our sticks the khabat, then moisten it with water and eat it. He said: We set out along the seacoast, and there was lifted for us on the seacoast like a huge dune. We came to it, and it was a beast called amber. Abu Ubaydah said: Carrion. Hasan ibn Musa said: Then he said: No, rather we are the messengers of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Hashim said in his hadith, he said: No, rather we are the messengers of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and in the path of Allah, and you have been compelled, so eat. We stayed with it a month, we three hundred, until we grew fat. I saw us scoop from the socket of its eye with jars the oil, and cut from it pieces like a bull, or as much as a bull. He said: Abu Ubaydah took from us thirteen men and seated them in the socket of its eye, and took a rib from its ribs and erected it, then saddled the greatest camel with us, Hasan said: Then he saddled the greatest camel with us, and it passed beneath it. We provisioned from its meat dried meat. When we arrived at Madinah, we came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned that to him, and he said: It is a provision Allah Almighty brought out for you; is any of its meat with you that you feed us? He said: So we sent to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from it, and he ate it."
"14391","Hashim and Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, they said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Hashim said in his hadith: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever has a partner in land or date-palms, he has no right to sell until he informs his partner; if he is pleased, he takes it, and if he dislikes, he leaves it."
"14392","Hashim and Hasan narrated to us, they said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Hashim said in his hadith: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let no townsman sell for a Bedouin; leave people, Allah provides some of them from others."
"14393","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Withhold your properties and do not spoil them, for whoever grants a life-grant, it belongs to the one to whom it was granted, alive and dead, and to his descendants."
"14394","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not send out your livestock and your children when the sun sets until the darkness of evening goes, for Satan is sent when the sun sets until the darkness of evening goes."
"14395","Hashim narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, who said: Sad ibn Muadh was shot in his akhal vein, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cauterized him with his hand with an arrowhead, then it swelled, and he cauterized him a second time."
"14396","Hashim narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed in a single garment wrapped with it. Some people said to Abu al-Zubayr: The prescribed? He said: The prescribed and other than the prescribed."
"14397","Hashim narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me while he was heading to Banu al-Mustaliq. I came to him while he was praying on his camel. I spoke to him, and he gestured with his hand thus. Then I spoke to him, and he gestured with his hand thus, while I heard him recite and nod with his head. When he finished, he said: What did you do about that for which I sent you, for nothing prevented me but that I was praying."
"14398","Hashim narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I have a slave girl, and she is our servant and caretaker; I go around her, while I dislike that she conceives. He said: Practice withdrawal from her if you wish, for what was decreed for her will come to her. He said: The man stayed, then came to him and said: The slave girl has conceived. He said: I told you that what was decreed for her will come to her."
"14399","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey, and it rained. He said: Let whoever wishes among you pray in his lodging."
"14400","Hasan narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not slaughter except a musinnah, except if it is difficult for you, then slaughter a jadhah of sheep."
"14401","Hasan narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no evil omen, no contagion, and no ghoul."
"14402","Hasan narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit until it ripens."
"14403","Hasan narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever plunders a plunder is not of us."
"14404","Hasan narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: We used to sharecrop in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we would get some unripe dates and such, then he said: Whoever has land, let him cultivate it or have his brother plow it for him, otherwise let him leave it."
"14405","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jubayr ibn Shaybah, who heard Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Jafar: I asked Jabir: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid fasting on Friday. He said: Yes, by the Lord of this House. Then it was said to Sufyan, while he was circumambulating the House: Yes."
"14406","Ibn Idris narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj informed us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned the first Jamrah on the Day of Sacrifice in the forenoon, and stoned it after that at the decline of the sun."
"14407","Ibn Idris narrated to us from al-Amash from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed there is in the night an hour which no Muslim servant coincides with while asking Allah for good therein except He gives it to him, and that is in every night."
"14408","Ibn Idris narrated to us from Husayn from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from Jabir, he said: A caravan once came to Madinah while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon, so the people left and twelve remained, then was revealed: And when they see trade or amusement they disperse toward it."
"14409","Ismail, meaning Ibn Ulayyah, narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, and Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, and Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes my name, let him not use my kunyah, and whoever uses my kunyah, let him not take my name."
"14410","Ismail narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade muhaqalah, muzabanah, mukhabarah, muawamah, thunya, and he permitted arayas."
"14411","Jarir narrated to us from Mughirah from al-Shabi from Jabir, he said: Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Haram, meaning his father, died or was martyred, and he owed a debt, so I sought the help of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with his creditors to remit something of his debt, and he asked them but they refused, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Go and sort your dates into kinds, the Ajwah by itself, and Idhq Zayd by itself, and its kinds, then send for me. He said: So I did, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and sat upon its top or in its middle, then he said: Measure out for the people. He said: So I measured out for the people until I paid them in full, and my dates remained as if nothing had decreased from them."
"14412","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir and Ibn al-Zubayr, meaning that he stoned the Jamrah with pebbles like the pebbles of khadhf."
"14413","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr informed me from Jabir from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he stoned with pebbles like the pebbles of khadhf."
"14414","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah: Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari informed me, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever revives a dead land, he has a reward for it, and whatever wild creatures eat from it, he has a reward for it."
"14415","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Salim from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: A man from the Ansar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have a servant girl who draws water, and he once said draws water, upon a camel of mine, and I used to practice coitus interruptus with her while also having intercourse with her, and she bore a child, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever soul Allah has decreed to create, it will surely come to be."
"14416","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Salim from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take my name but do not use my kunyah, for I was made a divider, dividing among you."
"14417","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take my name but do not use my kunyah."
"14418","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Salih from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in his Hajj: Which day has the greatest sanctity. They said: This day of ours. He said: Then which month has the greatest sanctity. They said: This month of ours. He said: Then which land has the greatest sanctity. They said: This land of ours. He said: Then indeed your blood and your wealth are forbidden to you like the sanctity of this day of yours in this month of yours in this land of yours."
"14419","Abu Muawiyah and Ibn Numayr narrated to us, they said: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and Ibn Numayr said in his hadith: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed Satan has despaired of being worshipped by those who pray, but in stirring discord among them."
"14420","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Salih from Jabir, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he asked for water, then a man said: Shall I not give you nabidh to drink. He said: Yes. He said: So the man went out hurrying. He said: Then he brought a vessel containing nabidh, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you not cover it, even by placing a stick across it. He said: Then he drank."
"14421","Abu Muawiyah, Yala, and Waki narrated to us, they said: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which prayer is best. He said: Lengthy standing."
"14422","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: Abd al-Malik narrated to us from Ata from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began with the prayer before the sermon on the two Eids, without adhan and without iqamah. He said: Then he addressed the men while leaning upon a bow. He said: Then he went to the women and addressed them and urged them to give charity. He said: So they began throwing earrings, rings, and jewelry to Bilal. He said: And he did not pray before the prayer nor after it."
"14423","Ibn Numayr narrated to us: Ashath narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: We performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and with us were women and children, and we stoned on their behalf."
"14424","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: Hajjaj narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling palm trees for two years and three years ahead."
"14425","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no living soul that a hundred years will come upon it and it remains."
"14426","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: One of our companions narrated to us from al-Amash from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies upon something, Allah will resurrect him upon it."
"14427","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: al-Zubayr is the son of my paternal aunt and my disciple from my ummah."
"14428","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Hisham, and I narrated it to Wahb ibn Kaysan and he said: I bear witness that Jabir ibn Abdillah narrated to me, he said: The matter became severe on the Day of the Trench, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is there not a man who will bring us news of Banu Qurayzah. So al-Zubayr went and brought their news, then the matter became severe again, and he mentioned three times, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed every prophet has a disciple, and al-Zubayr is my disciple."
"14429","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, and al-Amash narrated to us from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and when we drew near Madinah, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am newly married, so permit me to hasten to my family. He said: Have you married. He said: I said: Yes. He said: A virgin or a previously married woman. He said: I said: A previously married woman. He said: Why not a virgin whom you play with and who plays with you. He said: I said: Abdullah died and left young girls under my care, so I disliked bringing to them one like them, then he said: Do not come to your family by night. He said: And I was upon a camel that had become exhausted. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) caught up with me while I was at the rear of the people. He said: Then he said: What is wrong with you, O Jabir. He said: I said: My camel has become exhausted. He said: So he took hold of its tail then prodded it. He said: So I kept on being at the front of the people, its head worrying me, and when we drew near Madinah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: What happened to the camel. I said: Here it is. He said: Then sell it to me. I said: No, rather it is yours. He said: Sell it to me. He said: I said: It is yours. He said: No, I have taken it for an uqiyyah. Ride it, and when you arrive, bring it to us. He said: So when I arrived in Madinah I brought it to him, then he said: O Bilal, weigh out for him an uqiyyah and add to him a qirat. He said: I said: This is a qirat which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) added for me, it shall never part from me until I die. He said: So I put it in a pouch, and it remained with me until the people of Syria came on the Day of al-Harrah and took it among what they took."
"14430","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Iblis places his throne upon the water, then he sends out his troops, and the closest of them to him in station is the greatest of them in trial. One of them comes and says: I did such and such, and he says: You have done nothing. He said: And one of them comes and says: I did not leave him until I separated between him and his family. He said: So he brings him close to him, or he said: He embraces him, and says: What an excellent man you are. Abu Muawiyah once said: So he brings him close to him."
"14431","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey. He said: Then a severe wind blew, so he said: This is for the death of a hypocrite. He said: So when we arrived in Madinah, behold a great hypocrite among the great hypocrites had died."
"14432","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a physician to Ubayy ibn Kab, and he cut a vein for him then cauterized over it."
"14433","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram for Hajj in his Hajj."
"14434","Abu Muawiyah and Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, they said: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever among you fears that he will not stand at the end of the night, let him pray witr at the beginning of the night, for the recitation at the end of the night is witnessed, and that is better."
"14435","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us, and Ibn Numayr from al-Amash from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade ruqyah. Ibn Numayr said in his hadith: Then my maternal uncle came to him, and he used to treat the scorpion sting by ruqyah. He said: Then the family of Amr ibn Hazm came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we had a ruqyah with which we treated the scorpion sting, and you have forbidden ruqyah. He said: So they presented it to him, then he said: I see no harm. Whoever among you is able to benefit his brother, let him benefit him."
"14436","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw last night in what the sleeper sees as if my neck was struck and my head fell, so I followed it and took it and put it back in its place, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Satan toys with one of you, let him not narrate it to the people."
"14437","Abu Muawiyah and Waki narrated to us, they said: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prostrates, let him be balanced and not spread his forearms as the dog spreads them."
"14438","Abu Muawiyah and Ibn Abi Ghaniyyah, with the same meaning, narrated to us, they said: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Umm Salamah. Ibn Abi Ghaniyyah said: He entered upon Aishah with a boy whose nostrils were flowing with blood. Abu Muawiyah said in his hadith: And with her was a boy whose nostrils were gushing blood. He said: Then he said: What is wrong with him. He said: Then they said: He has udhrah. He said: Then he said: Why do you torment your children. It suffices one of you to take Indian costus, rub it with water seven times, then pour it into his mouth. Ibn Abi Ghaniyyah said: Then administer it to him as nasal drops. So they did, and he recovered."
"14439","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us, and Ibn Numayr from al-Amash from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying three days before his death: Let none of you die except while thinking well of Allah."
"14440","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no male nor female except upon his head is silk tied with three knots when he sleeps. If he wakes and remembers Allah the Exalted, one knot is untied, and when he stands and performs ablution, one knot is untied, and when he stands for prayer, all his knots are untied."
"14441","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash informed us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the morsel of one of you falls, let him take it and remove what is on it of harm and eat it, and not leave it for Satan."
"14442","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The food of one suffices two, and the food of two suffices four."
"14443","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you eats, let him not wipe his hand until he licks it, for he does not know in which food blessing is given to him."
"14444","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you attends prayer in a mosque, let him make for his house a share of his prayer, for Allah the Mighty and Majestic will place in his house good from his prayer."
"14445","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw people performing ablution while water had not touched their heels, so he said: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"14446","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: Fever sought permission upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Who is this. She said: Umm Mildam. He said: Then he ordered her to the people of Quba, and they suffered from it what Allah knows, then they came to him and complained of that to him, so he said: As you wish. If you wish, I will supplicate Allah for you and He will remove it from you, and if you wish, it will be a purification for you. They said: O Messenger of Allah, will you do that. He said: Yes. They said: Then leave it."
"14447","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us from al-Amash, and Ibn Numayr informed us: al-Amash from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: al-Numan ibn Qawqal came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me, if I make lawful the lawful and forbid the unlawful and pray the prescribed prayers, and Ibn Numayr said in his hadith: And I do not add to that, shall I enter Paradise. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Yes."
"14448","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you finishes prayer in his mosque, let him make for his house a share of his prayer, for Allah the Mighty and Majestic will place in his house good from his prayer."
"14449","Ibn Numayr narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When one of you finishes, then he mentioned it."
"14450","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me about Umrah, is it obligatory. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, and that you perform Umrah is better for you."
"14451","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drove seventy sacrificial camels in the year of Hudaybiyah. He said: Then he sacrificed each camel on behalf of seven."
"14452","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us from Abu Nadrah from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), some of us fasting and some of us breaking the fast, and neither would find fault with the other."
"14453","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Throne of Allah shook for the death of Sad ibn Muadh."
"14454","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise eat and drink therein, and do not defecate, urinate, blow their noses, or spit. Their food is belching and sweat like the sweat of musk."
"14455","Ismail narrated to us: Layth informed us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: Abu Quhafah was brought on the Day of the Conquest to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while his head was as if it were thaghamah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take him to one of his women and let her change it with something, and keep him away from black."
"14456","Ismail narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Preemption is in every partnership, in land or a wall. It is not lawful for him to sell until he informs his partner, and if he sells, he has more right to it until he informs him."
"14457","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the caller to prayer calls, Satan flees until he is at al-Rawha, which is thirty miles from Madinah."
"14458","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: Sulayk al-Ghatafani came on Friday while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon, then he sat, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes on Friday while the imam is delivering the sermon, let him pray two rakahs then sit."
"14459","Ismail, he is Ibn Ulayyah, narrated to us from al-Jurayri from Abu Nadrah, he said: We were with Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: The people of Iraq are about to receive neither qafiz nor dirham. We said: From where is that. He said: From the non-Arabs, they will withhold that. Then he said: The people of Syria are about to receive neither dinar nor mudd. We said: From where is that. From the Romans, they will withhold that. He said: Then he paused a while, then he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be at the end of my ummah a caliph who will scoop wealth scooping, not counting it counting. al-Jurayri said: So I said to Abu Nadrah and Abu al-Ala: Do you consider him to be Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him. So they said: No."
"14460","Ismail narrated to us from al-Hajjaj al-Sawwaf from Abu al-Zubayr, if Allah wills, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O assembly of the Ansar, withhold your properties and do not grant them as umra, for whoever is granted something for his lifetime, it is his for his life and his death."
"14461","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of the five prayers is like a flowing abundant river at the door of one of you, bathing from it every day five times."
"14462","Ismail narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj informed us from Ata, he said: Jabir ibn Abdillah said: We, the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), entered ihram for Hajj purely with nothing else with it, purely alone, then we arrived in Makkah on the morning of the fourth that had passed of Dhu al-Hijjah, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Release your ihram and make it Umrah. Then it reached him that we were saying: Since there are only five days between us and Arafah, he orders us to release our ihram so that some of us will go to Mina while our private parts drip with semen, so he addressed us and said: What you said has reached me, and I am indeed the most pious of you and the most righteous of you, and were it not for the sacrificial animal I would have released my ihram, and had I faced of my affair what I now know, I would not have brought the sacrificial animal. Release your ihram and make it Umrah. He said: And Ali, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, arrived from Yemen. He said: With what did you enter ihram. He said: With what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram with. He said: Then offer the sacrifice and remain forbidden as you are."
"14463","Ismail narrated to us from Shubah from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad ibn Zurarah from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey, he saw a crowd and a man who was shaded over, so he asked about him, and they said: This is a fasting man, then he said: Righteousness is not to fast while traveling."
"14464","Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us from al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of a dog except a trained dog."
"14465","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj: Ata informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: We used not to eat of the meat of the sacrificial camels except for three days of Mina, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted us, he said: Eat and take provisions. He said: So we ate and took provisions. I said to Ata: Until we came to Madinah. He said: No."
"14466","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj: Abu al-Zubayr informed me, he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah asking about riding the sacrificial animal, then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Ride it properly when you are compelled to it until you find another mount."
"14467","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj: Abu al-Zubayr informed me, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: Neither the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) nor his companions circumambulated between al-Safa and al-Marwah except once, his first circumambulation."
"14468","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated in the Farewell Hajj upon his mount, the House and al-Safa and al-Marwah, so that the people could see him and so he could be above them and they could ask him, for the people crowded around him."
"14469","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Abd al-Malik: Ata informed me from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mixing fresh ripe dates with unripe dates, and dates with raisins."
"14470","Yahya narrated to us from Abd al-Malik: Ata informed me from Jabir, he said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and that was the day on which Ibrahim, peace be upon him, the son of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), died, so the people said: The sun only eclipsed for the death of Ibrahim, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and prayed with the people six bowings in four prostrations. He said takbir then recited and lengthened the recitation, then he bowed about as long as he stood, then he raised his head and recited less than the first recitation, then he bowed about as long as he stood, then he raised his head and recited less than the second recitation, then he bowed about as long as he stood, then he raised his head and went down to prostration and prostrated twice, then he stood and bowed three bowings before prostrating, in which no bowing was but the one before it was longer than the one after it, except that his bowing was about as his standing. Then he moved backward in his prayer and the rows moved backward with him, then he moved forward and stood in his place and the rows moved forward, then he finished the prayer while the sun had risen, then he said: O people, indeed the sun and the moon are two signs from the signs of Allah the Mighty and Majestic, and they do not eclipse for the death of a human. When you see anything of that, pray until it clears. Indeed there is nothing you are promised except I have seen it in this prayer of mine. The Fire was indeed brought, and that was when you saw me move backward for fear its heat would strike me, until I said: My Lord, while I am among them. And I saw therein the man with the hooked staff dragging his intestines in the Fire. He used to steal from the pilgrims with his hooked staff. If he was detected, he said: It only caught upon my staff, and if he was unnoticed, he went away with it. And I saw therein the woman with the cat which she tied up and neither fed it nor left it to eat from the vermin of the earth until it died of hunger. And Paradise was brought, and that was when you saw me move forward until I stood in my place, then I stretched my hand wanting to take of its fruit so you could look at it, then it occurred to me not to do so."
"14471","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj: Abu al-Zubayr informed me, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying, while informing about the Hajj of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Then he ordered us after we circumambulated to release our ihram. He said: And when you intend to set out to Mina, enter ihram. So we entered ihram from al-Batha."
"14472","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir saying: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoning upon his mount on the Day of Sacrifice, saying to us: Take your rites, for I do not know, perhaps I will not perform Hajj after this Hajj of mine."
"14473","Yahya narrated to us from Abd al-Malik: Ata narrated to us from Jabir, he said: I witnessed the prayer with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a day of Eid, and he began with the prayer before the sermon, without adhan and without iqamah. When he finished the prayer, he stood leaning upon Bilal, and praised Allah and extolled Him, and admonished the people and reminded them and urged them to obey Him, then he went to the women, and with him was Bilal, and he ordered them to fear Allah and admonished them, and praised Allah and extolled Him and urged them to obey Him, then he said: Give charity, for most of you are the fuel of Hell. Then a woman from the lowly women with dark spots on her cheeks said: Why, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Because you complain much and deny the husband. So they began taking off their jewelry, necklaces, earrings, and rings, throwing them into the garment of Bilal, giving them in charity."
"14474","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us: Abd al-Malik narrated to us from Ata from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: I witnessed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a day of Eid, and he began with the prayer before the sermon, then he mentioned its meaning."
"14475","Yahya narrated to us from Abd al-Malik from Ata from Jabir, he said: We performed tamattu with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we slaughtered a cow on behalf of seven, sharing in it."
"14476","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj: Abu al-Zubayr informed me, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing anything of animals by confinement."
"14477","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj: Abu al-Zubayr informed me, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us from branding in the face and striking in the face."
"14478","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj: Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr informed me that Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Ammar informed him, he said: I asked Jabir, and I said: The hyena, may I eat it. He said: Yes. He said: I said: Is it game. He said: Yes. I said: Did you hear that from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Yes."
"14479","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Shubah: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Hasan from Jabir ibn Abdillah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey and saw a man with a crowd around him who was shaded over, so he said: What is this. They said: A fasting man. He said: Fasting while traveling is not righteousness, or: The fasting traveler is not righteous."
"14480","Yahya narrated to us from Hisham, and Abd al-Wahhab al-Khaffaf narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Ubaydullah ibn Miqsam from Jabir, he said: A funeral passed by us, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood for it, and we stood with him, then I said: O Messenger of Allah, it is the funeral of a Jew. He said: Indeed death is a fright, so when you see a funeral, stand."
"14481","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Abi Arubah from Qatadah from al-Nadr ibn Anas from Bashir ibn Nahik from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Umra is an inheritance for its people, or a gift for its people. Yahya narrated to us."
"14482","Ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us from Qatadah from Ata from Jabir from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly, like it. Thus said Yahya."
"14483","Yahya narrated to us from Jafar: My father narrated to me, he said: Jabir said to me, he said: Your cousin al-Hasan ibn Muhammad asked me about the bath for major impurity, so I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pour with his hands upon his head three times. Then he said: I have thick hair. So I said: Hush, O son of my brother, the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was thicker than your hair and better."
"14484","Yahya narrated to us from Jafar: My father narrated to me from Jabir ibn Abdillah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in his sermon after the tashahhud: Indeed the best speech is the Book of Allah the Mighty and Majestic, and the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad. Yahya said: And I know only that he said: And the worst of matters are invented ones. And when he mentioned the Hour, he raised his voice with it and his anger intensified as if he were warning of an army, then he would say: I was sent and the Hour like these two, and he gestured, and Yahya described with the index and middle fingers."
"14485","Yahya narrated to us from Misar: Muharib narrated to me, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) owed me a debt, so he repaid me and added to me, and he was in the mosque, then he said to me: Pray two rakahs."
"14486","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj: Ata narrated to us from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Today a righteous servant of Allah, Ashamah, has died, so stand and pray over him. Then he stood and led us and prayed over him."
"14487","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj: Ata narrated to us from Jabir from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Lock your door and mention the name of Allah the Mighty and Majestic, for Satan does not open a locked door. Extinguish your lamp and mention the name of Allah, cover your vessel even with a stick you place across it, and mention the name of Allah, and tie your waterskin and mention the name of Allah the Mighty and Majestic."
"14488","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj: Abu al-Zubayr informed me, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoning on the Day of Sacrifice in the forenoon alone, and as for after that, then after the decline of the sun."
"14489","Yahya narrated to us from Abd al-Malik: Ata narrated to me from Jabir ibn Abdillah that he prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the fear prayer, and he mentioned that the enemy were between him and the qiblah, and we lined up behind him in two rows. Then he said takbir and we said takbir with him all together, then he bowed and we bowed with him all together. When he raised his head from bowing, he prostrated and the row next to him prostrated with him, while the rear row stood facing the enemy. When he stood and the row next to him stood with him, the rear row went down in prostration. Then the rear row moved forward and the front row moved backward, then he bowed and we bowed with him all together, then he prostrated and the row next to him prostrated with him. When the row next to him prostrated and sat, the rear row went down in prostration. Then he gave salam and we gave salam all together. Jabir said: As these guards of yours do with their commanders."
"14490","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir saying: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoning the Jamrah with the pebbles of khadhf."
"14491","Yahya narrated to us: Salim ibn Hayyan narrated to us: Said ibn Mina narrated to us: I heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit until it ripens. I said: When does it ripen. He said: When it reddens or yellows and is eaten from."
"14492","Yahya narrated to us from Shubah: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to me: I heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: I sought permission upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Who is this. So I said: I. So he said: I, I, as if he disliked that."
"14493","Yahya narrated to us: Jafar narrated to us: My father narrated to me, he said: We came to Jabir ibn Abdillah while he was among Banu Salamah, and we asked him about the Hajj of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained in Madinah nine years without performing Hajj, then it was announced among the people that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform Hajj this year. He said: So many people came down to Madinah, all of them seeking to follow the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and do as he does. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out with ten nights remaining of Dhu al-Qadah, and we went out with him until he came to Dhu al-Hulayfah. Asma bint Umays gave birth to Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, so she sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): How shall I do. He said: Bathe, then wrap yourself with a cloth, then enter ihram. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out until when his camel stood straight with him upon al-Bayda, he entered ihram with tawhid: Here I am, O Allah, here I am. Here I am, there is no partner for You, here I am. Indeed praise and favor are Yours, and dominion, there is no partner for You. And the people called talbiyah, and the people added Dhu al-Maarij and similar speech, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard without saying anything to them. So I looked as far as my sight, and before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were riders and walkers, and behind him likewise, and to his right likewise, and to his left likewise. Jabir said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among us, the Quran descending upon him, and he knows its interpretation, and whatever he acted upon of it, we acted upon. So we went out intending only Hajj until we came to the Kabah, then the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touched the Black Stone, then he trotted three circuits and walked four, until when he finished he went to the Station of Ibrahim and prayed behind it two rakahs, then he recited: And take the Station of Ibrahim as a place of prayer. My father said: Abu Abdillah, meaning Jafar, said: Then he recited therein with al-Tawhid and Say O disbelievers, then he touched the Stone and went out to al-Safa, then he recited: Indeed al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the rites of Allah, then he said: We begin with what Allah began with. So he ascended al-Safa until when he looked toward the House he said takbir. He said: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner. To Him is dominion and to Him is praise, and He is over all things capable. There is no god but Allah. He fulfilled His promise, aided His servant, and defeated the confederates alone. Then he supplicated, then he returned to these words, then he descended until when his feet poured forth in the valley he trotted until when he ascended he walked until he came to al-Marwah, then he ascended it until he looked toward the House, then he said upon it as he said upon al-Safa. When it was the seventh at al-Marwah, he said: O people, had I faced of my affair what I now know, I would not have driven the sacrificial animal, and I would have made it Umrah. Whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him, let him release his ihram and make it Umrah. So all the people released their ihram. Then Suraqah ibn Malik ibn Jushum, while at the foot of al-Marwah, said: O Messenger of Allah, is it for this year of ours or forever. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) interlaced his fingers and said: Forever, three times, then he said: Umrah has entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection. He said: And Ali came from Yemen and brought sacrificial animals, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drove sacrificial animals with him from Madinah. Then behold Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, had released her ihram and put on dyed clothes and applied kohl, so Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, disapproved of that in her, so she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me with it. He said: Ali said in Kufah. Jafar said: My father said: This word Jabir did not mention. So I went provoked to ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a ruling about what Fatimah mentioned. I said: Fatimah put on dyed clothes and applied kohl, and said: My father ordered me with it. He said: She spoke the truth, she spoke the truth, she spoke the truth. I ordered her with it. Jabir said: And he said to Ali: With what did you enter ihram. He said: I said: O Allah, I enter ihram with what Your Messenger enters ihram with. He said: And I have the sacrificial animal with me. He said: Then do not release your ihram. He said: So the total of the sacrificial animals which Ali, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, brought from Yemen and which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought was one hundred. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed with his hand sixty-three, then he gave to Ali, and he sacrificed what remained, and he shared with him in his sacrifice. Then he ordered a piece from every camel to be put in a pot, and they ate of its meat and drank of its broth. Then the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have sacrificed here, and all of Mina is a place of sacrifice. And he stood at Arafah and said: I have stood here, and all of Arafah is a standing place. And he stood at Muzdalifah and said: I have stood here, and all of Muzdalifah is a standing place."
"14494","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar informed us from Ibn Khuthaym from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit from Jabir ibn Abdillah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Kab ibn Ujrah: May Allah protect you from the rule of the foolish. He said: And what is the rule of the foolish. He said: Rulers who will be after me, they will not follow my guidance nor follow my practice. Whoever believes them in their lies and aids them in their wrongdoing, those are not of me and I am not of them, nor will they come to me at the Pond. And whoever does not believe them in their lies nor aid them in their wrongdoing, those are of me and I am of them, and they will come to me at the Pond. O Kab ibn Ujrah, fasting is a shield, charity extinguishes sin, and prayer is an offering, or he said: A proof. O Kab ibn Ujrah, indeed no flesh grown from unlawful earnings shall enter Paradise. The Fire is more deserving of it. O Kab ibn Ujrah, people are two who go out in the morning: One who sells himself and frees it, and one who sells himself and destroys it."
"14495","Muhammad ibn Bakr and Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no owner of camels who does not fulfill their due except they will come on the Day of Resurrection more numerous than they ever were, and he will be seated for them upon a flat plain, and they will trample him with their legs and hooves. And no owner of cattle who does not fulfill their due except they will come on the Day of Resurrection more numerous than they ever were, and he will be seated for them upon a flat plain, and they will gore him with their horns and trample him with their legs. And no owner of sheep who does not fulfill their due except they will come on the Day of Resurrection more numerous than they ever were, and he will be seated for them upon a flat plain, and they will gore him with their horns and trample him with their hooves. There will be among them neither hornless nor broken-horned. And no owner of treasure who does not fulfill its due except his treasure will come on the Day of Resurrection as a bald serpent following him with its mouth open. When it comes to him, he flees from it, then his Lord calls to him: Take your treasure which you hoarded, for I am richer than you without it. When he sees that he must face it, he puts his hand into its mouth and it bites it as the stallion bites."
"14496","Abu al-Zubayr said: And I heard Ubayd ibn Umayr saying: A man said: O Messenger of Allah. Abd al-Razzaq said in his hadith: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the due of camels. He said: Milking them at the water, lending their bucket, lending their stallion, granting their milk, and carrying upon them in the cause of Allah. Abd al-Razzaq said: In all of them, and he sat for them. And Abd al-Razzaq said therein: Abu al-Zubayr said: I heard Ubayd ibn Umayr saying this statement, then we asked Jabir al-Ansari about that, and he said like the statement of Ubayd ibn Umayr."
"14497","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj informed us: Abu al-Zubayr informed us that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade shighar."
"14498","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj informed us: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: My maternal aunt was divorced and wanted to harvest her palm trees, but a man forbade her from going out, so she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he said: Yes, harvest your palm trees, for perhaps you will give charity or do good."
"14499","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj informed us, and Rawh informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed us: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote upon every clan its blood-money, then he wrote that it is not lawful for the freed slave of a Muslim man to ally himself with another without his permission. Rawh said: Yutawalla."
"14500","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj informed us: Abu al-Zubayr informed me from Jabir that he heard him saying: We used to sell our concubines and mothers of our children while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was alive among us, seeing no harm in that."
"14501","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned a man from Aslam and a man from the Jews and a woman."
"14502","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr informed me that Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Ammar informed him that Jabir ibn Abdillah says: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that any animal be killed by confinement."
"14503","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr informed me that Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Ammar informed him, he said: I asked Jabir ibn Abdillah al-Ansari about the hyena, I said: Do I eat it? He said: Yes. I said: Is it game? He said: Yes. I said: Did you hear that from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes."
"14504","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah say: We ate during Khaybar horses and wild donkeys, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the domestic donkey."
"14505","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: They ask me about the Hour, and its knowledge is only with Allah, and I swear by Allah, there is no living soul on the earth today that a hundred years will come upon it."
"14506","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj said, and Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not walk in one sandal, and do not sit with your knees drawn up in a single lower garment, and do not eat with your left hand, and do not wrap yourself in al-samma, and do not put one of your feet over the other when lying on your back."
"14507","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, and Muhammad ibn Bakr informed me from Ibn Jurayj, Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir informed me, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdillah say: Bread and meat were brought near for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he called for ablution water and performed ablution, then he prayed al-Zuhr, then he called for the remainder of his food and ate, then he stood for prayer and did not perform ablution. Then I entered with Umar and a large bowl was placed for him here, and Ibn Bakr said: In front of us was a bowl containing bread and meat, and here was a bowl containing bread and meat, so Umar ate, then he stood for prayer and did not perform ablution."
"14508","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Part of the completion of prayer is straightening the row."
"14509","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us from Layth from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: Abu Quhafah was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Conquest, as if his head were a white thaghamah plant, so he said: Change it and avoid black."
"14510","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us from Ibn Khuthaym from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed in Makkah ten years following the people in their dwellings at Ukaz and Majannah and during the seasons at Mina, saying: Who will shelter me, who will support me so that I convey the message of my Lord, and for him is Paradise, until a man would come out from Yemen or from Mudar, thus he said, and his people would come to him and say: Beware of the youth of Quraysh, let him not tempt you, and he would walk among their men while they pointed at him with fingers, until Allah sent to him from Yathrib, so we sheltered him and believed him, and a man among us would go out and believe in him and he would teach him the Quran, then he would return to his family and they would become Muslim through his Islam, until no house among the houses of the Ansar remained except that therein was a group of Muslims openly showing Islam. Then we all conspired together and said: How long shall we leave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to be driven about in the mountains of Makkah in fear. So seventy men among us traveled to him until they came to him in the season, and we promised to meet him at the pass of al-Aqabah, so we gathered upon him one man and two men until we were all assembled, and we said: O Messenger of Allah, we pledge to you. He said: You pledge to me to hear and obey in activity and laziness, and to spend in hardship and ease, and to enjoin good and forbid evil, and to speak for Allah fearing in Allah no blame of any blamer, and to support me and protect me when I come to you as you protect yourselves and your wives and your children, and for you is Paradise. He said: So we rose to him and pledged to him, and Asad ibn Zurarah took his hand, and he was among the youngest of them, and said: Wait, O people of Yathrib, for we did not spur the camels except while we know that he is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and that bringing him out today is separation from all the Arabs and killing of your best men and that swords will bite you. So either you are people who will be patient over that, and your reward is upon Allah, or you are people who fear cowardice from yourselves, then make that clear, for it is an excuse for you before Allah. They said: Leave us alone, O Asad, for by Allah we shall never abandon this pledge nor ever take it back. He said: So we rose to him and pledged to him, and he took our covenant and stipulated, and he gives us Paradise for that."
"14511","Dawud ibn Mihran narrated to us, Dawud, meaning al-Attar, narrated to us from Ibn Khuthaym from Abu al-Zubayr Muhammad ibn Muslim, that he narrated to him from Jabir ibn Abdillah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained ten years, then he mentioned the hadith, and he said: Until a man would travel from the outskirts of Mudar and Yemen, and he said: Separation from the Arabs, and he said: You fear cowardice from yourselves, and he said concerning the pledge: We shall not seek its cancellation."
"14512","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us from Ibn Khuthaym from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir ibn Abdillah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained ten years, then he mentioned the hadith, except that he said: Until a man travels from Mudar and Yemen, and he said: Separation from the Arabs, and he said in the speech of Asad: You fear apprehension from yourselves, and he said concerning the pledge: We shall not seek its cancellation."
"14513","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, al-Thawri informed us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a donkey that had been branded on its face with its nostrils smoking, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who did this? Let no one brand the face, let no one strike the face."
"14514","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me, I heard Jabir ibn Abdillah say: A dabb lizard was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he refused to eat it, and said: I do not know, perhaps it is from the generations that were transformed."
"14515","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Miqsam that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of wrongdoing, for wrongdoing is darknesses on the Day of Resurrection, and fear miserliness, for miserliness destroyed those before you, it drove them to shed their blood and to deem their sacred things lawful."
"14516","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Jabir that a man from Aslam came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and confessed adultery, so he turned away from him, then he confessed and he turned away from him, until he testified against himself four times, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Are you mad? He said: No. He said: Are you married? He said: Yes. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to be stoned at the prayer place, and when the stones hurt him he fled and was caught and stoned until he died, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke good of him and did not pray over him."
"14517","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Ikrimah, meaning Ibn Ammar, narrated to us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: When the day of Khaybar came, hunger afflicted the people, so they seized domestic donkeys and slaughtered them and filled the pots with them, and that reached the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Jabir said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us and we overturned the pots, and he said: Allah Almighty will bring you provision that is more lawful for you than this and better than this. He said: So we overturned the pots that day while they were boiling, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that day domestic donkeys and the meat of mules and every fanged beast of prey and every taloned bird, and he forbade the tied-up target animal and the stolen kill and the plundered spoil."
"14518","Yahya ibn Adam and Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever plunders a plunder is not from us."
"14519","Yahya ibn Adam and Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not find two sandals, let him wear two leather socks, and whoever does not find a lower garment, let him wear trousers."
"14520","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade, or he forbade us, selling fruit until it ripens."
"14521","Yahya ibn Adam and Abu al-Nadr said, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed us, Jabir narrated to us, he said: Two boys fought, a boy from the Muhajirun and a boy from the Ansar, so the Muhajir said: O Muhajirun, and the Ansari said: O Ansar, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and said: Is it the call of ignorance? They said: No, by Allah, except that two boys struck one another. He said: No harm, let a man support his brother whether wrongdoer or wronged. If he is a wrongdoer, let him restrain him, for that is support for him, and if he is wronged, let him support him."
"14522","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he preached would lean against a palm trunk among the pillars of the mosque, and when the pulpit was made for him and he stood upon it, the pillar shook like the moaning of a she-camel until the people of the mosque heard it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended to it and embraced it and it became still. And Abd al-Razzaq and Rawh said: That pillar shook, and Rawh said: So he embraced it and it became still, and Abd al-Razzaq said: So it fell silent."
"14523","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr said, Jabir ibn Abdillah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays in a single garment, let him wrap it over his shoulders."
"14524","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir ibn Abdillah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prays, let him not spit in front of him nor to his right, but let him spit to his left or under his left foot."
"14525","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer on the day of sacrifice at Madinah, then two men came forward and sacrificed, thinking that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had sacrificed, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered whoever had sacrificed before him to repeat with another sacrifice, and: Do not sacrifice until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrifices."
"14526","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me that he said, Ata ibn Abi Rabah said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdillah while he was in Makkah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in the year of the Conquest: Allah Almighty and His Messenger forbade the sale of wine and carrion and pigs and idols. So it was said to him then: O Messenger of Allah, what about the fat of carrion, for ships are greased with it and skins are greased with it and people light lamps with it? He said: No, it is unlawful. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said then: May Allah fight the Jews, for when Allah Almighty forbade fats to them, they melted them, then sold them and ate their prices."
"14527","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, and Hajjaj from Ibn Jurayj, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah being asked about riding the sacrificial animal, so he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Ride it properly when you are compelled to it until you find another mount."
"14528","Abu Amir narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ata from Abd al-Malik ibn Jabir ibn Atik from Jabir ibn Abdillah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever speaks a saying in a gathering then turns, it is a trust."
"14529","Abu Abd al-Rahman Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Haywah informed us, Abu Hani informed me that he heard Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli say that Jabir ibn Abdillah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A bed for a man, and a bed for a woman, and a bed for a guest, and the fourth is for Satan."
"14530","Abu Abd al-Rahman Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us from his memory, Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, Amr ibn Jabir Abu Zura al-Hadrami narrated to me, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdillah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The poor Muslims enter Paradise forty autumns before the rich."
"14531","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Said narrated to us, Amr ibn Jabir al-Hadrami narrated to me, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdillah al-Ansari say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever fasts Ramadan and six from Shawwal, it is as if he fasted the whole year."
"14532","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Said narrated to us, Amr ibn Jabir narrated to me, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdillah al-Ansari say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fleeing from plague is like fleeing from battle, and the patient therein is like the patient in battle."
"14533","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us from Asim from Abu Nadrah from Jabir, he said: Two enjoyments were in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then Umar, may Allah تعالى be pleased with him, forbade us them, so we refrained."
"14534","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us from Ali ibn Zayd from Abu al-Mutawakkil from Jabir that he bought a camel for thirteen dinars, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: For how much did you take it? He said: For thirteen dinars. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Sell it to me for what you took it, and its back to Madinah is yours."
"14535","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Mahdi narrated to us, Wasil narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) three days before his death say: Let none of you die except while thinking well of his Lord."
"14536","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thabit narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The accepted Hajj has no reward except Paradise. They said: O Prophet of Allah, what is the accepted Hajj? He said: Feeding food and spreading peace."
"14537","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Uqayl narrated to us from Ibn Shihab, he said: I heard Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman say, Jabir ibn Abdillah informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Then revelation paused from me for a while, and while I was walking I heard a voice from heaven, so I raised my sight toward heaven, and behold the angel who had come to me in Hira was now sitting on a chair between heaven and earth, so I was stricken with fear of him until I fell to the ground, then I came to my family and said: Wrap me, wrap me, wrap me, so they wrapped me, then Allah Almighty sent down: O you wrapped up, arise and warn, and your Lord magnify, and your garments purify, and defilement shun. Abu Salamah said: Al-rujz is idols. Then revelation became intense afterward and continued."
"14538","Hajjaj narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir say: A slave of Hatib ibn Abi Baltaah, one of Banu Asad, came complaining of his master, and said: O Messenger of Allah, Hatib will surely enter the Fire. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: You lied, he will not enter it, for he witnessed Badr and al-Hudaybiyah."
"14539","Hajjaj narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj said, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir being asked: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) take the pledge at Dhu al-Hulayfah? He said: No, but he prayed there, and he did not take the pledge at a tree except the tree of al-Hudaybiyah. And he informed us that he heard Jabir invoke Allah at the well of al-Hudaybiyah."
"14540","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Israil narrated to us from Jabir from al-Shabi from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: A young man from Banu Salamah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I saw a rabbit and threw a stone at it, and I had no iron with me to slaughter it, and I slaughtered it with a sharp stone, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Eat."
"14541","Hajjaj narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir being asked about riding the sacrificial animal, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Ride it properly when you are compelled to it until you find another mount."
"14542","Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever meets Allah not associating anything with Him enters Paradise, and whoever dies associating with Him enters the Fire."
"14543","Abu Nuh Qurad narrated to us, Malik narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to walk in one sandal."
"14544","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Sharik informed us from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil from Jabir ibn Abdillah that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: What if I strive with myself and my wealth and am killed patiently seeking reward, advancing not retreating, shall I enter Paradise? He said: Yes. Then he repeated that two or three times. He said: Unless you die owing a debt for which you have no repayment."
"14545","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the people of Paradise are distinguished from the people of the Fire, and the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of the Fire enter the Fire, the messengers will stand and intercede, then He says: Go forth, or: Go, and whomever you recognize, bring him out. So they will bring them out burned, then they will cast them into a river, or upon a river, called al-Hayah. He said: Their burns fall off at the bank of the river, and they come out white like thaarir birds. Then they intercede, and He says: Go, or: Proceed, and whomever you find in whose heart is a qirat weight of faith, bring them out. He said: So they bring out many people. Then they intercede, and He says: Go, or: Proceed, and whomever you find in whose heart is a mustard seed weight of faith, bring him out. Then Allah Almighty says: Now I bring out by My knowledge and mercy. He said: So He brings out multiples of what they brought out and multiples thereof, then it is written on their necks: The freed ones of Allah Almighty. Then they enter Paradise and are called therein the Hell-dwellers."
"14546","Abu al-Nadr and Hasan ibn Musa said, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, Hasan said in his hadith: From Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The wife of Bashir said: Give my son your slave boy and have the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) witness for me. He said: So he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: The daughter of so-and-so asked me to give her son my slave boy, and she said: Have the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) witness for me. He said: Does he have brothers? He said: Yes. He said: Did you give all of them like what you gave him? He said: No. He said: This is not right, and I witness only to what is true."
"14547","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, al-Mubarak narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us from Jabir ibn Abdillah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the Hour a month before he died, so he said: You ask me about the Hour, and its knowledge is only with Allah Almighty, so by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, I do not know today of any living soul that a hundred years will come upon it."
"14548","Ismail ibn Aban Abu Ishaq narrated to us, Yaqub narrated to us from Isa ibn Jariyah from Jabir al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the dogs of Madinah to be killed, then Ibn Umm Maktum came and said: My house is distant and I have a dog, so he permitted him for some days, then he ordered his dog to be killed."
"14549","Abu Asim al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib informed me that Ata wrote mentioning that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say in the year of the Conquest: Allah Almighty and His Messenger forbade the sale of pigs and the sale of carrion and the sale of wine and the sale of idols. And a man said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about the fat of carrion, for ships and skins are greased with it and lamps are lit with it? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah fight the Jews, for when Allah forbade its fat to them, they took it and melted it, then sold it and ate its price."
"14550","Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to us, Shurahbil narrated to me from Jabir, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood praying al-Maghrib, so I came and stood at his left side, and he forbade me and placed me at his right, then a companion of mine came and we lined up behind him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer in a single garment with its ends crossed."
"14551","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Jabir that he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathering kabath fruit, and he said: Take the black thereof, for it is the tastiest. He said: We said: Did you herd sheep, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes, and was there any prophet but herded them."
"14552","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Usamah narrated to us from Ata from Jabir that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed and shaved and sat for the people, and he was not asked about anything except he said: No harm, no harm, until a man came to him and said: I shaved before I sacrificed. He said: No harm. Then another came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I shaved before I stoned. He said: No harm. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Arafah, all of it is a standing place, and Muzdalifah, all of it is a standing place, and Mina, all of it is a slaughter place, and all the roads of Makkah are a road and a slaughter place."
"14553","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us from Jabir, he said: Infusion was made for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a waterskin, and if no waterskin was found, infusion was made for him in a stone vessel. One of the people said to him, while I was listening: From brass? He said: Or from brass."
"14554","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Aqil narrated to us, Abu Aqil, his name is Abdullah ibn Aqil, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi narrated to me from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever revives a dead land, for him therein is reward, and whatever the wild creatures eat from it is charity for him."
"14555","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Rashid, narrated to us from Sulayman ibn Musa from Ata from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: We used to obtain with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in our spoils from the polytheists waterskins and vessels, and we distributed them, and all of them were carrion."
"14556","Hashim and Hasan ibn Musa said, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, Hasan said: From Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not slaughter except a musinnah, unless it is difficult for you, then slaughter a jadhaah of sheep."
"14557","Hashim and Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr said, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us from Jabir, may Allah تعالى be pleased with him, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey and it rained, so he said: Let whoever wishes among you pray in his lodging."
"14558","Hashim narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, or: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If the strap of the sandal of one of you breaks, or: If the strap of the sandal of one of you is cut, let him not walk in one sandal until he repairs his strap, and let him not walk in one leather sock, and let him not eat with his left hand, and let him not sit with knees drawn up in a single garment, and let him not wrap al-samma."
"14559","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abdillah ibn Usamah ibn Yazid al-Laythi and Yahya ibn Said narrated to me from Muadh ibn Rifaah al-Zuraqi from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said of this righteous servant for whom the Throne shook and for whom the gates of heaven were opened: He was pressed, then Allah relieved him. And he said once: Were opened, and he said once: Then Allah relieved him. And he said once: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said of Sad on the day he died while he was being buried."
"14560","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, Said narrated to us from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: We used to pray al-Zuhr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I would take in my hand a handful of pebbles and place it in my other hand until it cooled, then I would prostrate upon it because of the intense heat. Abdullah said: And it was in the book of my father from Said from Abu Said al-Khudri, so my father struck it out because it is a mistake, rather it is Said ibn al-Harith, Ibn Bishr erred."
"14561","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Amr from Said ibn al-Harith al-Ansari from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: I used to pray al-Zuhr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I would take a handful of pebbles in my palm to cool it so that I could prostrate upon it because of the intense heat."
"14562","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me from Abu al-Zubayr, he said: I heard Jabir say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man turning his back to his belly, so he asked about him, and they said: He is fasting, O Prophet of Allah. So he called him and ordered him to break his fast, and said: Is it not enough for you in the path of Allah and with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that you fast."
"14563","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid informed us from Abu al-Zubayr that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah say: We ate with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dried meat in Madinah from the dried sacrificial meat."
"14564","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid informed us from Abu al-Zubayr, he said: I heard Jabir say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you buy food, do not sell it until you take possession of it."
"14565","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Ayyash ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Khayr ibn Nuaym narrated to me from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The ten are the ten of sacrifice, and al-witr is the day of Arafah, and al-shaf is the day of sacrifice."
"14566","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to me, Jabir narrated to us, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: It is written between the eyes of the Dajjal: Disbeliever, every believer reads it."
"14567","Zayd narrated to us, Husayn narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was brought the keys of the world upon a piebald horse with a velvet cloth of silk brocade upon it."
"14568","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us from Ibn Abi Dhib, and Ibn Abi Bukayr, I am Ibn Abi Dhib, from Shurahbil from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For one of you to withhold his hand from pebbles is better for him than a hundred she-camels all black-eyed. If Satan overcomes one of you, let him wipe a single wiping."
"14569","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr Abu Amir said, Zakariya, meaning Ibn Ishaq, narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: Abu Bakr came seeking permission upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while the people were sitting at his door, and he was not permitted. Then Umar came and sought permission and was not permitted. Then Abu Bakr and Umar were permitted and entered, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting with his wives around him, silent. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I shall surely speak to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), perhaps he will laugh. So Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, if you had seen the daughter of Zayd, the wife of Umar, when she asked me for maintenance just now and I struck her neck. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed until his molars appeared. He said: They are around me as you see asking me for maintenance. So Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, rose to Aishah to strike her, and Umar rose to Hafsah, both saying: Do you ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for what he does not have. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade them. His wives said: By Allah, we shall not ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after this gathering for what he does not have. He said: And Allah Almighty sent down the choice, so he began with Aishah and said: I want to mention to you a matter, I do not want you to hasten therein until you consult your parents. She said: What is it? He said: So he recited to her: O Prophet, say to your wives, the verse. Aishah said: Concerning you shall I consult my parents? Rather I choose Allah and His Messenger. And I ask you not to mention to any of your wives what I chose. He said: Allah Almighty did not send me harsh, but He sent me a teaching facilitator. No woman among them asks me about what you chose except I inform her."
"14570","Rawh narrated to us, Zakariya narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us from Jabir, then he mentioned similar to it, except that he said: His wives around him silent, and he said: He did not send me harsh or divisive."
"14571","Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil from Jabir that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: So-and-so has a date cluster in my wall, and it has harmed me and its place has become hard upon me. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to him and said: Sell me your cluster that is in the wall of so-and-so. He said: No. He said: Then give it to me. He said: No. He said: Then sell it to me for a cluster in Paradise. He said: No. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have not seen one more miserly than you except one who is miserly with peace."
"14572","Abu Amir narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, Said ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: We entered upon Jabir ibn Abdillah while he was praying in a single garment wrapped in it, and his cloak was near, if he reached for it he could reach it. When he finished we asked him about that, so he said: I only do this so that fools like you may see me and spread the concession that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allowed concerning Jabir. Then Jabir said: I went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his journeys, and I came to him at night while he was praying in a single garment, and I had one garment, so I wrapped myself in it then stood at his side. He said: O Jabir, what is this wrapping? If you pray in a single garment, if it is wide then wrap yourself in it, and if it is narrow then wear it as a lower garment."
"14573","Abu Amir narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us from Said ibn al-Harith from Jabir that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon a man from the Ansar with a companion of his, and greeted, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: If you have water kept overnight this night in a waterskin, otherwise we drink directly. And the man was diverting water in a garden, so the man said: I have overnight water. So he took them to the trellis and poured water into a cup, then milked a household goat over it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank, then the man who came with him drank."
"14574","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Ghalib ibn Sulayman Abu Salih narrated to us from Kathir ibn Ziyad al-Bursani from Abu Sumayyah, he said: We differed here concerning the coming, so some of us said: No believer enters it, and some of us said: They all enter it, then Allah saves those who feared Him. So I met Jabir ibn Abdillah and said to him: We differed concerning that coming, for some of us said: No believer enters it, and some of us said: They all enter it. So he pointed with his fingers to his ears and said: May they be deaf if I did not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The coming is entering, no righteous nor wicked remains except enters it, so it will be upon the believer coolness and peace as it was upon Ibrahim, until the Fire, or he said: Hell, has a clamor from their coolness. Then Allah saves those who feared Him and leaves the wrongdoers therein kneeling."
"14575","Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith and Abu Said said, Zaidah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to us from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shrouded Hamzah in a single garment. Jabir said: That garment was a striped cloak."
"14576","Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, al-Husayn narrated to us from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from Jabir, he said: The people thirsted on the day of al-Hudaybiyah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had before him a small vessel from which he was performing ablution, when the people crowded toward him. He said: What is the matter with you? They said: O Messenger of Allah, we have no water to drink from nor water to perform ablution with except what is before you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his hand in the vessel, and water began to gush from between his fingers like springs. So we drank and performed ablution. I said: How many were you? He said: Had we been a hundred thousand it would have sufficed us, we were fifteen hundred."
"14577","Rawh narrated to us, Zakariya narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah say: I raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) nineteen raids. Jabir said: I did not witness Badr nor Uhud, my father prevented me. He said: When Abdullah was killed on the day of Uhud, I never stayed behind from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in any raid."
"14578","Rawh narrated to us, Zakariya, meaning Ibn Ishaq, narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Zubayr, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdillah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you shrouds his brother, let him beautify his shroud if he is able."
"14579","Rawh narrated to us, Zakariya narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood for the funeral of a Jew until it passed him."
"14580","Rawh narrated to us, Zakariya narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see the crescent, fast, and when you see it, break fast, and if it is obscured for you, count thirty days."
"14581","Rawh narrated to us, Zakariya narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us that he heard Jabir say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept away from his wives for a month, so he would be upstairs and they downstairs, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended to them after twenty-nine nights. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, you stayed twenty-nine nights. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The month is like this and like this, with the fingers of his hand twice, and he folded his thumb on the third."
"14582","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) withdrew from his wives for a month, then he mentioned its meaning."
"14583","Rawh narrated to us, Zakariya narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah say: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a raid he raided, and that was in Ramadan, then a man among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted and became severely weak, and thirst almost killed him, and his camel kept going under the thorn trees. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed of him and said: Bring him to me. So he was brought to him and he said: Are you not in the path of Allah and with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Break fast. So he broke fast. Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: A man among us fasted while we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in one of his raids, then he mentioned its meaning. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a cup and raised it upon his hands and drank so that the people would see that he was not fasting."
"14584","Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: A man among us fasted while we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in one of his raids, then he mentioned its meaning. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a cup and raised it upon his hands and drank so that the people would see that he was not fasting."
"14585","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best charity is from surplus wealth, and begin with those you support, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand."
"14586","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us from al-Amash from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) three before his death say: Let none of you die except while thinking well of Allah."
"14587","Ismail narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai informed us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray upon his mount toward the east, but when he wanted to pray the obligatory prayer he descended and faced the qiblah."
"14588","Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, al-Qasim, meaning Ibn al-Fadl, and he is al-Huddani, narrated to us, Said ibn al-Muhallab narrated to us from Talq ibn Habib, he said: I was among the most severe of people in denying intercession until I met Jabir ibn Abdillah, so I recited to him every verse Allah Almighty mentioned therein the eternity of the people of the Fire, so he said: O Talq, do you think you recite the Book of Allah better than I and know the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) better than I. So I humbled myself to him and said: No, by Allah, rather you recite the Book of Allah better than I and know His Sunnah better than I. He said: What you recited, its people are the polytheists, but a people committed sins and were punished for them, then brought out. May they be deaf, and he pointed with his hands to his ears, if I did not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: They come out of the Fire, while we recite what you recite."
"14589","Abd al-Samad and Muawiyah ibn Amr said, Zaidah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to us from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Bakr: At what time do you pray witr? He said: At the beginning of the night after the night prayer. He said: And you, O Umar? He said: At the end of the night. So he, (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: As for you, O Abu Bakr, you took the firm hold, and as for you, O Umar, you took strength."
"14590","Abd al-Samad and Abu Said with the meaning said, Zaidah narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil from Jabir, he said: A man died and we washed him and embalmed him and shrouded him, then we brought him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pray over him, so we said: Will you pray over him. He stepped forward steps then said: Is there debt upon him? We said: Two dinars. So he turned away, then Abu Qatadah bore them, so we came to him and Abu Qatadah said: The two dinars are upon me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is the creditor secured and the dead freed from them? He said: Yes. So he prayed over him. Then he said after that by a day: What happened to the two dinars? He said: He only died yesterday. He said: So he returned to him the next morning and said: I have paid them. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Now his skin has cooled. Muawiyah ibn Amr said in this hadith: So we washed him, and he said: So we said: Shall we pray over him."
"14591","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Harb, meaning Ibn Abi al-Aliyah, narrated to me from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir ibn Abdillah al-Ansari that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a woman and she pleased him, so he came to Zaynab while she was kneading leather, and fulfilled his need from her, and said: A woman comes in the image of Satan and turns in the image of Satan, so if one of you sees a woman and she pleases him, let him come to his family, for that repels what is in his soul."
"14592","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us from Husayn ibn Ali, he said: Wahb ibn Kaysan narrated to me from Jabir ibn Abdillah, and he is al-Ansari, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was visited by Jibril who said: Rise and pray it. So he prayed al-Zuhr when the sun declined, then he came to him for al-Asr and said: Rise and pray it. So he prayed al-Asr when the shadow of everything became like it, or he said: His shadow became like it. Then he came to him for al-Maghrib and said: Rise and pray it. So he prayed when the sun set, then he came to him for al-Isha and said: Rise and pray it. So he prayed when the twilight disappeared, then he came to him for al-Fajr and said: Rise and pray it. So he prayed when the dawn shone, or he said: When the dawn spread. Then he came to him the next day for al-Zuhr and said: Rise and pray it. So he prayed al-Zuhr when the shadow of everything became like it, then he came to him for al-Asr and said: Rise and pray it. So he prayed al-Asr when the shadow of everything became twice it, then he came to him for al-Maghrib, al-Maghrib at a single time, he did not move from it. Then he came for al-Isha, al-Isha when half the night had gone, or he said: A third of the night, so he prayed al-Isha. Then he came to him for al-Fajr when it was very bright, and said: Rise and pray it. So he prayed al-Fajr, then he said: What is between these two is time."
"14593","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Hasan ibn Ayyash, the brother of Abu Bakr, narrated to us from Jafar ibn Muhammad from his father from Jabir, he said: We used to pray Friday with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then we would return and rest our water camels. Hasan said: I said to Jafar: And when was that? He said: The decline of the sun."
"14594","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Qutbah narrated to us from al-Amash from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you perfume the dead with incense, perfume him three times."
"14595","Yahya ibn Adam and Abu Ahmad said, Abd al-Hamid ibn Yazid al-Ansari narrated to us, Abu Ahmad said: Uqbah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir narrated to me from Jabir, he said: We used to pray Friday with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then we would return and take a midday nap. Abu Ahmad said: Then we would return to Banu Salamah and take a nap, and it is two miles away."
"14596","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid narrated to us from Uqbah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Jabir, he said: We used to pray al-Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then we would return to Banu Salamah and see the sites of arrows."
"14597","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from al-Amash from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every servant is resurrected upon what he died upon."
"14598","He said, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In the night there is an hour, no Muslim servant coincides with it asking Allah therein for anything except He gives it to him, and it is in every night."
"14599","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from al-Amash from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People follow Quraysh in good and evil."
"14600","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil from Jabir from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade a man to wrap al-samma and to sit with knees drawn up in a single garment with nothing thereof over his private part."
"14601","Shadhan narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When he sees what has been made spacious for him in his grave, he says: Leave me so I may give glad tidings to my family, and it is said to him: Remain still."
"14602","Muhammad ibn Maymun Abu al-Nadr al-Zafarani narrated to us, Jafar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from his father, he said: I asked Jabir when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray al-Jumuah, and he said: We used to pray it with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then we would return and rest our water-camels. Jafar said: And the resting of the water-camels is when the sun declines."
"14603","Muhammad ibn Maymun narrated to us, Jafar narrated to me, from his father, from Jabir, that the sacrificial camels which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, slaughtered were one hundred badanah; he slaughtered sixty-three with his hand, and Ali slaughtered what remained, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered a piece from each badanah, and it was placed in a pot, then they drank of its broth."
"14604","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at a woman of the Ansar who had prepared food for him, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There will enter upon you a man of the people of Paradise, and Abu Bakr entered, so we congratulated him. Then he said: There will enter upon you a man of the people of Paradise, and Umar entered, so we congratulated him. Then he said: There will enter upon you a man of the people of Paradise, and I saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, inserting his head under the palm-frond shade, saying: O Allah, if You will, make him Ali. Then Ali entered, so we congratulated him."
"14605","Abu Ahmad and Abdullah ibn al-Walid said, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The best of the rows of men is the foremost, and the worst of them is the last, and the best of the rows of women is the last, and the worst of them is the foremost."
"14606","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When a morsel falls from the hand of one of you, let him remove whatever harm is on it, and let him not leave it for Satan, and let him not wipe his hand with a cloth, but let him lick his fingers, for he does not know in which of his food the blessing lies."
"14607","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, set out with tranquility upon him, and hastened in the valley of Muhassir, and he showed them pebbles like those of khadhf, and he ordered them to be tranquil, and said: Let my nation take its rites, for I do not know, perhaps I shall not meet them after this year of theirs."
"14608","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The throne of Iblis is upon the sea; he sends out his detachments, and the greatest of them in rank with him is the greatest of them in trial."
"14609","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me on an errand, and I came while he was praying on his mount facing toward the east, gesturing with gestures, the prostration lower than the bowing. So I greeted him, and when he finished he said: What did you do regarding such-and-such errand; I was praying."
"14610","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Nubayh, from Jabir, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would come out of his house, we would walk in front of him, and we would leave his back for the angels."
"14611","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sulayman ibn Qays, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Madinah will be left by its people while it is fruitful. They said: Then who will eat it, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The beasts of prey and the birds. Abu Awanah said: And I was told that Abu Bishr said: It was in the book of Sulayman ibn Qays."
"14612","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sulayman, from Jabir, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Faith is among the people of the Hijaz, and hardness of hearts and coarseness are among the loud-voiced herdsmen among the people of the east."
"14613","Abu Amir narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Usayd, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever leaves al-Jumuah three times without an excuse, Allah seals his heart."
"14614","Abu Amir narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, and Abu al-Nadr, Sharik narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah; and when they say it, they protect from me their blood and their wealth and themselves except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah, mighty and majestic."
"14615","Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, Qurrah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir, he said: While the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was distributing the spoils of Hunayn, a man stood up to him and said: Be just. He said: I am indeed wretched if I am not just."
"14616","Abu Amir narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Muhammad ibn Tahlah narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abi Hayyan narrated to us, from Jabir, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever takes others than his masters as patrons has cast off the bond of faith from his neck."
"14617","Abu Amir narrated to us, Kathir, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Kab ibn Malik narrated to me, Jabir, meaning Ibn Abdullah, narrated to me, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, supplicated in the mosque of al-Fath three times, on Monday and on Tuesday and on Wednesday, and he was answered on Wednesday between the two prayers, and joy was recognized on his face. Jabir said: And no grave important matter ever befell me except that I sought that hour and supplicated in it, and I recognized the answer."
"14618","Abu Amir and Abu Ahmad said, Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Yazid narrated to me, Abu Ahmad said: from al-Harith ibn Abi Yazid, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not wish for death, for the terror of the place of emergence is severe, and part of happiness is that the lifespan of the servant is long and Allah grants him repentance."
"14619","Ibn Ulayyah or another narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade plastering graves."
"14620","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Jabir, he said: The open lands around the mosque became vacant, and Banu Salimah wanted to move near the mosque, and that reached the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said to them: It has reached me that you want to move near the mosque. They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, we wanted that. He said: So he said: O Banu Salimah, your dwellings, your traces will be recorded; your dwellings, your traces will be recorded."
"14621","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Dawud narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said and Jabir ibn Abdullah, they said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There will be at the end of time a caliph who distributes wealth and does not count it."
"14622","Rawh narrated to us, Ashath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: We used to travel with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and when we ascended we would say Allahu Akbar, and when we descended we would glorify Allah."
"14623","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Dajjal is one-eyed, and he is the severest of liars."
"14624","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir saying: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: I am only a human, and I stipulate upon my Lord that any servant among the Muslims whom I insult or revile, that it be for him purification and reward."
"14625","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Jafar ibn Muhammad narrated to me that he heard his father narrating that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah narrating about the Hajj of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Then he descended from al-Safa until his feet poured into the belly of the valley, hastening until when we ascended the other side he walked."
"14626","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah being asked about the place of entering ihram, and he said: I heard, then he stopped, I think he meant the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The place of entering ihram of the people of Madinah is from Dhu al-Hulayfah, and the other road is al-Juhfah, and the place of entering ihram of the people of Iraq is from Dhat Irq, and the place of entering ihram of the people of Najd is from Qarn, and the place of entering ihram of the people of Yemen is from Yalamlam."
"14627","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir saying: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Asma bint Umays: What is the matter that the bodies of the sons of my brother are emaciated; does need afflict them. She said: No, but the evil eye hastens to them; shall we use ruqyah for them. He said: And with what. So she presented it to him, and he said: Use ruqyah for them."
"14628","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, and Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: If there is anything in anything, then it is in the dwelling and the horse and the woman."
"14629","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us to kill dogs, to the extent that a woman would come from the desert with her dog and we would kill it; then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade killing them, and said: Upon you is the jet-black dog with two spots, for it is a devil."
"14630","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Ismail informed me, from Sulayman ibn Atiq, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: When Safiyyah bint Huyayy entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in his tent, people were present, and I was present with them so that there would be a share in it; then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out and said: Rise from your mother. And when evening came we were present, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to us with about a mudd and a half of ajwah dates in the edge of his cloak, and said: Eat of the wedding feast of your mother."
"14631","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed us that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: He heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."
"14632","Rawh narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to carry stones with them for the Kabah while he had a waist-wrapper on him, and al-Abbas, his uncle, said to him: O son of my brother, if only you would loosen your waist-wrapper and place it on your shoulders beneath the stones. He said: So he loosened it and placed it on his shoulders, and he fell unconscious, and he was never seen naked after that day."
"14633","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, circumambulated in the Farewell Hajj upon his mount around the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah, so that the people could see him and so he could overlook them and they could ask him, for the people crowded over him."
"14634","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Let none of you die except while he thinks well of Allah."
"14635","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: We prepared an earthenware vessel for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I brought it to him and placed it before him, and he looked into it and said, I thought it was meat; so I mentioned that to my family, and they slaughtered a sheep for him."
"14636","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thabit narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: An accepted Hajj has no reward except Paradise. They said: O Prophet of Allah, what is the accepted Hajj. He said: Feeding food and spreading peace."
"14637","Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna Abu Umar narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would not fight in the sacred month unless he was attacked or they were attacked; and if that occurred, he would remain until it elapsed."
"14638","Hujayn and Yunus said, Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that a man of the Ansar said: Is there ruqyah for the scorpion. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever among you is able to benefit his brother, let him do so."
"14639","Hujayn and Yunus said, Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had kept away from his wives for a month, then he came out to us on the twenty-ninth, and we said: Today is only the twenty-ninth. He said: The month is such, and he clapped with his hands three times, and withheld one finger in the last one. And Yunus said: one finger."
"14640","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Waqid ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad ibn Muadh, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you proposes to a woman, if he is able to look at that of her which invites him to marry her, let him do so. He said: So I proposed to a girl of Banu Salimah, and I used to hide for her under the date-palm stumps until I saw of her some of what invited me to marry her, and I married her."
"14641","Yunus ibn Muhammad and Hujayn said, Layth narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not eat with the left hand, for Satan eats with the left hand."
"14642","Yunus ibn Muhammad and Hujayn said, Layth narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had sent me on an errand, then I caught up with him and greeted him, and he gestured to me; and when he finished he called me and said: You greeted me just now while I was praying, and he was at that time facing toward the east."
"14643","Yunus and Hujayn said, Layth narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: The prophets were shown to me: and Musa, peace be upon him, was a lean man among men, as though he were of the men of Shanua; and I saw Isa son of Maryam, peace be upon him, and the one I saw most resembling him was Urwah ibn Masud; and I saw Ibrahim, peace be upon him, and the one I saw most resembling him was your companion, meaning himself, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; and I saw Jibril, peace be upon him, and the one I saw most resembling him was Dihyah."
"14644","Yunus and Hujayn narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fell ill, and we prayed behind him while he was sitting, and Abu Bakr would say the takbir to make the people hear his takbir; then he turned to us and saw us standing, so he gestured to us, and we sat and prayed with his prayer sitting. And when he prayed he said: You were just now almost doing the deed of Persia and Rome: they stand over their kings while they are sitting, so do not do so; follow your imams: if he prays standing, pray standing, and if he prays sitting, pray sitting."
"14645","Yunus narrated to us, Aban, meaning al-Attar, narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ubaydullah ibn Miqsam, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a funeral passed, and we went to carry it, and it was the funeral of a Jew or a Jewess; so we said: O Messenger of Allah, it was only the funeral of a Jew or a Jewess. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Death is a fright, so when you see a funeral, stand."
"14646","Ismail ibn Muhammad, and he is Abu Ibrahim al-Muaqqib, narrated to us, Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The stray grazing animal, and Khalaf ibn al-Walid said: the stray grazing animal, is without liability, and the well is without liability, and the mine is without liability, and in buried treasure is the fifth. He said: Al-Shabi said: Buried treasure is the ancient hoard."
"14647","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, Mujalid ibn Said narrated to us, al-Shabi narrated to me, Jabir ibn Abdullah narrated to me, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prescribed the camel and the cow on behalf of seven."
"14648","Yunus narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn al-Ghasil, narrated to us, Shurahbil Abu Sad narrated to me that he entered upon Jabir ibn Abdullah while he was praying in a single garment with garments around him; and when he finished his prayer he said: I said: May Allah forgive you, O Abu Abdullah, you pray in a single garment while these garments of yours are at your side. He said: I wanted that a fool like you would enter upon me and see me praying in a single garment. Did every companion of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, have two garments. He said: Then Jabir began narrating to us, and said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the garment is wide, wrap it over your shoulders, then pray, and when it is too narrow for that, fasten it about your waist, then pray without a cloak over it."
"14649","Abdullah ibn al-Harith al-Makhzumi narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Hardness of hearts and coarseness are among the people of the east, and faith is among the people of the Hijaz."
"14650","Abdullah ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah asserting that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade images in the house, and forbade a man to make that, and that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered Umar ibn al-Khattab at the time of the Conquest, while he was at al-Batha, to come to the Kabah and efface every image in it, and he did not enter the House until every image in it had been effaced."
"14651","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyash, he said: Sad was asked about selling sult grain for barley or something of this, and he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about dates for fresh dates, and he said: Does the fresh date decrease when it dries. They said: Yes. He said: Then no."
"14652","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr informed me that Bukayr narrated to him that Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah narrated to him that Jabir ibn Abdullah visited al-Muqanna and said: I will not leave until you are cupped, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Indeed in it is healing."
"14653","Hasan narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr Muhammad ibn Muslim, freedman of Hakim ibn Hizam, narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Abdullah al-Ansari, companion of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade plunder."
"14654","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr informed me, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, do we act for a matter already completed or for a matter we are beginning. He said: For a matter already completed. So Suraqah said: Then what is the point of action. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Every worker is facilitated for his work."
"14655","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever finds means, let him shroud in a garment of hibarah."
"14656","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: A woman was punished for a cat or a kitten which she tied until it died, and she did not release it so it could eat of the vermin of the earth, and Hell became due for her thereby."
"14657","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: I asked Jabir: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say regarding buried treasure: the fifth. And he said: Yes."
"14658","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The servant is with whom he loves."
"14659","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wrote before he died to Kisra and to Qaysar and to every tyrant."
"14660","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Be upright and give glad tidings."
"14661","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: If I live, if Allah wills, I shall forbid that one be named Barakah and Yasar and Nafi. Jabir said: I do not know whether he mentioned Rafi or not: it is said to him: Is there here Barakah, and it is said: No; and it is said: Is there here Yasar, and it is said: No. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, died and did not forbid that, and Umar wanted to forbid it, then he left it."
"14662","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, Jabir informed me that the commander of the expedition was Ghalib al-Laythi, and Qutbah ibn Amir who entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the palm-trees while he was in ihram, then he came out of the door though he had climbed over from the side of the wall, and Abdullah ibn Unays who asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about Laylat al-Qadr when twenty-two nights had passed, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Seek it in these last seven that remain of the month."
"14663","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, that he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: When one of you defecates, let him wipe three times."
"14664","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: I asked Jabir about prostration, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanding to be moderate in prostration, and that a man not prostrate while spreading his forearms."
"14665","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When Satan hears the call to prayer, he flees the distance between al-Rawha and Madinah, passing wind."
"14666","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: I asked Jabir: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying anything about the multitude of the steps of a man to the mosque. And he said: We intended to move from our homes to Madinah to be near the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade us that and said: Do not leave Madinah vacant, for you have a merit over those by the mosque for every step a degree."
"14667","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The best to which mounts are ridden are the mosque of Ibrahim, peace be upon him, and my mosque."
"14668","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade cleaning oneself with dung or with a bone."
"14669","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, Jabir ibn Abdullah narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered Umar ibn al-Khattab at the time of the Conquest to come to the House while he was at al-Batha and efface every image in it, and he did not enter it until every image in it had been effaced."
"14670","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: I asked Jabir about the place of entering ihram, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The place of entering ihram of the people of Madinah is from Dhu al-Hulayfah, and the place of entering ihram of the people of the other road is from al-Juhfah, and the place of entering ihram of the people of Iraq is from Dhat Irq, and the place of entering ihram of the people of Najd is from Qarn, and the place of entering ihram of the people of Yemen is from Yalamlam."
"14671","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, declared sacred what is between the two lava tracts of Madinah: no tree of it is cut except that a man feeds his camel from it."
"14672","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Say takbir over your dead by night and by day, four takbirs."
"14673","Hasan ibn Musa al-Ashyab narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stoned the jamrah upon his camel with pebbles of khadhf, saying: Let you take your rites, for I do not know, perhaps I shall not perform Hajj after this Hajj of mine."
"14674","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever says when the caller calls: O Allah, Lord of this perfect call and the established prayer, send blessings upon Muhammad and be pleased with him with a pleasure after which there is no anger, Allah will answer his supplication."
"14675","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, that a monk gifted to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a cloak of sundus, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wore it, then he came to the House and put it down, and he sensed a delegation coming to him, and Umar ordered him to wear the cloak for the arrival of the delegation, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Wearing it is not proper for us in this world, but it is proper for us in the Hereafter; but take it, O Umar. He said: He dislikes it and I take it. He said: I do not command you to wear it, but send it to the land of Persia and gain wealth by it. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent it to the Negus, who had done good to those who fled to him of the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"14676","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seeking food, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fed him a wasq of barley; and the man kept eating from it, he and his wife and a servant of theirs, until they measured it. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Had you not measured it, you would have eaten from it and it would have sufficed you."
"14677","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: I asked Jabir: Did you see the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying while riding. He said: Yes. Then a man came to him who had bought a she-camel so that he might supplicate to Allah, mighty and majestic, for it, and he spoke to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, remained silent until he finished, then he supplicated for him."
"14678","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was the lightest of people in prayer."
"14679","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever of you fears that he will not rise at night, let him pray witr then sleep, and whoever of you hopes to rise, let him pray witr at the end of the night, for the recitation at the end of the night is witnessed, and that is better."
"14680","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you spits, let him not spit to his right nor before him, but let him spit to his left or under his foot."
"14681","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Take much of these sandals, for one of you remains as a rider so long as he wears sandals. And in another place: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying in a campaign he fought: Take much of sandals, for a man remains as a rider so long as he wears sandals."
"14682","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Be moderate and upright, for none of you will be saved by his deed. They said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Not even I, unless Allah envelops me with His mercy."
"14683","Abdullah ibn al-Walid, who is called al-Adani, narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the morsel of one of you falls, let him remove what is on it of harm, then let him eat it and not leave it for Satan, and let none of you wipe his hand with a cloth until he licks his fingers or has them licked, for he does not know in which of his food the blessing lies."
"14684","Ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Jafar narrated to us, from his father, from Jabir, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mentioned the Hour, his cheeks would redden and his anger would intensify and his voice would rise, as though he were warning of an army: You will be attacked in the morning, you will be attacked in the evening. He said: And he used to say: I am closer to the believers than their own selves; and whoever leaves wealth, it is for his family, and whoever leaves debt or dependents, it is to me and upon me, and I am closer to the believers."
"14685","Yunus and another said, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, Mujalid narrated to us, from Amir al-Shabi, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not ask the People of the Book about anything, for they will never guide you, and they have gone astray; for you will either affirm a falsehood or deny a truth; for had Musa been alive among you, nothing would have been lawful for him except to follow me."
"14686","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: A man of the Emigrants kicked a man of the Ansar, and the people of this one gathered and the people of that one gathered, and these said: O Emigrants, and these said: O Ansar. And that reached the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Leave it, for it is foul. He said: Then he said: What is the matter with the call of ignorance; what is the matter with the call of ignorance."
"14687","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Asim, from al-Shabi, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A woman is not married together with her paternal aunt, nor with her maternal aunt, nor a woman together with her brother's daughter, nor with her sister's daughter."
"14688","Yunus narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: For every prophet there is a disciple, and my disciple is al-Zubayr."
"14689","He said: I heard Sufyan ibn Uyaynah saying: Al-Hawari means the helper."
"14690","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, he said: I heard Amr ibn Dinar saying, from Jabir, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade leasing land."
"14691","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever revives a dead land, it is his, and what wild creatures eat of it is charity for him. So a man said: O Abu al-Mundhir, Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu al-Mundhir is Hisham ibn Urwah: What is al-afiyah. He said: Whatever seeks it of anything."
"14692","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Jabir, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to me with Abu Bakr and Umar, and I fed them fresh dates and gave them water to drink, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: This is of the bliss about which you will be asked."
"14693","Shadhan Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wanted to leave Ali behind, Ali said to him: What will people say about me when you leave me behind. He said: So he said: Are you not pleased to be from me in the position of Harun from Musa, except that there is no prophet after me, or there will be no prophet after me."
"14694","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade selling surplus water."
"14695","Hasan and Musa ibn Dawud said, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade selling white land for two or three years."
"14696","Hasan and Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik said, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: Ahmad in his hadith said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: Abu Quhafah was brought to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, or he came in the year of the Conquest, while his head and his beard were like thagham or like thaghamah. Hasan said: So he ordered him to his womenfolk, he said: Change this gray hair. Hasan said: Zuhayr said: I said to Abu al-Zubayr: Did he say: Avoid black. He said: No."
"14697","Hasan narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me while he was heading to Banu al-Mustaliq, and I came to him while he was praying on his camel; and I spoke to him, and he said with his hand like this, and Zuhayr gestured with his palm; then I spoke to him, and he said with his hand like this, while I heard him reciting and gesturing with his head. And when he finished he said: What did you do regarding what I sent you for, for nothing prevented me from speaking to you except that I was praying."
"14698","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Hasan ibn Salih informed us, from Jabir, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever has an imam, his recitation is recitation for him."
"14699","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade selling surplus water."
"14700","Aswad narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Yazid, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: We went out on campaign with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and we caught locusts and ate them."
"14701","Hajjaj narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that any animal be killed by confinement."
"14702","Hajjaj narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid that a man sit upon the grave, or that it be plastered, or that a structure be built over it."
"14703","Hajjaj narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade shighar."
"14704","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from al-Hasan, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No polytheist shall enter this mosque of ours after this year of ours, except the People of the Book and their servants."
"14705","Aswad narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir, raising the hadith, he said: I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah; then when they say it, their blood and their wealth become inviolable to me, and their reckoning is upon Allah - or: and their reckoning is upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"14706","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not enter the bathhouse except with a waist-wrapper; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not admit his wife into the bathhouse; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not sit at a table upon which wine is drunk; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not be alone with a woman who has no mahram relative of hers with her, for the third of the two is Satan."
"14707","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, and from Khayr ibn Nuaym, from Ata, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of the dog, and forbade the price of the cat."
"14708","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Abu al-Zubayr, that Jabir ibn Abd Allah narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained ten years following the pilgrims in their dwellings during the season, and at Majannah, and at Ukaz, and in their dwellings at Mina: Who will shelter me, who will aid me, so that I may convey the messages of my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and for him is Paradise; but he found no one to aid him and shelter him, to the point that a man would depart from Mudar, or from Yemen, or from Zawr Samad, and his people would come to him and say: Beware of the youth of Quraysh, lest he tempt you; and he would walk among their saddles calling them to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, while they pointed at him with fingers; until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent to him men from Yathrib, so a man would come to him and believe in him, and he would teach him the Quran, and he would return to his family and they would embrace Islam through his Islam, until there remained no house among the houses of Yathrib except that in it was a group of Muslims openly showing Islam; then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent us, so we deliberated and gathered, seventy men of us, and we said: How long shall we leave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) driven away in the mountains of Makkah and in fear; so we entered until we came to him in the season, and we promised to meet him at the pass of al-Aqabah; so his uncle al-Abbas said: O son of my brother, I do not know who these people are who have come to you; I know the people of Yathrib; so we gathered with him one man and two men, and when al-Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, looked at our faces, he said: These are a people I do not know; these are youths; so we said: O Messenger of Allah, upon what shall we pledge allegiance to you; he said: You pledge allegiance to me upon hearing and obeying in activity and laziness, and upon spending in hardship and ease, and upon enjoining good and forbidding evil, and upon speaking for Allah without fearing in Him the blame of any blamer, and upon aiding me when I come to Yathrib, defending me as you defend yourselves, your wives, and your children, and for you is Paradise; so we stood to pledge allegiance to him, and Asad ibn Zurarah took his hand, and he was the youngest of the seventy, and said: Gently, O people of Yathrib; we did not smite the livers of camels toward him except while knowing that he is the Messenger of Allah; indeed bringing him out today means separation from all the Arabs, the killing of your best men, and that swords shall bite you; so if you are a people who will endure swords when they touch you, and the killing of your best men, and separation from all the Arabs, then take him, and your reward is upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic; but if you are a people who fear for yourselves, then leave him, for that is more excusing for you before Allah; they said: O Asad ibn Zurarah, take your hand away from us; by Allah, we shall neither abandon this pledge nor seek release from it; so we stood to him, man by man, he taking from us upon the condition of al-Abbas, and granting us Paradise upon that."
"14709","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When Satan causes me to forget something of my prayer, let the men say tasbih and let the women clap."
"14710","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the lightest of people in prayer while making it complete."
"14711","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Jafar ibn Rabiah, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: When it was the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poured out the wine, broke its jars, and forbade its sale and the sale of idols."
"14712","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the son of Adam had a valley of wealth, he would wish for two valleys; and if he had two valleys, he would wish for a third; and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust."
"14713","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us: Israil ibn Yunus informed us, from Zayd ibn Ata ibn al-Saib, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah forgave a man before you who was easy when he sold, easy when he bought, easy when he settled a debt, easy when he sought repayment."
"14714","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Layth, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not sleep until he recited Alif Lam Mim, the revelation of the prostration, and Blessed is He in whose hand is dominion."
"14715","Abu Salamah al-Khuzai narrated to us: Sulayman - meaning Ibn Bilal - informed us, Jafar ibn Muhammad informed him, or narrated to him, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he heard it from him, he said: We arrived with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Makkah; he said: Then he circumambulated seven times, trotting three of them and walking four."
"14716","Abu Salamah al-Khuzai narrated to us: Malik narrated to us, from Jafar, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began at the Stone, then trotted until he returned to it three times, and walked four."
"14717","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Qarm narrated to us, from Abu Yahya al-Qattat, from Mujahid, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The key to Paradise is prayer, and the key to prayer is purification."
"14718","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr informed us, from Jabir, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us regarding the day of Ashura to fast it, and said: It is a day which the Jews used to fast."
"14719","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, that Umm Malik al-Bahziyyah used to present clarified butter in a skin of hers to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); then while her sons were asking her for condiment and she had nothing with her, she went to her skin in which she used to present to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and found in it clarified butter; and it continued to provide the condiment of her sons until she squeezed it; then she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Did you squeeze it; she said: Yes; he said: Had you left it, that would have remained for you established."
"14720","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us that he asked Jabir: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If the son of Adam had a valley, he would wish for another; so Jabir said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: If the son of Adam had a valley of date-palms, he would wish for its like, then wish for its like, until he would wish for valleys; and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust."
"14721","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Concerning that which the sky and springs water, the tenth; and concerning that which the water-wheel camel waters, half the tenth."
"14722","Harun narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to me: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to me that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah mentioning that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Concerning that which rivers and rain water, the tenths; and concerning that which the water-wheel camel waters, half the tenths."
"14723","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sternly forbade urinating into stagnant water."
"14724","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Our Lord, Mighty and Majestic, said: Fasting is a shield by which the servant seeks protection from the Fire, and it is for Me, and I reward for it."
"14725","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: I asked Jabir: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Do not fast until you see the crescent, and if it is hidden from you, then complete thirty."
"14726","And Jabir said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept away from his wives for a month, then came down after twenty-nine, and said: The month is but twenty-nine."
"14727","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: I asked Jabir: When would the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast the pebbles; so he said: As for the first day, in the forenoon; and as for after that, at the decline of the sun."
"14728","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a woman impresses one of you, let him go to his wife and be intimate with her, for that repels what is in himself."
"14729","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: I asked Jabir about the affair of Thaqif when it pledged allegiance; so he said: It stipulated upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that there be no charity upon it and no jihad."
"14730","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: And Jabir informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They will give charity and perform jihad when they embrace Islam - meaning Thaqif."
"14731","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying during the expedition of Tabuk, after we returned: Indeed in Madinah there are people - you did not travel any journey nor descend any valley but they were with you; sickness detained them."
"14732","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, that they took part in an expedition between Makkah and Madinah, and a violent wind blew upon them until it pushed the men; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is for the death of a hypocrite; so we returned to Madinah and found a hypocrite of great hypocrisy had died."
"14733","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: I asked Jabir about al-Aqabah; so he said: Seventy witnessed it; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met them, with Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib holding his hand; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have taken and I have given."
"14734","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A rider shall indeed travel beside the valley of Madinah and shall indeed say: There was once in this place a large multitude of believers."
"14735","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: Jabir informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Its people shall indeed abandon it full of ripe dates; they said: Then who will eat it, O Messenger of Allah; he said: Those of the birds and beasts that come seeking food."
"14736","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us: Jabir ibn Abd Allah informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There shall indeed come upon Madinah a time when people therein shall set out to the horizons seeking prosperity, and find prosperity, then come and carry their families to the place of prosperity; while Madinah is better for them, had they known."
"14737","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us: Jabir informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The dream of the believing man is a part of prophethood."
"14738","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: I asked Jabir about the purple saddle pad; so he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not ride upon it, nor wear a shirt edged with silk, nor wear qassi."
"14739","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: I asked Jabir about a mouse that dies in food or drink: Should I eat it; he said: No; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sternly forbade that; we used to put clarified butter in jars, and he said: If a mouse dies in it, do not eat it."
"14740","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: I asked Jabir about the dabb; so he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought it, and said: I do not eat it, and he found it distasteful; so Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not forbid it, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, indeed benefits more than one person by it, and it is the food of most shepherds; had it been with me, I would have eaten it."
"14741","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you make his brother stand on Friday, then go to his seat and sit in it; rather let him say: Make room."
"14742","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: I asked Jabir about a man who takes as client the freed slave of another man without his permission; so he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote upon each clan its blood-money obligations, then wrote: Indeed it is not lawful for the freed slave of a Muslim man to be taken as client without his permission."
"14743","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed in his document whoever does that."
"14744","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever leaves a dinar, it is a branding."
"14745","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the call to prayer is announced, the gates of heaven are opened and supplication is answered."
"14746","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day, and he looked toward Sham and said: O Allah, turn their hearts; and he looked toward Iraq and said the like of that; and he looked toward every horizon and did that; and said: O Allah, provide us from the fruits of the earth, and bless for us our mudd and our sa."
"14747","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The omen of every servant is upon his neck."
"14748","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us: He heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that he said: The wives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked him for maintenance, but he had nothing with him, until they pressed him; so Abu Bakr came and sought permission upon him, but was not permitted; then Umar came and sought permission upon him, but was not permitted; then they sought permission after that and were permitted, and found him among them; so Umar said to him: O Messenger of Allah, the daughter of Zayd asked me for maintenance, so I struck her on the face, or the like of that, intending thereby to make him laugh; so he laughed until his molars appeared, and said: By Him in whose hand is my soul, nothing detained me but that; so they stood to their daughters and took their hands and said: Do you ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for what he does not have; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade them concerning the two; so they said: We shall not return; and at that the option was revealed."
"14749","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from the nephew of Jabir ibn Abd Allah, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gatherings are by trust, except three gatherings: a gathering in which unlawful blood is shed, a gathering in which an unlawful private part is made lawful, and a gathering in which wealth is taken without right."
"14750","Husayn - meaning Ibn Muhammad - and Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad al-Khattabi narrated to us, they said: Ubayd Allah - meaning Ibn Amr al-Raqqi - narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Ata, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in what is besides it, except the Sacred Mosque; and a prayer in the Sacred Mosque is better than a hundred thousand prayers; Husayn said: in what is besides it."
"14751","Husayn narrated to us: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, he said: I said to Jabir ibn Abd Allah: Pray with us as you saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying; so he prayed with us in a single garment, tying it below the chest."
"14752","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Awzai: Abu Ammar narrated to me: A neighbor of Jabir ibn Abd Allah narrated to me, he said: I arrived from a journey, and Jabir ibn Abd Allah came to me greeting me; so I began telling him about the division of the people and what they had innovated; so Jabir began weeping, then said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Indeed the people entered the religion of Allah in crowds, and they shall leave it in crowds."
"14753","Sayyar ibn Hatim narrated to us: Jafar - meaning Ibn Sulayman - narrated to us: Al-Jad Abu Uthman narrated to us: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, he said: The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complained to him of thirst; he said: So he called for a large cup, and something of water was poured into it; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his hand in it and said: Give drink; so the people drank; he said: So I saw springs gushing from between the fingers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"14754","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Ata, from Jabir, he said: We would obtain with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), among our spoils from the polytheists, skins and vessels, and we would divide them, and all of them were carrion."
"14755","Rawh narrated to us: Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to wipe ourselves with a bone or dung."
"14756","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us: Fulayh narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Harith, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered, with a man of his companions, upon a man of the Ansar in a garden, while he was diverting water; so he said: Do you have water that spent the night in a skin, otherwise we shall drink directly; so he said: I have overnight water; so he went to a trellis, milked a sheep for him, then poured overnight water upon it, then gave him drink, and did the like with his companion."
"14757","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr - and he is Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri - narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman - meaning Ibn al-Ghasil - informed us, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: If there is, or if there be, in any of your remedies any good, then it is in a cupper's incision, or a draught of honey, or a touch of fire meeting a disease; and I do not like to be cauterized."
"14758","Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us: Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit and Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, guide Thaqif; Abd Allah said: And I heard it myself from Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah, and he mentioned the like of it."
"14759","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us: Ismail - meaning Ibn Jafar - narrated to us: Dawud ibn Bakr ibn Abi al-Furat informed me, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whatever intoxicates in large amount, its small amount is unlawful."
"14760","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, by recitation: Sadaqah ibn Yasar narrated to me, from Aqil ibn Jabir, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the expedition of Dhat al-Riqa, and a woman of the polytheists was injured; then when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) departed returning, and her husband came, and he had been absent, he swore that he would not stop until he shed blood among the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so he went out following the track of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alighted at a dwelling and said: Who is a man to guard us this night of ours; so a man of the Emigrants and a man of the Ansar volunteered, and said: We will, O Messenger of Allah; he said: Then be at the mouth of the pass; he said: And they had alighted at a pass of the valley; then when the two men went out to the mouth of the pass, the Ansari said to the Muhajiri: Which part of the night is more beloved to you that I suffice you, its beginning or its end; he said: Suffice me its beginning; so the Muhajiri lay down and slept, and the Ansari stood praying; and the man came, and when he saw the figure of the man, he knew that he was the watcher of the people, so he shot him with an arrow and placed it in him, so he pulled it out and laid it down, and remained standing; then he shot him with another arrow and placed it in him, so he pulled it out and laid it down, and remained standing; then he returned to him with a third and placed it in him, so he pulled it out and laid it down, then bowed and prostrated, then woke his companion and said: Sit, for I have been wounded; so he leapt up, and when the man saw the two of them, he knew that they had become aware of him, so he fled; then when the Muhajiri saw the blood upon the Ansari, he said: Glory be to Allah, why did you not wake me; he said: I was in a chapter reciting it, and I did not wish to cut it until I completed it; then when the shooting continued, I bowed, so I showed you; by Allah, were it not that I would neglect a post which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to guard, my soul would have been severed before I cut it or completed it."
"14761","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us: Malik ibn Anas informed me, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a man eat with his left hand, or walk in a single sandal, or wrap himself in the sammah wrap, or sit bundled in a single garment uncovering his private part."
"14762","Ishaq narrated to us: Malik narrated to me, from Hashim ibn Hashim ibn Utbah ibn Abi Waqqas, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Nistas narrating from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let no one swear upon this minbar of mine falsely except that he takes his seat in the Fire."
"14763","Ishaq ibn Isa and Abu Said - meaning the freed slave of Banu Hashim - narrated to us, the meaning, and this is the wording of Ishaq, they said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Mawal al-Madani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us istikhara as he used to teach us a chapter of the Quran, saying: When one of you intends a matter, let him bow two rakahs of other than the obligatory, then let him say: O Allah, I seek good from You by Your knowledge, and I seek ability from You by Your power, and I ask You of Your immense bounty; for You decree and I do not decree, and You know and I do not know, and You are the Knower of the unseen; O Allah, if You know this matter - he names it by its name - to be good for me in my religion and my livelihood - Abu Said said: and my life - and the outcome of my affair, then decree it for me and ease it, then bless me in it; O Allah, and if You know it to be evil for me in my religion and my livelihood and the outcome of my affair, then turn me away from it and turn it away from me, and decree for me good wherever it be, then make me pleased with it; and Abu Said said: and the outcome of my affair, then decree it for me, ease it for me, bless me in it; O Allah, and if You know it to be evil for me in my religion and my livelihood and the outcome of my affair, then turn me away from it and turn it away from me, and decree for me good wherever it be, then make me pleased with it."
"14764","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated it to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Mawal narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"14765","Ishaq narrated to us: Fulayh ibn Sulayman al-Madani narrated to me, from Said ibn al-Harith, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to a people of the Ansar visiting a sick man, and sought drink from them, with a stream near him, and said: If they have water that spent the night in a skin, otherwise we shall drink directly."
"14766","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us: Al-Munkadir ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every good is charity; and among good is that you meet your brother with a cheerful face, and that you pour from your bucket into his vessel."
"14767","Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated to us: Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Amr ibn Jabir al-Hadrami, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Ramadan and six days of Shawwal, it is as if he fasted the whole year."
"14768","Hashim narrated to us: Al-Mubarak narrated to us: Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The two that necessitate: whoever meets Allah, Mighty and Majestic, associating nothing with Him, enters Paradise; and whoever meets Allah, Mighty and Majestic, as a polytheist, enters the Fire."
"14769","Surayj narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz - meaning Ibn Abd Allah - narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed every prophet has a disciple, and indeed my disciple is al-Zubayr."
"14770","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us: Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not raid in the sacred month, except that he be raided, or they be raided; then if it came upon him, he remained until it elapsed."
"14771","Musa ibn Dawud and Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, they said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr - Hasan said in his hadith, he said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us - from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Ghifar - may Allah forgive it; and Aslam - may Allah grant it peace."
"14772","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Harshness of hearts and dryness are toward the east, while faith and tranquility are among the people of the Hijaz."
"14773","Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that Umar ibn al-Khattab informed him that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I shall indeed expel the Jews and Christians from the Arabian Peninsula, until I leave none in it except a Muslim."
"14774","Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said a month before he died: You ask me about the Hour, and its knowledge is only with Allah; I swear by Allah, there is no soul alive upon the earth today over which a hundred years shall pass."
"14775","Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Before the Hour there shall be liars, among them the chief of al-Yamamah, and among them the chief of Sanaa, al-Ansi, and among them the chief of Himyar, and among them the Dajjal, and he is the greatest of them in tribulation; Jabir said: And some of my companions say: near thirty liars."
"14776","Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I am your forerunner before you; then if you do not see me, I shall be at the Hawd, the distance between Aylah and Makkah; and men and women shall come with skins and vessels, but they shall not taste anything from it."
"14777","Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There shall remain a group of my community fighting upon the truth, triumphant, until the Day of Resurrection; he said: Then Isa ibn Maryam, peace be upon him, shall descend, and their commander shall say: Come, pray with us; so he shall say: No; indeed some of you are commanders over others, that Allah may honor this community."
"14778","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, that he asked Jabir about the coming; he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: We shall be on the Day of Resurrection upon a heap above the people; then the nations shall be called with their idols and what they used to worship, the first then the first; then our Lord, Mighty and Majestic, shall come to us after that and say: What are you awaiting; so they shall say: We await our Lord, Mighty and Majestic; so He shall say: I am your Lord; so they shall say: Until we look upon Him; he said: Then He shall manifest Himself to them, Mighty and Majestic, while laughing, and give every human among them, hypocrite and believer, a light, and darkness shall cover them; then they shall follow Him, with the hypocrites with them, upon the bridge of Hell, wherein are hooks and thorns seizing whom He wills; then the light of the hypocrites shall be extinguished, and the believers shall be saved; so the first group shall be saved, their faces like the moon on the night of fullness, seventy thousand not taken to account; then those who follow them like the brightest star in the sky, then that, until intercession becomes lawful; so they shall intercede until whoever said: There is no god but Allah, among those in whose heart is the weight of a barley grain, shall come out, and be placed at the courtyard of Paradise, and the people of Paradise shall pour water upon them until they sprout as a thing sprouts in the flood, and their burning shall depart; then he shall ask Allah, Mighty and Majestic, until He grants him the world and ten times its like."
"14779","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, that he asked Jabir ibn Abd Allah about the triers of the grave; so he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: This community shall be tried in their graves; then when the believer is admitted to his grave and his companions turn away from him, an angel of severe rebuke shall come and say to him: What did you say concerning this man; so the believer shall say: I say that he is the Messenger of Allah and His servant; so the angel shall say to him: Look at your seat which was in the Fire; Allah has saved you from it, and exchanged for your seat which you see of the Fire your seat which you see of Paradise; so he shall see both of them; then the believer shall say: Leave me to bear glad tidings to my family; so it shall be said to him: Remain; but as for the hypocrite, he shall be seated when his family turn away from him, and it shall be said to him: What did you say concerning this man; so he shall say: I do not know; I say what the people say; so it shall be said to him: You neither knew; this is your seat which was for you of Paradise; you have been exchanged in its place your seat of the Fire; Jabir said: Then I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Every servant shall be raised in the grave upon what he died: the believer upon his faith, and the hypocrite upon his hypocrisy."
"14780","Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, that he asked Jabir about the funeral; he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood for a funeral that passed, with those with him, until it disappeared."
"14781","Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I hope that those who follow me of my community on the Day of Resurrection shall be a quarter of the people of Paradise; he said: Then we magnified Allah; then he said: I hope that they shall be a third of the people; he said: Then we magnified Allah; then he said: I hope that they shall be the half."
"14782","Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No believing man, nor believing woman, nor Muslim man, nor Muslim woman falls ill, except that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, removes thereby his sins."
"14783","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called at his death for a document to write therein a writing after which they would not stray; he said: Then Umar ibn al-Khattab dissented upon it until he rejected it."
"14784","Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, that he said: I asked Jabir: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The best of jihad is one whose horse is hamstrung and whose blood is shed; so Jabir said: Yes."
"14785","Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The best of charity is charity from surplus wealth; and begin with those you support; and the upper hand is better than the lower hand."
"14786","Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, that he asked Jabir: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When a man enters his house, he greets."
"14787","And the believer eats in a single intestine; he said: Yes."
"14788","He said: And I asked Jabir: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When a man enters his house and mentions the name of Allah when he enters and when he eats, Satan says: There is no lodging for you nor supper here; but if he enters and does not mention the name of Allah at his entering, he says: You have attained lodging; and if he does not mention the name of Allah at his food, he says: You have attained lodging and supper; he said: Yes."
"14789","Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, that he asked Jabir about the servant of a man when he spares him hardship and heat; so he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to call him; then if one dislikes to eat with him, let him feed him a morsel in his hand."
"14790","Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, he said: I asked Jabir: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The fornicator does not fornicate while he fornicates as a believer, nor steal while he steals as a believer; Jabir said: I did not hear him; Jabir said: And Ibn Amr informed me that he heard it."
"14791","Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, that Jabir informed him that they took part in an expedition between Makkah and Madinah, and a violent wind blew upon them; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed it is for the death of a hypocrite; so we returned to Madinah and found a hypocrite of great hypocrisy had died."
"14792","Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that when Hunayn was conquered, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent detachments, and they brought camels and sheep, and he divided them among Quraysh; he said: So we found resentment against him, O Ansar; and that reached him, so he gathered us and addressed us and said: Are you not pleased that you have been given the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); by Allah, were people to take a valley and you to take a mountain pass, I would follow your pass; they said: We are pleased, O Messenger of Allah."
"14793","Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, he said: I asked Jabir about al-Aqabah; he said: Seventy witnessed it; and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met them, with Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib holding his hand; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have taken and I have given."
"14794","Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that he informed him that Umar ibn al-Khattab informed him that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The people of Makkah shall indeed leave it, then they shall not inhabit it, or it shall be inhabited but little; then it shall be inhabited and filled and built; then they shall leave it and never return to it."
"14795","Musa and Qutaybah narrated to us, they said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A rider shall indeed travel in the direction of Madinah - Qutaybah said: in the side of Madinah - and shall indeed say: There was once in this place a large multitude of believers."
"14796","Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, that Jabir informed him that he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: It is not lawful for anyone to carry weapons therein for fighting; so Qutaybah said: meaning Madinah."
"14797","Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was presented by a monk of Sham with a cloak of sundus; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wore it, then came to the House and laid it down; and he was informed of a delegation coming to him, so Umar ibn al-Khattab ordered him to wear the cloak for the coming of the delegation; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not proper for us to wear it in this world, while it is proper for us to wear it in the Hereafter; but take it, O Umar; so he said: Do you dislike it while I take it; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not command you to wear it, but that you send it to the land of Persia and obtain wealth by it; so Umar refused; then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent it to the Negus, and he had done good to those who fled to him among the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"14798","Musa and Hasan narrated to us, they said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us - Hasan said in his hadith: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us - and Ibn Lahiah said: from Abu al-Zubayr, that he asked Jabir about a saddle pad - he said: the purple; so Jabir said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not ride upon it, nor wear a shirt edged with silk, nor wear qassi."
"14799","Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from al-Bahziyyah Umm Malik: She used to present clarified butter in a skin of hers to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); then while her sons were asking her about condiment and she had nothing with her, she went to her skin-bag in which she used to present clarified butter to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and found therein clarified butter; and it continued to provide the condiment of her sons until she squeezed it; so she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Did you squeeze it; so she said: Yes; he said: Had you left it, that would have remained established."
"14800","Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a man came to him seeking food, so he fed him half a wasq of barley; and the man continued eating from it, he and his wife and a servant of theirs, until they measured it; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had you not measured it, you would have eaten from it and it would have remained for you."
"14801","Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that Bannah al-Juhani informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by people in the mosque or in the gathering drawing a sword among themselves, handing it to one another unsheathed, and he said: May Allah curse whoever does that, or: Did I not forbid you from this? When you draw the sword, let a man sheathe it, then let him hand it over like that."
"14802","Musa and Hasan narrated to us, and the wording is Hasan's wording, they both said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: I asked Jabir: Did you hear the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A man is in prayer as long as he waits for prayer? He said: We waited for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night for the Atamah prayer, and he was delayed from us until it was close to half the night or reached that, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and we prayed, then he said: Sit, and he addressed us and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people have prayed and slept, and you have continued to be in prayer as long as you waited for prayer."
"14803","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, he said: Jabir informed me, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When a woman pleases one of you and she falls into his mind, let him go to his wife and have intercourse with her, for that repels what is in himself."
"14804","Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, he said: I asked Jabir about a man who performs witr in the evening then sleeps. Jabir said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever among you fears that he will not rise at night, let him perform witr then sleep, and whoever among you hopes to rise, let him perform witr at the end of the night, for recitation at the end of the night is attended, and that is better."
"14805","Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is an hour in the night that no Muslim servant coincides with while asking Allah for good except He gives it to him, and it is every night."
"14806","Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that Numan ibn Qawqal came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think, if I pray the prescribed prayers and fast Ramadan and forbid the unlawful and permit the lawful and do not add anything to that, shall I enter Paradise? He said: Yes. So he said: By Allah, I will not add anything to that."
"14807","Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that he informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the most lightening of people in prayer."
"14808","Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, that he said: I asked Jabir: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combine Maghrib and Isha? He said: Yes, at the time of our raid on Banu al-Mustaliq."
"14809","Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, that he asked Jabir about clapping and tasbih. Jabir said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Clapping is for women in prayer, and tasbih is for men."
"14810","Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) campaigned six times before the fear prayer, and the fear prayer was in the seventh year."
"14811","Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, he said: I asked Jabir about ghusl. Jabir said: Thaqif came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Our land is a cold land, so how do you command us regarding ghusl? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for me, I pour over my head three times, and he said nothing else."
"14812","Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, he said: I asked Jabir about a man touching a man directly. Jabir said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that."
"14813","And with its isnad he said: I asked Jabir about a woman touching a woman directly. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that."
"14814","And with its isnad he said: I asked Jabir about a man intending fasting while the vessel is in his hand to drink from it and he hears the call. Jabir said: We used to narrate that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let him drink."
"14815","And with its isnad, from Jabir, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The sun rises in the horn of Satan."
"14816","And with its isnad he said: I asked Jabir about riding the sacrificial animal. Jabir said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Ride it in a proper manner until you find a back."
"14817","Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to fast the day of Ashura."
"14818","Musa and Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, they said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, he said: I asked Jabir about slaughter. Jabir said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer on the day of sacrifice in Madinah, then men went forward and slaughtered, thinking that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had slaughtered, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded whoever had slaughtered to repeat another slaughter, and not to slaughter until he slaughters."
"14819","Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, he said: I asked Jabir about a man allying himself to the freedmen of a man without his permission. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote upon every clan their blood-money, then he wrote that it is not lawful to ally oneself to the freedmen of a man without his permission."
"14820","Musa and Hasan narrated to us, they said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the believer is like the likeness of the ear of grain, falling once and standing straight once, and the likeness of the disbeliever is like the arz tree, remaining upright until it falls and does not perceive. Hasan said: Al-arzah."
"14821","Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, he said: I asked Jabir about the eclipse of the sun and the moon. Jabir said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When the sun and the moon are eclipsed, or one of them, and you see that, then pray until the eclipse of whichever of them was eclipsed clears."
"14822","Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, he said: I asked Jabir about the slain man who was killed and Suhaym proclaimed concerning him. Jabir said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Suhaym to proclaim among the people: No one enters Paradise except a believer. Jabir said: And I do not know that anyone was killed."
"14823","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: I asked Jabir about the slain man who was killed and Suhaym proclaimed concerning him. He said: We were at Hunayn, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Suhaym to proclaim among the people that none enters Paradise except a believer. He said: And I do not know that anyone was killed. Musa ibn Dawud said: He killed someone."
"14824","Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, he said: I asked Jabir: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say anything about omens and contagion? Jabir said: I heard him say: Every servant's omen is in his neck."
"14825","Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When one of you shrouds his brother, let him make his shroud good, and pray over the dead with four takbirs, in night and day alike."
"14826","Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of the sinnar, and it is the cat."
"14827","Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, while the funeral of Sad ibn Muadh was before them: The Throne of the Most Merciful shook for it."
"14828","Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The people of Paradise eat therein and drink, and do not blow their noses nor defecate nor urinate; their food is only belching, sweat like the sweat of musk, and they are inspired with tasbih and tahmid as they are inspired with breath."
"14829","Hujayn and Yunus narrated to us, they said: Layth narrated to us, Yunus said: From Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade wrapping in a single garment, and sitting with knees drawn up in a single garment, and that a man raise one of his legs over the other while lying on his back."
"14830","Hujayn and Yunus narrated to us, they said: Al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that a slave of Hatib came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complaining about Hatib, and said: O Messenger of Allah, Hatib will surely enter the Fire. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have lied, he will not enter it, for he witnessed Badr and al-Hudaybiyah."
"14831","Hujayn narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, and Ishaq ibn Isa, Layth narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: A slave came and pledged the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for migration, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not know that he was a slave, then his master came seeking him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sell him to me, and he bought him for two black slaves, then he did not pledge anyone after that until he asked him: Is he a slave?"
"14832","Hujayn and Yunus narrated to us, they said: Al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that he said: On the day of al-Ahzab, Sad ibn Muadh was shot and they cut his median vein, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cauterized him with fire, then his hand swelled, so he cauterized him and his hand swelled, then he cauterized him again and his hand swelled, then he bled him, and when he saw that he said: O Allah, do not take my soul until You cool my eye from Banu Qurayzah, so his vein held and did not drip a drop until they came down to the judgment of Sad, then he was sent for and he judged that their men be killed and their women and offspring be spared, for the Muslims to seek help through them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have hit the judgment of Allah concerning them, and they were four hundred, then when the killing of them was finished his vein burst open and he died."
"14833","Hujayn and Yunus narrated to us, they said: Al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that Hatib ibn Abi Baltaah wrote to the people of Makkah mentioning that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to raid them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was directed to the woman who had the letter, and he sent to her and her letter was taken from her head, and he said: O Hatib, did you do it? He said: Yes, but I did not do it out of betrayal of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Yunus said: Out of betrayal, O Messenger of Allah, nor hypocrisy; I knew that Allah would make His Messenger victorious and complete His matter for him, except that I was honored among them and my mother was among them, so I wanted to gain favor with them through this. Umar said to him: Shall I not strike the head of this one? He said: Do you kill a man from the people of Badr? What informs you, perhaps Allah Almighty looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do whatever you wish."
"14834","Hujayn and Yunus narrated to us, they said: Al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that Umm Salamah asked permission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for cupping, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Abu Taybah to cup her. He said: I thought he was her brother through suckling or a boy who had not reached puberty."
"14835","Hujayn and Yunus narrated to us, they said: Al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that they, when they were present with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Madinah and he sent the sacrificial animals, whoever of us wished entered ihram and whoever wished left it."
"14836","Hujayn and Yunus narrated to us, they said: Al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade urinating in stagnant water."
"14837","Hujayn and Yunus narrated to us, they said: Al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: No one of those who pledged under the tree will enter the Fire."
"14838","Hujayn and Yunus narrated to us, they said: Al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in sleep has seen me, for Satan may not take my likeness."
"14839","And he said: When one of you dreams, let him not tell people of Satan playing with him in sleep."
"14840","Hujayn and Yunus narrated to us, they said: Al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: When one of you sees a vision he dislikes, let him spit to his left three times, and Yunus said: Let him spit, and let him seek refuge in Allah from Satan three times, and let him turn from the side he was on."
"14841","Hujayn and Yunus narrated to us, they said: Al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he commanded a man who was giving charity of arrows in the mosque not to come with them except holding their blades."
"14842","Hujayn and Yunus narrated to us, they said: Al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The best mounts journeyed to are this mosque of mine and the Ancient House."
"14843","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Kathir ibn Shinzhir narrated to us, Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me on an errand, so I went and returned after fulfilling it, then I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and greeted him and he did not reply to me. He said: Something fell into myself, Allah knows it. He said: I said: Perhaps the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is angry with me for delaying, so I greeted him and he did not reply to me, and there fell into myself what Allah knows, more severe than the first, then I greeted and he replied to me and said: Nothing prevented me from replying to you except that I was praying, and he was on his mount facing other than the qiblah."
"14844","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Wasil, freedman of Abu Uyaynah, narrated to us, Khalid ibn Urfutah narrated to me, from Talhah ibn Nafi, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the wind of a foul corpse rose, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know what this wind is? This is the wind of those who backbite the believers."
"14845","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions passed by a woman, and she slaughtered for them a sheep and made food for them, then when he returned she said: O Messenger of Allah, we have made food for you, so enter and eat. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions entered, and they would not begin until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a morsel and could not swallow it, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is a sheep slaughtered without the permission of its owners. The woman said: O Prophet of Allah, we do not stand on formality with the family of Sad ibn Muadh, nor do they stand on formality with us; we take from them and they take from us."
"14846","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Ammar narrated to us, I heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar ate fresh dates and drank water, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is among the bliss you will be asked about."
"14847","Abd al-Samad and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad narrated to us, Affan said in his hadith: Abu al-Zubayr informed us, and Abd al-Samad said in his hadith: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw as if I were in strong armor, and I saw slaughtered cattle, so I interpreted the strong armor as Madinah, and the cattle, by Allah, is good. He said: So he said to his companions: If we stayed in Madinah, and they entered upon us therein, we would fight them. They said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, it was never entered upon us therein in Jahiliyyah, so how will it be entered upon us therein in Islam? Affan said in his hadith: So he said: Then as you wish. He said: So he wore his armor. He said: So the Ansar said: We turned down the opinion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so they came and said: O Prophet of Allah, as you wish then. So he said: It is not for a prophet, when he wears his armor, to lay it down until he fights."
"14848","Abd al-Samad and Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, they said: Hisham narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me on an errand of his, so I returned to him while he was on his mount, and I greeted him and he did not reply to me, and I saw him bowing and prostrating, so I withdrew from him, then he said to me: What did you do about your errand? I said: I did such and such. He said: Nothing prevented me from replying to you except that I was praying."
"14849","Abu Jafar al-Madaini Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Warqa informed us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and we came to a watering place, and he said: Will you water, O Jabir? He said: So I said: Yes. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dismounted and I watered. He said: Then he went for his need and I placed ablution water for him, then he came and performed ablution, then he stood and prayed in a single garment, crossing its ends, so I stood behind him and he took my ear and placed me on his right."
"14850","Abd Allah ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Thawr ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the prayer times, so he said: Pray with me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Fajr when the dawn rose, then prayed Zuhr when the sun declined, then prayed Asr when a man's shadow was like him, then prayed Maghrib when the sun set, then prayed Isha when the twilight disappeared, then he prayed Fajr with brightness, then prayed Zuhr when a man's shadow was like him, then prayed Asr when a man's shadow was twice him, then prayed Maghrib before the disappearance of the twilight, then prayed Isha, and some of them said: A third of the night, and some of them said: Half of it."
"14851","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq and Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, they said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Utbah, and Ali said: Utbah ibn Abi Hakim informed us, Husayn ibn Harmalah narrated to me, from Abu Musabbih, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Horses have good tied in their forelocks, and booty, until the Day of Resurrection, and their people are aided over them, so wipe their forelocks and pray for blessing for them and hang necklaces on them, and do not hang them with strings. And Ali said: And do not hang strings on them."
"14852","Abu Salamah al-Khuzai narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ata, that Abd al-Malik ibn Jabir ibn Atik informed him that Jabir ibn Abd Allah informed him that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When a man is told a hadith and the speaker turns around, it is a trust."
"14853","Abu Salamah informed us, Bakr ibn Mudar informed us, from Amr ibn Jabir al-Hadrami, that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say about the plague: The one fleeing from it is like the one fleeing on the day of battle, and whoever endures in it will have the reward of a martyr."
"14854","Abu Salamah informed us, Bakr ibn Mudar informed us, Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Asad ibn Zurarah, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), on some of his journeys, saw people gathered around a man, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked, and they said: A man exhausted by fasting. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Righteousness is not fasting while traveling."
"14855","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah, meaning Ibn Amr al-Raqqi, informed us, from Abd al-Karim, from Ata, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An Umrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj."
"14856","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: What do you think, if I strive in the path of Allah with myself and my wealth until I am killed, patient, seeking reward, advancing, not retreating, shall I enter Paradise? He said: Yes. Then when he turned away he called him and said: Except if you have a debt with no repayment for it with you."
"14857","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned its meaning."
"14858","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir, he said: The wife of Sad ibn al-Rabi came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with her two daughters by Sad, and said: O Messenger of Allah, these are the two daughters of Sad ibn al-Rabi; their father was killed with you at Uhud as a martyr, and their uncle took their wealth and left nothing for them, and they cannot be married except with wealth. He said: So he said: Allah will judge in that. He said: Then the verse of inheritance was revealed, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to their uncle and said: Give the two daughters of Sad two-thirds, and their mother an eighth, and what remains is yours."
"14859","Zakariyya narrated to us, Ubayd Allah informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir, he said: He prayed with his companions in his house, so we said to him: Pray with us as we saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray. He said: So he prayed with us in a sheet, tying it under the armpits, and said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray."
"14860","Zakariyya informed us, Ubayd Allah informed us, and Husayn ibn Muhammad, they said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir, he said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in our rows in prayer, the Zuhr or Asr prayer, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached for something then withdrew, so the people withdrew, then when he finished the prayer Ubayy ibn Kab said to him: Something you did in prayer that you did not do. He said: Paradise was displayed to me with its blossom and beauty in it, so I took a bunch of grapes from it to bring to you, but I was prevented from it, and if I had brought it to you, all between heaven and earth would have eaten from it without diminishing anything, then the Fire was displayed to me, and when I felt its heat I withdrew from it, and most of those I saw in it were women who, when entrusted, disclose, and when asked, withhold, and when they ask, press. Husayn said: And when they are given, they do not thank. And I saw in it Luhayy ibn Amr dragging his intestines in the Fire, and the one I saw most resembling him was Mabad ibn Aktham al-Kabi. Mabad said: O Messenger of Allah, is resemblance feared for me, though he is a father? He said: No, you are a believer and he is a disbeliever. Husayn said: And he was the first who led the Arabs to worship idols. Husayn said: I withdrew from it, and were it not for that it would have overwhelmed you."
"14861","Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us, Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: There was a man of the Ansar called Abu Shuayb, and he had a butcher boy, so he said to him: Make food for us, perhaps I will invite the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as the sixth of six. So he invited them, and a man followed them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: This one has followed us, do you permit him? He said: Yes."
"14862","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abu Uways narrated to us, Shurahbil narrated to us, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade the price of the dog, and said: It is food of Jahiliyyah."
"14863","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, that Abu al-Zubayr narrated to him that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah mention that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says: For what rivers and flood irrigate, a tenth, and for what is irrigated by the camel, half a tenth."
"14864","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Shihab informed us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the year of al-Jiranah while he was dividing silver in the garment of Bilal for the people, then a man said: O Messenger of Allah, be just. He said: Woe to you, and who will be just if I am not just? I have indeed failed if I am not just. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, let me kill this hypocrite. So he said: Allah forbid that people talk that I kill my companions. This one and his companions recite the Quran not passing their throats or their collarbones; they pass through religion as the arrow passes from the target."
"14865","Hashim narrated to us, Abu Jafar narrated to us, from al-Rabi ibn Anas, from al-Hasan, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every newborn is born upon fitrah until his tongue expresses from him, then when his tongue expresses from him, either grateful or ungrateful."
"14866","Hashim narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Amr ibn Murrah and Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: Thirst struck us at al-Hudaybiyah, so we rushed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and before him was a small vessel with water in it, so he said with his fingers thus in it, and said: Take, in the name of Allah. He said: So the water flowed from between his fingers as if springs, and it sufficed us and was enough for us. And Husayn said in his hadith: So we drank and performed ablution."
"14867","Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Hajjaj ibn Abi Zaynab, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What a good condiment vinegar is; no house with vinegar in it is destitute."
"14868","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Abu Bishr narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Qays, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: We slaughtered with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of al-Hudaybiyah seventy camels, the camel for seven."
"14869","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Abu Bishr Jafar ibn Abi Wahshiyyah narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Qays, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Abu Taybah and he cupped him. He said: So he asked him: How much is your tax? He said: Three sas. He said: So he reduced a sa from him."
"14870","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The stray animal is without liability, and the well is without liability, and the mine is without liability, and in buried treasure is a fifth. He said: And al-Shabi said: Al-rikaz is the ancient buried treasure."
"14871","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are today upon a religion, and I will boast multitude with you over the nations, so do not walk backward after me."
"14872","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, Ubayd Allah ibn Miqsam narrated to me, Jabir ibn Abd Allah narrated to me, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a funeral passed by us, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and we stood with him, then we went to carry it, when it was the funeral of a Jewish woman, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, it is the funeral of a Jewish woman. He said: Death has a fright, so when you see the funeral, stand for it."
"14873","Abu al-Mughirah and Muhammad ibn Musab narrated to us, they said: al-Awzai narrated to us, Ata narrated to me, and Ibn Musab said: From Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir, he said: Men had surplus lands, and they used to lease them for a third and a fourth and a half, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has land, let him plant it or lend it to his brother, and if he refuses, let him keep his land."
"14874","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Safwan narrated to us, Maiz al-Tamimi narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The throne of Iblis is upon the sea; he sends his detachments every day tempting people, and the greatest of them in status with him is the greatest of them in tempting people."
"14875","Al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, from Maiz al-Tamimi, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Do the people of Paradise eat? He said: Yes, and they drink, and they do not urinate therein nor defecate nor spit; that is only belching and sweat like the sweat of musk, and they are inspired with tasbih and tahmid as you are inspired with breath."
"14876","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Safwan narrated to us, from Maiz al-Tamimi, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Satan has despaired that the worshippers worship him, but in stirring discord among them."
"14877","Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says when he hears the call: O Allah, Lord of this complete call and the established prayer, give Muhammad al-wasilah and excellence, and raise him to the praised station which You promised him, except intercession becomes due for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"14878","Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that an amir from the amirs of fitnah came to Madinah, while the sight of Jabir had gone, so it was said to Jabir: If you withdrew from him. So he went out walking between his two sons and stumbled, then said: Wretched is whoever frightens the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). His two sons, or one of them, said: O father, and how did he frighten the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) though he has died? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever frightens the people of Madinah has frightened what is between my sides."
"14879","Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to me, Abu al-Zubayr informed me, he said: I heard Jabir say: My eye saw and my ear heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Jiranah, while in the garment of Bilal was silver, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was handing it to the people, giving them, then a man said: Be just. He said: Woe to you, and who will be just if I am not just? Umar ibn al-Khattab said: O Messenger of Allah, let me kill this evil hypocrite. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah forbid that people talk that I kill my companions. This one and his companions recite the Quran not passing their collarbones; they pass through religion as the arrow passes from the target."
"14880","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Muan ibn Rifah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided the spoils of Hawazin among the people at al-Jiranah, a man from Banu Tamim stood and said: Be just, O Muhammad. He said: Woe to you, and who will be just if I am not just? I have indeed failed and lost if I am not just. He said: So Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not stand and kill this hypocrite? He said: Allah forbid that the nations hear that Muhammad kills his companions. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This one and companions for him recite the Quran not passing their collarbones; they pass through religion as the arrow passes from the target. Muadh said: So Abu al-Zubayr said to me: I presented this hadith to al-Zuhri, and he did not differ from me except that he said: Al-nadiyy. I said: Al-qidh? He said: Are you not an Arab man?"
"14881","Yazid ibn Abd Rabbihi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb narrated to us, al-Zubaydi narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Amr ibn Aban ibn Uthman, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that he used to narrate that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A righteous man was shown tonight that Abu Bakr was attached to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Umar was attached to Abu Bakr, and Uthman was attached to Umar. Jabir said: So when we rose from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we said: As for the righteous man, it is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and as for the mention of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of the attaching of some of them to some, they are the rulers of this matter with which Allah sent His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"14882","Hashim narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Sayyar Abu al-Hakam narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Shabi narrate from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you enters at night, let him not come to his family by surprise, so that the woman whose husband was absent shaves and the unkempt combs."
"14883","Yunus ibn Muhammad and Hujayn narrated to us, they said: Layth narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: On the day of al-Hudaybiyah we were one thousand four hundred, so we pledged him, with Umar holding his hand under the tree, and it is a samurah, and he said: We pledged him not to flee, and we did not pledge him unto death."
"14884","Yunus narrated to us, Salih ibn Muslim ibn Ruman narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr Muhammad ibn Muslim informed me, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a man gives a woman a dowry filling his hands with food, she is lawful to him."
"14885","Yunus narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Harith, or Ibn Abi al-Harith, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and a man of his companions entered upon a man of the Ansar in a garden while he was turning water, and he said: Do you have water that spent this night in a skin? Otherwise we lap. He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. So he went with him to the trellis and milked a sheep for him, then poured over it water that spent the night in a skin, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank and watered his companion."
"14886","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Ayyub, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he poured forth from Arafah, began saying with his hand: Tranquility, servants of Allah, tranquility, servants of Allah."
"14887","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over al-Najashi, and we lined behind him in two rows."
"14888","Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Qays ibn Sulaym al-Anbari narrated to us, Yazid al-Faqir narrated to me, Jabir ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will exit the Fire burning in it except the circles of their faces, until they enter Paradise."
"14889","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Yazid, meaning Ibn al-Had, from Yahya ibn Said, from Jafar ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Hakam, from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Cover the vessel and tie the waterskin, for in the year there is a night in which pestilence descends; it does not pass an uncovered vessel nor an untied waterskin except some of that pestilence falls into it."
"14890","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Yazid, meaning Ibn al-Had, from Umar ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn, that he said: It reached me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Lessen going out after stillness, for Allah Almighty has creatures He spreads, and when you hear the barking of a dog or the braying of donkeys, seek refuge in Allah from Satan."
"14891","And he said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Yazid said: And Shurahbil narrated this hadith to me, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: He heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"14892","Sulayman ibn Hayyan Abu Khalid, meaning al-Ahmar, narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw with pebbles like khadhf pebbles."
"14893","Sulayman ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: I do not know with how many the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw."
"14894","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Ayyub, he said: I heard Mujahid say, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Labbayk for Hajj, then he commanded us and we made it Umrah."
"14895","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd and Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Nadrah, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: We enjoyed two mutahs at the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Hajj and women, then Umar forbade us from them and we stopped."
"14896","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, Abu al-Malih narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The first news that came to us about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was that a woman had a follower, he said: So he came to her in the form of a bird and fell upon a trunk of theirs. He said: So she said: Will you not come down so we inform you and you inform us? He said: A man has emerged in Makkah who forbade us adultery and prevented fleeing."
"14897","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A man shall not touch a man in a single garment, nor shall a woman touch a woman in a single garment."
"14898","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, my master al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab informed me, that Jabir ibn Abd Allah said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) Eid al-Adha, then when he finished a ram was brought and he slaughtered it and said: In the name of Allah, Allah is Greatest, O Allah, this is from me and from whoever has not sacrificed of my nation."
"14899","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, Abu al-Malih narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will appear to you from under this wall a man from the people of Paradise. He said: So Abu Bakr appeared to them, may Allah be pleased with him, and we congratulated him for what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. Then he stayed a while, then said: There will appear to you from under this wall a man from the people of Paradise. He said: So Umar appeared. He said: So we congratulated him for what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. He said: Then he said: There will appear to you from under this wall a man from the people of Paradise. O Allah, if You wish, make him Ali, three times. So Ali appeared, may Allah be pleased with him."
"14900","Yunus and Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever revives a dead land has a reward in it, and what wild creatures eat from it is charity for him. And Ibn Abi Bukayr said: Whoever revives a dead land, it is his."
"14901","Haddathana Affan and Hasan and Yunus, they said: Thana Hammad - Affan said in his hadith: Akhbarana Abu al-Zubayr - from Jabir, he said: We slaughtered on the day of Khaybar horses and mules and donkeys, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us mules and donkeys, and he did not forbid us horses."
"14902","Haddathana Yunus, Haddathana Hammad, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade muzabanah and muhaqalah and mukhabarah and thunya and muawamah."
"14903","Haddathana Yunus and Affan, they said: Haddathana Hammad - Affan said in his hadith: Akhbarana Abu al-Zubayr - from Jabir, in what I think, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of water."
"14904","Haddathana Yunus, Haddathana Hammad, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dubba and muzaffat and naqir."
"14905","Haddathana Yunus and Affan, they said: Haddathana Hammad, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in a single garment wrapped in it - Affan said: He had crossed its two ends."
"14906","Haddathana Mamar ibn Sulayman al-Raqqi, Haddathana Hajjaj, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, is Umrah obligatory? He said: No."
"14907","Haddathana Abd al-Quddus ibn Bakr ibn Khunays, Akhbarana Hajjaj, from Abu al-Zubayr, he said: Jabir was asked about what is supplicated for the dead, so he said: Neither the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) nor Abu Bakr nor Umar permitted us anything concerning it."
"14908","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Humayd Abu Sufyan, meaning al-Mamari, from Sufyan - and Abu Ahmad Haddathana Sufyan - from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The disbeliever eats in seven intestines, and the believer eats in one intestine."
"14909","Haddathana Yahya ibn Ishaq, Haddathana Ibn Lahiah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: One who saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in a single garment, having crossed its two ends, informed me."
"14910","Haddathana Ali ibn Thabit, Haddathani Abd Allah ibn al-Muammal, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The water of Zamzam is for what it is drunk for."
"14911","Haddathana Miskin ibn Bukayr, Haddathana al-Awzai, from Hassan ibn Atiyyah, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us visiting in our house, and he saw a disheveled man, so he said: Could this one not find something with which to settle his head? And he saw a man upon him dirty clothes, so he said: Could this one not find something with which to wash his clothes?"
"14912","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Ubayd, Haddathana Abd al-Malik, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dubba and muzaffat."
"14913","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Ubayd, Haddathana Abd al-Malik, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah - and Haddathana Muawiyah ibn Amr, Anbaana Zaidah, Haddathana Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil ibn Abi Talib, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shrouded Hamzah, may Allah be pleased with him, in a single garment. Jabir said: That garment was a namirah."
"14914","Haddathana Ammar ibn Muhammad, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of these five prayers is the likeness of a flowing river at the door of one of you; he bathes in it every day five times, so what would that leave of dirt?"
"14915","Haddathana Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata, from Said, from Qatadah, from Sulayman al-Yashkuri, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever has a partner in a walled garden, let him not sell it until he offers it to him."
"14916","Haddathana Abd al-Wahhab, meaning Ibn Ata, Anbaana Usamah ibn Zayd al-Laythi, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque, and in it were a people reciting the Quran. He said: Recite the Quran and seek Allah, Mighty and Majestic, by it, before there come a people who set it upright like the setting upright of the arrow, hastening it for this world and not deferring it."
"14917","Haddathana Abd al-Wahhab, Akhbarana Hisham ibn Abi Abd Allah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not wrap yourselves in samma in a single garment, and let none of you eat with his left hand, nor walk in a single sandal, nor sit ihtiba in a single garment."
"14918","Haddathana Abd al-Wahhab, Haddathana Hisham, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in ihram for a pain in his back or in his hip - Hisham doubted."
"14919","Haddathana Abd al-Wahhab, Akhbarana Hisham, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of palm trees until they become edible."
"14920","Haddathana Ubaydah ibn Humayd, Haddathani Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tasbih in prayer is for men, and clapping is for women."
"14921","Haddathana Ubaydah, Haddathani al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Nubayh al-Anazi, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: We traveled with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: The prayer came due. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is there any purification water among the people? He said: A man came with a leftover in a water skin. He said: He poured it into a cup. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution, then the people came to the remainder of the purification water and said: Wipe, wipe. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard them and said: Take it easy. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck his hand into the cup into the water. He said: Then he said: Perform ablution fully, the purification water. He said: Jabir ibn Abd Allah said: By the One who took away my sight - he said, and his sight had gone - I saw the water gushing from between the fingers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did not lift his hand until they all performed ablution. Al-Aswad said: I think he said: We were two hundred or more."
"14922","Haddathana Ubaydah, Haddathani al-Aswad, from Nubayh al-Anazi, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Jabir, do you have a wife? He said: I said: Yes. He said: Did you marry a previously married woman or a virgin? He said: I said to him: I married her while she was previously married. He said: He said to me: Why did you not marry her a young girl? He said: I said to him: My father was killed with you on such-and-such day, and he left young girls, so I disliked to bring together with them a girl like one of them, so I married a previously married woman who removes lice from one of them and sews the shirt of one of them when it tears. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then what you saw is good."
"14923","Haddathana Ubaydah, Haddathana al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Nubayh al-Anazi, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid one of us, when he came from a journey, to come upon his family by night. He said: Then we came upon them by night afterwards."
"14924","Haddathana Ubaydah, Haddathana al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Nubayh al-Anazi, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, he narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he intended a raid, so he said: O company of Muhajirun and Ansar, among your brothers are a people who have neither wealth nor clan, so let one of you join to himself two or three men. None of us had of the back of his camel except a turn like the turn of one of them. He said: I joined two or three to myself, and I had nothing but a turn like the turn of one of them from my camel."
"14925","Haddathana Ubaydah, Haddathana al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Nubayh, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: I lost my camel one night, so I passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was fastening for Aishah. He said: He said to me: What is the matter with you, O Jabir? He said: I said: I lost my camel, or my camel went away on a dark night. He said: He said to me: This is your camel, go and take it. He said: I went toward what he told me, and I did not find it. He said: I returned to him and said: O Prophet of Allah, I did not find it. He said: He said to me: This is your camel, go and take it. He said: I went toward what he told me, and I did not find it. He said: I returned to him and said: By my father and mother, O Prophet of Allah, no, by Allah, I did not find it. He said: He said to me: Wait, until when he finished he took my hand and set out with me until we came to the camel, and he handed it to me. He said: This is your camel. He said: And the people had departed. He said: While I was traveling on my camel in my turn - he said, and it was a camel in which was slowness - he said: I said: O my mother’s grief, that I should have but a slow camel. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was traveling behind me. He said: He heard what I said. He said: He caught up with me and said: What did you say before, O Jabir? He said: I forgot what I said. He said: I said: I said nothing, O Prophet of Allah. He said: Then I remembered what I said. He said: I said: O Prophet of Allah, O my grief, that I should have but a slow camel. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck the rump of the camel with a whip, or with my whip. He said: It set out the swiftest, or fastest, camel I ever rode, while it was pulling its halter from me. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Will you sell me this camel of yours? He said: I said: Yes. He said: For how much? He said: I said: For an uqiyyah. He said: He said to me: Splendid, splendid, how much in an uqiyyah of a water-carrying camel and a water-carrying camel? He said: I said: O Prophet of Allah, there is no water-carrying camel in Madinah I would love to be ours in its place. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have taken it for an uqiyyah. He said: I dismounted from the saddle to the ground. He said: What is the matter with you? He said: I said: It is your camel. He said: He said to me: Ride your camel. He said: I said: It is not my camel, but it is your camel. He said: We would review him twice in a matter when he commanded us with it, then when he commanded us the third time we would not review him. He said: I rode the camel until I came to my paternal aunt in Madinah. He said: I said to her: Have you not seen that I sold our water-carrier to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for an uqiyyah? He said: I did not see that it pleased her. He said: And it was an excellent water-carrier. He said: Then I took some tree leaves and fed them to it, then I took its halter and led it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing with a man speaking to him. He said: I said: Here is your camel, O Prophet of Allah. He said: He took its halter, then he called Bilal and said: Weigh for Jabir an uqiyyah and give him full measure. I set out with Bilal, and he weighed for me an uqiyyah and gave more than the weight. He said: I returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was standing talking to that man. He said: I said to him: He weighed for me an uqiyyah and gave me full. He said: While he was thus, I went to my house without perceiving. He said: He called: Where is Jabir? They said: He went to his family. He said: Catch up, bring him to me. He said: His messenger came to me hurrying. He said: O Jabir, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) calls you. He said: I came to him, and he said: Take your camel. I said: It is not my camel, it is your camel, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Take your camel. I said: It is not my camel, it is your camel, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Take your camel. He said: I took it. He said: He said: By my life, we did not benefit you only to dismount you from it. He said: I came to my paternal aunt with the water-carrier with me and with the uqiyyah. He said: I said to her: What do you think? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me an uqiyyah and returned my camel to me."
"14926","Haddathana Yaqub, Haddathana my father, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Haddathani Sadaqah ibn Yasar, from Aqil ibn Jabir, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, concerning what he mentions of the striving of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in worship, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and in another place: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a raid of Najd - and he seized the wife of a man of the polytheists, toward Najd, and we came upon a dwelling of the dwellings of the polytheists. He said: We seized the wife of a man of them. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned back returning, and her husband came, and he had been absent, and her affliction was mentioned to him, so he swore he would not return until he shed blood among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on part of the road, he alighted in a mountain pass of the passes, and said: Who are two men to guard us this night of ours from our enemy? He said: A man of the Muhajirun and a man of the Ansar said: We will guard you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: They went out to the mouth of the pass before the camp. Then the Ansari said to the Muhajiri: Will you suffice me the first of the night and I suffice you the last, or will you suffice me the last and I suffice you the first? He said: The Muhajiri said: Rather suffice me the first, and I suffice you the last. The Muhajiri slept, and the Ansari stood praying. He said: He opened a surah of the Quran, and while he was in it reciting, the husband of the woman came. He said: When he saw the man standing, he knew he was the watcher of the people, so he draws an arrow for him and places it in him. He said: He pulls it out and lays it down, while he is standing reciting in the surah he is in, and he did not move, disliking to cut it off. He said: Then the husband of the woman returned for him with another arrow and placed it in him, and he pulled it out and laid it down, while he is standing praying, and he did not move, disliking to cut it off. He said: Then the husband of the woman returned for him the third time with an arrow and placed it in him, and he pulled it out and laid it down, then he bowed and prostrated, then he said to his companion: Sit, for I have been hit. He said: The Muhajiri sat. When the husband of the woman saw them both, he fled, and knew he had been warned of. He said: And the Ansari was gushing blood from the shots of the husband of the woman. He said: His Muhajiri brother said to him: May Allah forgive you, why did you not alert me the first time he shot you? He said: He said: I was in a surah of the Quran I had opened, praying with it, and I disliked to cut it off. By Allah, were it not that I would waste a post the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to guard it, my soul would have been cut off before I cut it off."
"14927","Haddathana Yaqub, Haddathana my father, from Ibn Ishaq, Haddathani Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from his uncle Wasi ibn Habban, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded thereby, from every harvest, ten awsuq of dates."
"14928","Haddathana Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik, Haddathana Muhammad ibn Salamah, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from his uncle Wasi ibn Habban, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded, from every harvest, ten awsuq of dates, with a cluster hung in the mosque for the poor."
"14929","Haddathana Yaqub, Haddathana my father, from Ibn Ishaq, Haddathani Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from his uncle Wasi ibn Habban, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he permitted the people of araya to sell them by their estimate, saying: The wasq and the two wasqs and the three and the four."
"14930","Haddathana Yaqub, Haddathana my father, from Ibn Ishaq, Haddathani Dawud ibn al-Husayn, freedman of Amr ibn Uthman, from Waqid ibn Amr ibn Sad ibn Muadh, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When one of you proposes to a woman, if he can see of her some of what invites him to her, let him do so."
"14931","Haddathana Yaqub, Haddathana my father, from some of his family, from his father, from Talq ibn Habib, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Guard against the onset of the evening meal, as it were, because of what is feared of crowding."
"14932","Haddathana Yaqub, Haddathana Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab, from his uncle - and Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman Haddathani that Jabir ibn Abd Allah informed him - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed that whoever grants a man a life-grant for him and his posterity, it belongs to the one to whom it is granted; he has made it final, cut off from its owner who granted it, whatever falls of the inheritances of Allah and His right."
"14933","Haddathana Yaqub, Haddathana my father, from Ibn Ishaq, Haddathani Aban ibn Salih, from Mujahid ibn Jabr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had forbidden us to face the qiblah or turn our backs to it with our private parts when we pass water. He said: Then I saw him, a year before his death, urinating facing the qiblah."
"14934","Haddathana Yaqub, Haddathana my father, from Ibn Ishaq, Haddathani Muadh ibn Rifah al-Ansari, then al-Zuraqi, from Mahmud ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn al-Jamuh, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day to Sad ibn Muadh when he died. He said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over him, and he was placed in his grave, and it was leveled over him, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) glorified Allah, and we glorified long, then he said takbir, and we said takbir. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, why did you glorify then say takbir? He said: This righteous servant’s grave had become constricted upon him, until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, relieved him of it."
"14935","Haddathana Qutaybah, Haddathana Ibn Lahiah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take many sandals, for a man remains mounted as long as he wears sandals."
"14936","Haddathana Qutaybah, Haddathana Bakr ibn Mudar, from Amr ibn Jabir al-Hadrami, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one fleeing from plague is like the one fleeing from battle, and the one patient in it has the reward of a martyr."
"14937","Haddathana Qutaybah, Haddathana al-Mufaddal ibn Fadalah, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata and Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mukhabarah and muzabanah and muhaqalah, and the sale of fruit until it becomes edible, except araya."
"14938","Haddathana Qutaybah ibn Said, Haddathana al-Munkadir ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every good is charity, and of good is that you meet your brother with a cheerful face, and that you pour from your bucket into the vessel of your brother."
"14939","Haddathana Qutaybah, Haddathana Ibn Lahiah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The bird of every man is in his neck. Ibn Lahiah said: Meaning augury."
"14940","Haddathana Qutaybah ibn Said, Haddathana Ibn Lahiah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no one who supplicates with a supplication but Allah gives him what he asked, or averts from him like it of evil, so long as he does not supplicate with sin or severing kinship."
"14941","Haddathana Qutaybah, Haddathana Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that a man came from Jayshan - and Jayshan is of Yemen - and asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a drink they drink in their land, of corn, called mizr. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is it intoxicating? He said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is forbidden, and upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is a covenant for whoever drinks an intoxicant, to give him to drink of the mud of khabal. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the mud of khabal? He said: The sweat of the people of the Fire, or the juice of the people of the Fire."
"14942","Haddathana Ali ibn Abd Allah al-Madini, Haddathana Sufyan, Haddathana Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Rabiah al-Sulami, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Jabir, did you not know that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, brought your father to life and said to him: Wish of Me? He said: I am returned to the world and killed another time. He said: I have decreed the decree that they to it shall not be returned."
"14943","Haddathana Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad al-Khattabi, Haddathana Ubayd Allah, meaning Ibn Amr al-Raqqi, from Abd al-Karim, from Ata, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An Umrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj."
"14944","Haddathana Ali, Haddathana Sufyan, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the Jews: I will ask them about the soil of Paradise, and it is fine white flour. He asked them, and they said: It is a loaf, O Abu al-Qasim. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The loaf is of fine flour."
"14945","Haddathana Abd Allah, Haddathana Bahz, Haddathana Salim ibn Hayyan, Haddathana Said ibn Mina, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of fruit until it becomes fit. He said: I said to Said: What is becomes fit? He said: It reddens and yellows, and some of it is eaten."
"14946","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Hammad, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and Humayd from al-Hasan - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a sword be handed over unsheathed."
"14947","Haddathana Affan and Bahz, they said: Haddathana Hammam, Haddathana Qatadah, from Ata, Haddathani Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Umra is permissible."
"14948","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Salim ibn Hayyan, Akhbarana Said ibn Mina, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My likeness and the likeness of the prophets is the likeness of a man who kindled a fire, and moths and locusts began falling into it. He said: And he is driving them from it. He said: And I am holding you by your waist-wrappers from the Fire, while you slip from my hand."
"14949","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Salim ibn Hayyan, Haddathana Said ibn Mina, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: My likeness and the likeness of the prophets is the likeness of a man who built a house, and completed it and made it excellent, except the place of a brick. People began entering it and admiring it, saying: Were it not for the place of the brick. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the place of the brick; I came and sealed the prophets."
"14950","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Salim ibn Hayyan, Haddathana Said ibn Mina, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over Ashamah al-Najashi, and said takbir over him four times."
"14951","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Hammad ibn Zayd, Haddathana Amr ibn Dinar, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of Khaybar the flesh of donkeys, and permitted the flesh of horses."
"14952","Haddathana Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi, Akhbarana Abthar ibn al-Qasim Abu Zubayd, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gifted sheep to the House."
"14953","Haddathana Yahya ibn Ghaylan, Haddathana al-Mufaddal, Haddathani Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Husayn, from Amr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Jarhad, he said: I heard a man saying to Jabir ibn Abd Allah: Who remains with you of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Anas ibn Malik and Salamah ibn al-Akwa remain. A man said: As for Salamah, he has turned back from his migration. Jabir said: Do not say that, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying to Aslam: Go out to the desert, O Aslam. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we fear we may turn back after our migration. He said: You migrate wherever you are."
"14954","Haddathana Said ibn Mansur, Haddathana Yaqub ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: I witnessed the sacrifice with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the prayer place. When he finished his sermon, a ram was brought, and he slaughtered it with his hand, and said: In the name of Allah, and by Allah, O Allah, this is from me and from whoever of my Ummah did not sacrifice."
"14955","Haddathana Said ibn Mansur and Qutaybah ibn Said, they said: Haddathana Yaqub ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from al-Muttalib, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - and Qutaybah said in his hadith: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The game of the land is lawful for you - Said said: While you are in ihram, so long as you do not hunt it or it is hunted for you."
"14956","Haddathana Qutaybah, Haddathana Yaqub, from Amr, from al-Muttalib, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: I witnessed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the sacrifice at the prayer place. When he finished his sermon, he descended from his pulpit, and a ram was brought, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughtered it with his hand, and said: In the name of Allah, and Allah is Most Great, this is from me and from whoever of my Ummah did not sacrifice."
"14957","Haddathana Aswad ibn Amir, Akhbarana Abu Bakr, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a raid. He said: I asked permission to hasten. I said: I have married. He said: A previously married woman or a virgin? He said: I said: Previously married. He said: Why was she not a virgin, you play with her and she plays with you? He said: Go, and act sensibly. Abu Bakr said: Meaning: Do not come upon them by night."
"14958","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Hammad ibn Salamah, Akhbarana Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us that one of us walk in a single sandal."
"14959","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Hammad ibn Salamah, he said: Akhbarana Habib al-Muallim, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep your children in until the onset of the evening goes, for it is an hour in which devils spread."
"14960","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Hammad, Akhbarana Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to close the doors, and to tie the water skins, and to extinguish the lamps, and to hold back our livestock until the darkness of the evening goes, and he forbade us that a man eat with his left hand, and that he walk in a single sandal, and samma and ihtiba in a single garment."
"14961","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Hammad, Akhbarana Qays ibn Sad, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived when four of Dhu al-Hijjah had passed. When we circumambulated the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Make it an Umrah, except whoever has the sacrificial animal with him. When the day of Tarwiyah came, they entered ihram for Hajj. When the day of sacrifice came, they circumambulated, and they did not walk between al-Safa and al-Marwah."
"14962","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim, Haddathana Sulayman al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah - and from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be right and draw near, and the deed of none of you will save him. We said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even me, except that Allah envelop me from Him with mercy."
"14963","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim, Haddathana Sulayman al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah - and from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be right and draw near, and the deed of none of you will save him. We said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even me, except that Allah envelop me from Him with mercy."
"14964","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Hammad ibn Salamah, Haddathana Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: We slaughtered on the day of Khaybar horses and mules and donkeys, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us mules and donkeys, and he did not forbid horses."
"14965","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Hammad ibn Salamah, Akhbarana Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Jabir in the raid of Tabuk - he said, and my camel had become exhausted - and said: What is the matter with you, O Jabir? I said: My camel has stopped. He said: He came to it from before its rear - and Affan said, and its rear is the same - and he supplicated and drove it. He said: It kept leading the camels. He said: He came upon him and said: What happened to the camel? I said: It keeps leading them. He said: For how much did you take it? I said: For thirteen dinars. He said: Sell it to me for the price, and its back is yours to Madinah. I said: Yes. He said: When I arrived in Madinah, I haltered it, then I brought it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he gave me the price and gave me the camel."
"14966","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Hammad, Akhbarana Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered on the day of the conquest of Makkah, and upon him was a black turban."
"14967","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Hammad, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cauterized Sad ibn Muadh for his wound."
"14968","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Yazid ibn Ibrahim, Haddathana Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was preaching, and said: Did you pray the two rakahs? He said: No. He said: Pray them. He said: And Jabir used to say: If he prayed in his house, it pleases him, when he enters, to pray them."
"14969","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Yazid ibn Ibrahim, Haddathana Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him for some of his need. He said: He came, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying on his mount. He said: He greeted him, and he was silent. He greeted him, and he was silent. He greeted him, and he was silent, three times. He said: He said to him, when he finished: Nothing prevented me from answering you except that I was praying. He said: He prayed wherever his mount faced."
"14970","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Yazid ibn Ibrahim, Haddathana Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in ihram for a sprain he had."
"14971","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Shubah, Akhbarani Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and knocked on the door. He said: Who is this? I said: Me. He said: Me, me, as though he disliked it."
"14972","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Salim ibn Hayyan, Haddathana Said ibn Mina, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over Ashamah al-Najashi, and said takbir over him four times."
"14973","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Hammad ibn Salamah, Akhbarana Matar, from a man, I think him al-Hasan, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not exempt one who kills after taking the blood money."
"14974","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Said ibn Yazid, Akhbarana Layth, from Abu Bakr - and Affan said once: From Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad - from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever revives a land at a call from the town, or a throw from the town, it is his."
"14975","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Abd al-Wahid, Haddathana Hajjaj, from Ata, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go out on Eid, and bring out his family."
"14976","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Hammad, Akhbarana Qays ibn Sad, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed the camel for seven, and the cow for seven."
"14977","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Shubah, he said: Muharib ibn Dithar Akhbarani, he said: I heard Jabir saying: He was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and when he came to Madinah, he commanded him to come to the mosque and pray two rakahs."
"14978","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Hammad, Akhbarana Ali ibn Zayd and Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Nadrah, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: We performed tamattu of two mutahs in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Hajj and women - and Hammad also said: The mutah of Hajj and the mutah of women - then when Umar was, he forbade us them, and we abstained."
"14979","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Hammam, he said: Sulayman ibn Musa asked Ata, and I was witness, he said: Did Jabir narrate to you that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that unripe dates and ripe dates be steeped together, and raisins and dates together? Ata said: Yes."
"14980","And Sulayman ibn Musa said to him, and I was witness: Did Jabir narrate to you that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has land, let him cultivate it, or let his brother cultivate it, and let him not rent it? Ata said: Yes."
"14981","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Hammad ibn Salamah, Akhbarana Habib al-Muallim, from Ata, from Jabir, that a man said on the day of the conquest: O Messenger of Allah, I vowed, if Allah opens Makkah for you, to pray in Bayt al-Maqdis. He said: Pray here. He asked him. He said: Pray here. He asked him. He said: Then as you wish."
"14982","Haddathana Affan and Bahz, they said: Haddathana Hammam, he said: Bahz said: Haddathana Qatadah, he said: Sulayman ibn Hisham said to me: This one, meaning al-Zuhri, does not leave us eating anything but he commands us to perform ablution from it, meaning what fire touched. He said: I said to him: I asked about it Said ibn al-Musayyab, and he said: If you ate it, it is good, there is no ablution upon you for it; when it comes out, it is foul, upon you for it is ablution. He said: Is there in the town anyone? He said: I said: Yes, the most advanced man in the Arabian Peninsula in knowledge. He said: Who? I said: Ata ibn Abi Rabah. Bahz said: He sent to him, and he was brought. He said: He sent to him and said: Haddathani Jabir that they ate with Abu Bakr al-Siddiq bread and meat, and he prayed and did not perform ablution. He said: He said to Ata: What do you say, meaning about umra? He said: Haddathani Jabir that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Umra is permissible."
"14983","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Hammad ibn Zayd, Akhbarana Ayyub, from Abu al-Zubayr and Said ibn Mina, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade muhaqalah and muzabanah and muawamah - one of them said: And the sale of years - and the sale of thunya, and he permitted araya."
"14984","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Abd al-Wahid, Haddathana Sulayman ibn Mihran al-Amash, he said: I heard Abu Sufyan, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The people of Paradise eat in it and drink; they do not urinate, nor defecate, nor spit, nor blow their noses; their food is belching, and sweat like the sweat of musk."
"14985","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Abd al-Wahid, Haddathana Sulayman al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: We went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entering ihram for Hajj. We circumambulated the House and walked between al-Safa and al-Marwah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to dissolve. He said: We went out to al-Batha. He said: A man began saying: My covenant with my family is today. People spoke about that. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I faced of my affair what I have turned back from, I would have dissolved. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not dissolve, because he drove the sacrificial animal. We entered ihram when we headed to Mina."
"14986","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Abu Awanah, Haddathana Abu Bishr, Akhbarana Sulayman ibn Qays, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: We sacrificed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Hudaybiyah seventy camels; the camel for seven."
"14987","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Abu Awanah, Haddathana Abu Bishr, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought and asked his family for condiment. They said: We have nothing but vinegar. He said: He called for it, and began eating with it, saying: What an excellent condiment is vinegar."
"14988","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Hammad ibn Salamah, from Humayd, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that they would not put their hands in food until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the one to begin."
"14989","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Hammad ibn Salamah, Akhbarana Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that a man slaughtered before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, a young goat; The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It does not suffice for anyone after you, and he forbade that they slaughter until they pray."
"14990","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Aban, Haddathana Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: We came with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until when we were at Dhat al-Riqa. He said: When we came upon a shady tree, we left it for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). A man of the polytheists came, and the sword of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was hanging on a tree. He took the sword of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and drew it, then said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Do you fear me? He said: No. He said: Who prevents you from me? He said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, prevents me from you. He said: The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threatened him, so he sheathed the sword and hung it. Prayer was called, and he prayed with a group two rakahs, and they stepped back, and he prayed with the other group two rakahs. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had four rakahs, and the people two rakahs."
"14991","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Abu Awanah, Haddathana Abu Bishr, from Sulayman ibn Qays, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fought Muharib Khassafah at Nakhl. The Muslims gave them an opening. A man of them, called Ghawrath ibn al-Harith, came until he stood over the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the sword, and said: Who prevents you from me? He said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic. The sword fell from his hand, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it and said: Who prevents you from me? He said: Be as the best taker. He said: Do you testify that there is no god but Allah? He said: No, but I covenant you that I will not fight you, nor be with a people who fight you. He let him go. He said: He went to his companions. He said: I have come to you from the best of men. When it was noon or afternoon, he prayed with them the fear prayer. People were two groups: a group facing their enemy, and a group praying with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He prayed with the group who were with him two rakahs, then they left, and they were in the place of those who were facing their enemy, and those came, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with them two rakahs. The people had two rakahs each, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) four rakahs."
"14992","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Wuhayb, Haddathana Jafar, from his father, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to al-Aliyah and passed by the market, and passed by a dead kid with short ears. He took it and lifted it, then said: How much would you like this to be yours for? They said: We would not like it to be ours for anything, and what would we do with it? He said: How much would you like it to be yours for? They said: By Allah, had it been alive it would be a defect in it that it is short-eared, so how while it is dead? He said: By Allah, the world is more insignificant to Allah than this is to you."
"14993","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Hammad ibn Zayd, Haddathana Ayyub, Haddathana Mujahid, from Jabir, he said: We arrived with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while we were saying: Labbayk with Hajj. He commanded us, and we made it an Umrah."
"14994","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Abd al-Wahid, Haddathana al-Hajjaj, Haddathana Abu al-Zubayr, he said: Jabir ibn Abd Allah was asked: How did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do with the fifth? He said: He would carry a man with it in the path of Allah, then a man, then a man."
"14995","Haddathana Affan, Haddathana Shubah, Akhbarani Husayn and Amr ibn Murrah, they heard Salim, he said: I heard Jabir, he said: Thirst afflicted us, and we crowded toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: He placed his hand in a basin of water before him, and it began gushing from between his fingers as though springs - and Amr and Husayn, both said: Take, in the name of Allah - until it sufficed us and was enough for us - and he said to Jabir: How many were you? He said: We were a thousand and five hundred; had we been a hundred thousand, it would have sufficed us."
"14996","Haddathana al-Fadl ibn Dukayn, Haddathana Sharik, from Salamah, meaning Ibn Kuhayl, from Ata and Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that a man died and left a mudabbar and debt. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them to sell him for his debt, and they sold him for eight hundred."
"14997","Haddathana Abu Nuaym, Haddathana Zakariyya, Haddathana Amir, Haddathani Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that his father died owing debt. I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said to him: My father died owing debt, and I have nothing but what his palms yield, and what they yield does not reach a sixth of what is owed. He said: He went with me so that the creditors would not be harsh upon me. He walked around a heap of the heaps of dates, then he supplicated and sat upon it, and said: Where are his creditors? He paid them what was theirs, and there remained like what he gave them."
"14998","Haddathana Abu Nuaym, Haddathana Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who brings me news of the people on the day of al-Ahzab? Al-Zubayr said: I. Then he said: Who brings me news of the people? Al-Zubayr said: I. He said: Who brings me news of the people? Al-Zubayr said: I. He said: Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is al-Zubayr."
"14999","Haddathana Abu Nuaym, Haddathana Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, he said: I heard Jabir, he said: A bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Pledge me upon Islam. He pledged him upon Islam. Then he came the next day feverish and said: O Messenger of Allah, release me. He refused. Then he came the next day feverish and said: Release me. He refused. When he turned away, he said: Madinah is like the bellows; it expels its dross and makes its good pure."
"15000","Haddathana Abu Nuaym, Haddathana Sufyan, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a morsel of one of you falls, let him remove what touched it of harm, and let him not leave it for Satan, and let him not wipe his hand with the cloth until he licks it or has it licked, for he does not know in which of his food is the blessing."
"15001","Haddathana Abu Nuaym, Haddathana Sufyan, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The throne of Iblis is upon the sea, and he sends forth his detachments, and the greatest of them in his estimation is the greatest of them in trial."
"15002","Haddathana Abu Nuaym, Haddathana Sufyan, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Iblis has despaired of being worshipped by those who pray, but in stirring up discord among them."
"15003","Haddathanah Waki, from Sufyan, with its meaning."
"15004","Haddathana Abu Nuaym, Haddathana Sufyan, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Every servant will be raised upon that upon which he died."
"15005","Haddathana Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, meaning al-Zubayri, Haddathana Maqil, meaning Ibn Ubayd Allah al-Jazari, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as pilgrims, intending nothing but the Hajj and intending nothing else, until when we reached Sarif, Aishah menstruated, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in to her while she was weeping, and he said: What is with you, why are you weeping? She said: O Messenger of Allah, the ailment has afflicted me. He said: You are but one of the daughters of Adam; there befalls you what befalls them. He said: And we arrived at the Kabah after four of Dhu al-Hijjah had passed, days or nights, and we circumambulated the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us and we exited ihram fully. He said: And we discussed among ourselves and said: We went out as pilgrims intending nothing but the Hajj and intending nothing else, until when there remained between us and Arafat only four days or nights, we went out to Arafat while our male organs dripped semen from women. He said: And that reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he stood delivering a sermon and said: Verily Umrah has entered into the Hajj, and had I faced of my affair what I now look back upon, I would not have driven the sacrificial animals, and were it not for the sacrificial animals I would have exited ihram; so whoever does not have sacrificial animals with him, let him exit ihram. And Suraqah ibn Malik ibn Jushum stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, inform us with news of a people as though born today: is it for this year of ours or forever? He said: No, rather forever. He said: And we came to Arafat and departed from it, then Aishah said: O Messenger of Allah, I find within myself that they have performed Umrah. He said: You shall have the like of what they have. She said: O Messenger of Allah, I find within myself. And he halted at the upper part of the valley of Makkah and commanded her brother Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, and he mounted her behind him until she reached al-Tanim, then she came."
"15006","Haddathana Husayn ibn Muhammad and Khalaf ibn al-Walid, they said: Haddathana al-Rabi, meaning Ibn Subayh, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: We arrived with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the morning of the fourth of Dhu al-Hijjah that had passed, all of us entering ihram for Hajj, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us, and we circumambulated the House and prayed the two rakahs and ran between al-Safa and al-Marwah, then he commanded us and we shortened, then he said: Exit ihram. We said: O Messenger of Allah, what exiting? He said: The exiting of whatever becomes lawful for the non-muhrim, of women and perfume. He said: And women were approached and the incense burners diffused fragrance. Khalaf said: And it reached him that some of them said: One of us will go forth to Mina while his organ drips semen. He said: And he addressed them, and he praised Allah and extolled Him, then he said: Had I faced of my affair what I now look back upon, I would not have driven the sacrificial animals, and had I not driven the sacrificial animals I would have exited ihram. Verily, take your rites. He said: And the people remained in their exiting until when it was the day of al-Tarwiyah and they intended to head to Mina, they entered ihram for Hajj. He said: And the sacrificial animal was upon whoever found it, and fasting upon whoever did not find, and he joined them together in their sacrificial animals, the camel among seven and the cow among seven, and their circumambulation of the House and their running between al-Safa and al-Marwah for their Hajj and their Umrah was one circumambulation and one running."
"15007","Haddathana Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri, Haddathana Qatan, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), thinking only that we were pilgrims, and when we arrived at Makkah it was announced among us: Whoever among you does not have sacrificial animals with him, let him exit ihram, and whoever has sacrificial animals with him, let him remain in his ihram. He said: And the people exited ihram with an Umrah except whoever had driven the sacrificial animals. He said: And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained, and with him were one hundred camels, and Ali came from Yemen, and he said to him: With what did you enter ihram? He said: I said: O Allah, I enter ihram with that with which Your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram. He said: And he gave him somewhat more than thirty of the camels. He said: Then they both remained in their ihram until the sacrificial animals reached their place."
"15008","Haddathana Abu Ahmad, Haddathana Sufyan, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: People are minerals; the best of them in the Jahiliyyah are the best of them in Islam when they understand."
"15009","Haddathana Abu Ahmad, Haddathana Sufyan, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) moved forth with tranquility upon him, and he hastened in the valley of Muhassir, and he showed them the like of the pebbles of khadhf, and he commanded them with tranquility, and he said: Let my community take its rites, for I do not know, perhaps I shall not meet them after this year of mine."
"15010","Haddathana Hasan ibn al-Rabi, Haddathana Ibn Mubarak, from Utbah ibn Abi Hakim, from Husayn, from Abu al-Musabbih, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever both his feet become dusty in the path of Allah, they are both forbidden to the Fire."
"15011","Haddathana Ismail ibn Aban al-Warraq Abu Ishaq, Haddathana Yaqub, Akhbarana Isa ibn Jariyah, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: Ibn Umm Maktum came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my dwelling is distant and I am blind of sight, and I hear the call to prayer. He said: If you hear the call to prayer, then respond, even crawling or dragging."
"15012","Haddathana Abu al-Jawwab, Haddathana Ammar ibn Ruzayq, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prepared an army one night until half the night had gone, or it reached that, then he came out and said: The people have prayed and slept, and you are awaiting this prayer. Verily, you shall remain in prayer as long as you await it."
"15013","Haddathana Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri, Haddathana Sharik, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever intends to fast, let him take sahur with something."
"15014","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Sabiq, Haddathana Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that one of us walk in a single sandal."
"15015","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Sabiq, Haddathana Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: A man was struck with an arrow in his chest, or he said in his belly, and he died, and he was wrapped in his clothes as he was, and we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"15016","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Sabiq, Haddathana Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that he said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic granted Khaybar as spoils to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left them as they were, and made it between him and them, and he sent Abd Allah ibn Rawahah, and he assessed it against them, then he said to them: O company of Jews, you are the most hateful of creation to me; you killed the prophets of Allah the Mighty and Majestic and you lied against Allah, and my hatred of you does not move me to deal unjustly with you; I have assessed twenty thousand wasqs of dates, so if you wish then they are yours, and if you refuse then they are mine. And they said: By this the heavens and the earth stand; we have taken, so go out from us."
"15017","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Sabiq, Haddathana Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal will come forth in a lull of religion and a turning away of knowledge, and he will have forty nights roaming them in the earth, a day of them like a year, and a day of them like a month, and a day of them like a Friday, then the rest of his days like these days of yours, and he will have a donkey he rides, the width between its ears forty cubits, and he will say to the people: I am your lord, and he is one-eyed, and your Lord is not one-eyed, written between his eyes is kafir, kaf fa ra spelled out, which every believer will read, literate and illiterate; he will come to every water and watering place except Madinah and Makkah, which Allah has forbidden to him, and the angels will stand at their gates, and with him will be mountains of bread, and the people will be in hardship except whoever follows him, and with him will be two rivers, I know more about them than him, a river of which he says Paradise and a river of which he says Hell, so whoever is entered into that which he calls Paradise, it is the Fire, and whoever is entered into that which he calls Hell, it is Paradise. He said: And Allah will send with him devils speaking to the people, and with him will be a great trial; he will command the sky and it will rain in the sight of the people, and he will kill a soul then bring it to life in the sight of the people, he will not be given power over any other of the people, and he will say: O people, does any but the Lord the Mighty and Majestic do the like of this? He said: And the Muslims will flee to the mountain of al-Dukhan in Sham, and he will come to them and besiege them, and their siege will intensify and he will strain them with severe hardship, then Isa son of Maryam will descend and will call from the time before dawn and say: O people, what prevents you from going out to the lying wicked one? And they will say: This is a man who is a jinni. And they will set out, and behold they are with Isa son of Maryam (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the prayer will be established, and it will be said to him: Step forward, O Spirit of Allah. And he will say: Let your imam step forward and pray with you. And when he has prayed the dawn prayer, they will go out to him. He said: And when the liar sees him, he will melt as salt melts in water, and he will walk to him and kill him, until the tree and the stone will call: O Spirit of Allah, this is a Jew. And he will not leave any of those who followed him without killing him."
"15018","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Sabiq, Haddathana Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that he said: A woman of the Jews in Madinah gave birth to a boy whose eye was wiped, protruding and bulging, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) feared that he was the Dajjal, and he found him under a blanket murmuring, and his mother alerted him and said: O Abd Allah, here is Abu al-Qasim, he has come, so go out to him. And he came out of the blanket, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is with her, may Allah strike her dead; had she left him he would have made clear. Then he said: O Ibn Said, what do you see? He said: I see truth and I see falsehood and I see a throne upon the water. He said: And it was confused to him, and he said: Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah? And he said to him: Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah? And the Messenger of Allah said: I believe in Allah and His messengers. Then he went out and left him. Then he came to him another time and found him in his palm trees murmuring, and his mother alerted him and said: O Abd Allah, here is Abu al-Qasim, he has come. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is with her, may Allah strike her dead; had she left him he would have made clear. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was eager to hear something of his speech, that he might know whether it was him or not. He said: O Ibn Said, what do you see? He said: I see truth and I see falsehood and I see a throne upon the water. He said: Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah? He said to him: Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah? And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I believe in Allah and His Messenger, and it was confused to him. Then he went out and left him. Then he came a third or fourth time, and with him were Abu Bakr and Umar ibn al-Khattab among a group of the Emigrants and the Helpers, and I was with him. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hastened ahead of us, hoping to hear something of his speech, and his mother beat him to him and said: O Abd Allah, here is Abu al-Qasim, he has come. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is with her, may Allah strike her dead; had she left him he would have made clear. And he said: O Ibn Said, what do you see? He said: I see truth and I see falsehood and I see a throne upon the water. He said: Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah? He said: Do you bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah? And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I believe in Allah and His messengers, and it was confused to him. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Ibn Said, we have hidden for you something hidden, so what is it? He said: Al-Dukh al-Dukh. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Be gone, be gone. And Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Permit me to kill him, O Messenger of Allah. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If it is him, you are not his man; his man is only Isa son of Maryam (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and if it is not him, it is not for you to kill a man of the people of the covenant. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not cease fearing that he was the Dajjal."
"15019","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, Haddathana Shubah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, narrating from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) carrying the meat of the sacrificial animals as provision to Madinah."
"15020","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, Haddathana Shubah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: We used to do it in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), meaning azl. He said: I said to Amr: Did you hear it from Jabir? He said: No."
"15021","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, Haddathana Shubah, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I heard Jabir narrating that a man freed a slave of his as a dubur from him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for him and sold him."
"15022","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, Haddathana Shubah, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I heard Jabir narrating that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed and said: When one of you comes while the imam has come out, let him pray two rakahs."
"15023","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, Haddathana Shubah, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I heard Jabir say: Muadh used to pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then return and lead his people. He said: And he prayed with them once the Isha and recited the surah al-Baqarah, and a man set out deliberately and left, and Muadh would speak ill of him, and that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: A causer of trial, a causer of trial, or he said: A tempter, a tempter, a tempter. And he commanded him with two surahs of the middle mufassal. Amr said: I do not remember them."
"15024","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, Haddathana Shubah, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Why not a young girl you play with and she plays with you?"
"15025","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, Haddathana Said, from Qatadah, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that when the death of al-Najashi reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Pray over a brother of yours who died in other than your land. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions prayed over him. Jabir said: And I was in the second or the third row. He said: And his name was Ashamah."
"15026","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, Haddathana Shubah, from Husayn, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: A boy was born to a man of the Ansar, and he wanted to name him Muhammad, and he set out with him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they asked him, and he said: Name with my name and do not take my kunyah, for I was sent as a Qasim, dividing among you."
"15027","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, Haddathana Shubah, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that a man of the Ansar had a boy born to him and wanted to name him Muhammad, and it was as though they disliked it, and he carried him on his shoulder and brought him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take my name and do not take my kunyah."
"15028","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, Haddathana Shubah, from Abu Ishaq, that he heard Said ibn Abi Karib, or Shuayb ibn Abi Karb, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah, while upon a camel, say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"15029","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq, Akhbarana Ibn Jurayj, Akhbarani Amr ibn Dinar, that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: A man came while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was upon the minbar on Friday addressing, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Have you prayed two rakahs? And he said: No. And he said: Pray."
"15030","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, Haddathana Shubah, Haddathana Matar, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has land, let him cultivate it, and if he is unable to do it, let him grant its cultivation to his brother, otherwise let him leave it and not rent it out."
"15031","He said: And the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the mixture of unripe dates and ripe dates, and raisins and dates."
"15032","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, Haddathana Shubah, from Said ibn Ibrahim, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali, he said: Al-Hajjaj came to Madinah, and we asked Jabir ibn Abd Allah, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray the Zuhr in the midday heat, and the Asr while the sun was clear, and the Maghrib when it had set, and the Isha sometimes he delayed it and sometimes he hastened it, and when he saw them gathered he hastened, and when he saw them slow he delayed, and the Subh, he said: They were, or he said: He was, praying it in the darkness before dawn."
"15033","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq, Akhbarana Sufyan, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: Abu Madhkur freed a slave of his called Yaqub the Copt as a dubur, and that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Does he have wealth other than him? They said: No. He said: Who will buy him from me? And Nuaym ibn al-Nahham, the son-in-law of Umar ibn al-Khattab, bought him for eight hundred. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Spend it upon yourself, and if there is surplus then upon your family, and if there is surplus then upon your relatives, and if there is surplus then here and here and here."
"15034","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq, Akhbarana Sufyan, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: We used to pray the Maghrib with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then return to our dwellings, a mile away, while I could see the places where the arrows fell."
"15035","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Ubayd, Haddathana Ismail, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir, he said: It reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that a man of his companions freed a slave of his as a dubur, and he had no wealth other than him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sold the slave for eight hundred and handed it to his owners."
"15036","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq, Haddathana Mamar, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: A boy was born to a man of the Ansar, and he named him al-Qasim, and the Ansar said: By Allah, we shall never give you his kunyah. And that reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he praised the Ansar with good, then he said: Take my name and do not take my kunyah."
"15037","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq, Haddathana Mamar, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: Abu Humayd al-Ansari came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a cup in which was milk, carrying it uncovered, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Why did you not cover it, even with a stick you lay across it?"
"15038","Haddathana Said ibn Amir, he said: Shubah Akhbarana, from Mukhawwal, from Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Husayn, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he washed would pour over his head three times. He said: And a man of the Banu Hashim said: My hair is abundant. And Jabir said: The hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was more abundant than your hair and better."
"15039","Haddathana Ali ibn Asim, from Yazid, meaning Ibn Abi Ziyad, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A mudd of water suffices for wudu, and a sa for janabah. And a man said: It does not suffice me. And Jabir said: It sufficed one better than you and more abundant in hair, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"15040","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Sabiq, Haddathana Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah cursed the Jews; their fats were forbidden to them, and they ate their prices."
"15041","Haddathana Muawiyah ibn Amr, Haddathana Zaidah, from Husayn, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, Haddathana Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: While we were praying Friday with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a caravan carrying food approached. He said: And they turned to it until none remained with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except twelve men. And this verse came down: And when they see trade or amusement, they disperse to it and leave you standing."
"15042","Haddathana Muawiyah ibn Amr, Haddathana Abu Ishaq, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Between the servant and disbelief, or polytheism, is abandoning prayer."
"15043","Haddathana Muawiyah ibn Amr, Haddathana Abu Ishaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by people in a gathering drawing a sword, passing it among them unsheathed, and he said: Did I not forbid you from this? When one of you draws the sword, let him sheathe it, then let him give it to his brother."
"15044","Haddathana Muawiyah ibn Amr, Haddathana Abu Ishaq, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Akhbarani Abu al-Zubayr that he heard Jabir narrating that from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"15045","Haddathana Sulayman ibn Harb, Haddathana Hammad ibn Zayd, from al-Hajjaj al-Sawwaf, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that al-Tufayl ibn Amr al-Dawsi came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, do you want a strong fortress and protection? He said: And he said: A fortress that belonged to Daws in the Jahiliyyah. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) refused that, for what Allah the Mighty and Majestic had stored for the Ansar. And when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) emigrated to Madinah, al-Tufayl ibn Amr emigrated to him, and a man of his people emigrated with him, and they found Madinah unhealthy, and he fell ill and panicked, and he took arrowheads of his and cut his finger joints with them, and his hands bled profusely until he died. And al-Tufayl ibn Amr saw him in his sleep, and he saw him in a good state, and he saw him covering his hand. And he said to him: What did your Lord do with you? He said: He forgave me for my emigration to His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And why do I see you covering your hand? He said: It was said to me: We shall not repair of you what you corrupted. He said: And al-Tufayl recounted it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, and for his hands, so forgive."
"15046","Haddathana Abu Dawud, Haddathana Rabah al-Makki, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them to stone the jamarat with the like of the pebbles of khadhf."
"15047","Haddathana Waki, from Sufyan, from Jafar, from his father, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to stand and address, and praise Allah and extol Him with what He deserves, and say: Whoever Allah guides, none can misguide him, and whoever He misguides, none can guide him. The best of speech is the Book of Allah, and the best of guidance is the guidance of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the worst of matters are the invented ones, and every invented matter is an innovation. And when he mentioned the Hour, his cheeks reddened and his voice rose and his anger intensified, as though he were a warner of an army: It will come upon you in the morning, it will come upon you in the evening. Whoever leaves wealth, it is for the heirs, and whoever leaves helpless dependents or debt, it is upon me and to me, and I am the guardian of the believers."
"15048","Haddathana Asbat ibn Muhammad, Haddathana Abd Allah ibn al-Walid al-Wassafi, from Abd Allah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, he said: A group of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in to Jabir, and he offered them bread and vinegar, and said: Eat, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: An excellent condiment is vinegar. It is ruin for a man that a group of his brothers come in to him and he deems little what is in his house to offer them, and ruin for the people that they deem little what is offered to them."
"15049","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Bakr, Haddathana Abd al-Malik, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: When Abd Allah ibn Ubayy died, his son came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, if you do not come to him, we shall never cease being reproached for this. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him and found him already placed in his pit, and he said: Why not before you put him in? And he was taken out of his pit, and he spat upon him from his head to his foot, and clothed him in his shirt."
"15050","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Ubayd, Haddathana Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, he said: There was a man of the Banu Udhrah called Abu Madhkur, and he had a Coptic slave, and he freed him as a dubur from him, and he was needy. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is needy, let him begin with himself. He said: And he commanded him to benefit from him, and he sold him to Nuaym ibn Abd Allah al-Nahham al-Adawi for eight hundred dirhams."
"15051","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Ubayd, Haddathana Ubayd Allah ibn al-Walid, from Muharib ibn Dithar, he said: People of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in to Jabir ibn Abd Allah, and he brought near to them bread and vinegar, and said: Eat, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: An excellent condiment is vinegar."
"15052","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Ubayd, Haddathana al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: Ubayy ibn Kab fell ill with an illness, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a physician to him, and he cauterized him over his akhal."
"15053","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Ubayd, Haddathana al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us on the day of Nahr and said: Which day is greatest in sanctity? And they said: This day of ours. He said: And which month is greatest in sanctity? They said: This month of ours. He said: Which land is greatest in sanctity? They said: This land of ours. He said: Your blood and your wealth are forbidden to you like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this land of yours, in this month of yours. Have I conveyed? They said: Yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness."
"15054","Haddathana Ali ibn Bahr, Haddathana Isa ibn Yunus, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the Farewell Hajj, and he mentioned its meaning."
"15055","Haddathana Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith, Haddathana Shubah, Haddathana al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Jabir, that he said: The Banu Salimah wanted to sell their dwellings to move near the mosque, and that reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Your dwellings; your traces are but recorded."
"15056","Haddathana Husayn ibn Muhammad, Haddathana Jarir, meaning Ibn Hazim, from Ayyub, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes charge of his brother, let him make his shroud good."
"15057","Haddathana Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, Haddathani Shibl, he said: I heard Amr ibn Dinar say, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah and Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit until its soundness appears."
"15058","Haddathana Abd Allah ibn al-Walid, meaning al-Adani, Haddathana Sufyan, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: A man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which Islam is best? He said: That the Muslims be safe from your tongue and your hand. My father said:"
"15059","And Waki narrated it to us from al-Amash."
"15060","Haddathana Abd Allah ibn al-Walid, Haddathana Abd Allah ibn al-Muammal, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The water of Zamzam is for what it is drunk for."
"15061","Haddathana Azhar ibn al-Qasim al-Rasibi at Makkah and Kathir ibn Hisham, they said: Haddathana Hisham, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling palm trees until they are eaten from."
"15062","Haddathana Azhar ibn al-Qasim and Kathir ibn Hisham, they said: Haddathana Hisham, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: I fell ill while I had seven sisters, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in to me and sprinkled upon my face, and I awoke, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I bequeath two thirds for my sisters? He said: Do good. I said: Half? He said: Do good. He said: Then he went out and left me, then he returned and said: O Jabir, I do not see you dying of this ailment of yours, and Allah the Mighty and Majestic has sent down and clarified that which is for your sisters, and made two thirds for them. And Jabir used to say: This verse came down concerning me: They ask you for a ruling; say: Allah gives you a ruling concerning kalalah."
"15063","Haddathana Azhar ibn al-Qasim, Haddathana Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled with preemption as long as it is not divided or its boundaries fixed."
"15064","Haddathana Abu Said, freedman of the Banu Hashim, Haddathana Layth, Haddathana Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: A slave came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and pledged to him, and his master came and identified him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought him from him and freed him, then he would not pledge anyone after that until he asked him: Free or slave?"
"15065","Haddathana Abu Said, Haddathana Layth, Haddathana Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought a slave for two slaves."
"15066","Haddathana Hashim ibn al-Qasim, Haddathana Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Abi Salamah, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw myself entering Paradise, and behold I was with al-Rumaysa, the wife of Abu Talhah. He said: And I heard a light step before me, and I said: Who is this, O Jibril? He said: This is Bilal. He said: And I saw a white palace with a slave girl in its courtyard. He said: I said: Whose is this palace? He said: For Umar ibn al-Khattab. And I wanted to enter and look at it. He said: And I remembered your jealousy. And Umar said: For you my father and mother, O Messenger of Allah; would I be jealous with regard to you?"
"15067","Haddathana Abu Said, Haddathana Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Salamah, Haddathana Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, Haddathana Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and he mentioned its meaning. He said: And I heard a light step before me, meaning a sound."
"15068","Haddathana Abu Said, Haddathana Abu Aqil, meaning Bashir ibn Uqbah al-Dawraqi, Haddathana Abu al-Mutawakkil al-Naji, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: I travelled with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his journeys, and I think he said: As a warrior. And when we came back returning, he said: Whoever loves to hasten, let him hasten. And I was upon a reddish-grey camel, the like of which was not in the army, and I urged it on, and the people were behind me, and while I was thus, my camel stopped and would not move, and behold the voice of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And he said: What is with your camel, O Jabir? I said: O Messenger of Allah, I do not know what has come over it. He said: Hold fast, and give me the whip. And I gave him the whip, and he struck it a blow, and the camel went off with me in every direction. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me at that: O Jabir, will you sell me your camel? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Arrive at Madinah. And he arrived at Madinah and entered the mosque among groups of his companions, and I tied my camel and said: This is your camel, O Messenger of Allah. And he came out and began circling it and saying: An excellent camel is my camel. And he said: O so-and-so, go and bring me an uqiyah of gold. And he said: Give it to Jabir. And I took it, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have you received the price in full? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then the price is yours and the camel is yours, or: The camel is yours and the price is yours."
"15069","Haddathana Abu Said, Haddathana Abu Aqil, Haddathana Abu al-Mutawakkil, he said: I came to Jabir ibn Abd Allah and said: Narrate to me a hadith you witnessed from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And he said: My father died leaving twenty wasqs of dates as a debt upon him, and we had mixed assortments of dates, and the ajwah would not cover the debt upon us. And I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he sent to my creditor, and he refused but to take all the ajwah. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go and give him. And I went to a trellis of ours, I and a female companion of mine, and we cut our dates, and we had a she-goat we fed from the poor dates, and it had grown fat, when two men approached us, behold the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Umar. And I said: Welcome, O Messenger of Allah; welcome, O Umar. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Jabir, go with us that we may go round this palm grove of yours. And I said: Yes. And we went round it, and I ordered the she-goat slaughtered, then we brought a cushion, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reclined upon a cushion of hair stuffed with fibre, and as for Umar, I found no cushion for him. Then we brought a table of ours upon it moist dates and dry dates and meat, and we offered it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Umar, and they ate, and I was a man in whom shyness was deeply rooted. And when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to rise, my female companion said: O Messenger of Allah, supplications from you. He said: Yes, and may Allah bless you. He said: Yes, and may Allah bless you. Then after that I sent to my creditors, and they came with donkeys and sacks, and I had resolved to buy for them of the ajwah, to pay them the ajwah that was upon my father. And I paid them, by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, twenty wasqs of ajwah, and a good surplus remained. And I went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to gladden him with what Allah the Mighty and Majestic had granted me, and when I informed him, he said: O Allah, praise be to You; O Allah, praise be to You. And he said to Umar: Jabir has paid his creditor in full. And Umar began praising Allah."
"15070","Haddathana Abd Allah ibn al-Walid, Haddathana Sufyan, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has land, let him cultivate it or grant it to his brother."
"15071","Haddathana Hammad ibn Khalid, from Malik, from Jafar, from his father, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) trotted from the Stone to the Stone."
"15072","Haddathana Hammad al-Khayyat, Haddathana Asim ibn Umar, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever spends a day in ihram calling talbiyah until the sun sets, it sets with his sins as his mother bore him."
"15073","Haddathana Sahl ibn Yusuf, from Hajjaj, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions, when they arrived, did not add to one circumambulation."
"15074","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, Haddathana Zuhayr, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Tell me, if I strive in the path of Allah with myself and my wealth until I am killed, patient, seeking reward, advancing, not turning back, shall I enter Paradise? He said: Yes, except that you leave a debt for which you have no payment with you."
"15075","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, from Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to visit me ill, neither riding a mule nor a horse."
"15076","Haddathana Abu al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Zinad, Akhbarani Ishaq ibn Hazim, from Ibn Miqsam, he said: My father, meaning Ubayd Allah ibn Miqsam, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said concerning the sea: It is pure, its water purifying, its dead lawful."
"15077","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Abi Adi, from Sulayman, meaning al-Taymi, from Abu Nadrah, from Jabir, he said: I was travelling upon a watering camel of mine at the rear of the caravan, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck it a blow, or he said: He prodded it a prod. He said: And after that it would be at the front of the caravan, except that I held it back. He said: And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and said: Will you sell it to me for such and such, and Allah forgive you? He said: I said: It is yours, O Messenger of Allah. He said: And he increased me. He said: Will you sell it to me for such and such, and Allah forgive you? He said: I said: It is yours, O Messenger of Allah. Sulayman said: And I do not know how many times he said: Will you sell it to me for such and such? Then he said: Have you married after your father? He said: I said: Yes. He said: A virgin or a previously married woman? He said: I said: Previously married. He said: Why did you not marry her a virgin, you play with her and she plays with you, and you laugh with her and she laughs with you?"
"15078","Haddathana Kathir ibn Hisham, from Hisham, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating onion and leek, but need overcame us and we ate of it. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats of this foul-smelling tree, let him not approach our mosque, for the angels are harmed by what man is harmed by."
"15079","Haddathana Kathir ibn Hisham, Haddathana Hisham, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Close the doors at night, and extinguish the lamps, and tie the waterskins, and cover food and drink, even if you lay a stick across it."
"15080","Haddathana Kathir ibn Hisham, Haddathana Hisham, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever meets Allah the Mighty and Majestic associating nothing with Him shall enter Paradise, and whoever meets Allah associating with Him shall enter the Fire."
"15081","Haddathana Kathir, Haddathana Hisham, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hold back your wealth and do not grant it for life, for whoever is granted something for his lifetime, it is his for his lifetime and after his death."
"15082","Haddathana Kathir ibn Hisham, Haddathana Hisham ibn Abi Abd Allah, the companion of al-Dastuwai, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, he said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a day of severe heat, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with his companions and lengthened the standing until they began falling down, then he bowed and lengthened the bowing, then he raised his head and lengthened, then he bowed and lengthened the bowing, then he raised his head and lengthened, then he prostrated two prostrations, then he stood and did the like of that, then he began stepping forward, then he began stepping back, and they were four bowings and four prostrations. Then he said: Everything you are promised was shown to me; Paradise was shown to me, until had I taken a bunch from it I would have seized it, or he said: I took a bunch from it and my hand fell short of it, Hisham doubted. And the Fire was shown to me, and I began stepping back fearing it would overwhelm you. And I saw in it a Himyari black tall woman being punished for a cat of hers she had tied; she neither fed it nor gave it drink, nor let it eat of the vermin of the earth. And I saw Abu Thumamah Amr ibn Malik dragging his intestines in the Fire. And they are but two signs of the signs of Allah the Mighty and Majestic He shows you; when it eclipses, pray until it clears."
"15083","Haddathana Kathir ibn Hisham, Haddathana Hisham, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among palm trees, and he prayed the Zuhr with his companions. He said: And the polytheists plotted against them. He said: And he said: Leave them, for they have a prayer after this dearer to them than their children. He said: And Jibril came down to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with his companions, and arranged them in two rows, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before them, and they all said takbir, then those next to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated while the others stood. And when those who prostrated raised their heads, the others prostrated. And when they stood for the second rakah, those next to the first row stepped back, and the people of the second row stood, and the others advanced to the first row, and they all bowed. And when they raised their heads from bowing, those next to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated while the others stood. And when they raised their heads, the others prostrated."
"15084","Haddathana Yaqub, Haddathana my father, from Ibn Ishaq, Haddathani Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil ibn Abi Talib, he said: I came in to Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, the brother of the Banu Salimah, and with me were Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hasan ibn Ali and Abu al-Asbat, a freedman of Abd Allah ibn Jafar who pursued knowledge. He said: And we asked him about wudu from food touched by fire. And he said: I went out intending the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his mosque, and I did not find him, and I asked about him, and it was said to me: He is at al-Aswaf, with the daughters of Sad ibn al-Rabi, the brother of Balharith ibn al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj, dividing among them their inheritance from their father. He said: And they were the first women to inherit from their father in Islam. He said: And I went out until I came to al-Aswaf, and it is the property of Sad ibn al-Rabi, and I found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a stone enclosure of palm trees sprinkled for him, and he was in it. He said: And a morning meal of bread and meat made for him was brought, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate, and the people ate with him. He said: Then he urinated, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed wudu for Zuhr, and the people performed wudu with him. He said: Then he prayed Zuhr with them. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat through some of what remained of his division for them until the prayer came and he finished his affair with them. He said: And the remainder of his morning meal of bread and meat was returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ate, and the people ate with him, then he rose and prayed Asr with us, and neither he nor any of the people touched water."
"15085","Haddathana Yaqub, Haddathana my father, from Ibn Ishaq, Haddathani Bashir ibn Abi Bashir, freedman of the family of al-Zubayr, he said: I heard al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib asking Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, the brother of the Banu Salimah, about washing from janabah. And Jabir said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to scoop over his head three scoops with his hands, then pour water over his skin. He said: And al-Hasan said to him: The hair of my head is abundant, and I fear three scoops with my hands will not wash it. And Jabir said to him: The head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was more abundant and better than your head."
"15086","Haddathana Yaqub, Haddathana my father, from Ibn Ishaq, Haddathani Yazid ibn Abi Habib al-Misri, from Khalid ibn Abi Imran, from Abu Ayyash, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughtered two rams on the day of Eid, then said when he faced them: I have faced my face to Him who created the heavens and the earth, upright, a Muslim, and I am not of the polytheists. My prayer and my sacrifice and my living and my dying are for Allah, Lord of the worlds, no partner has He, and with that I am commanded, and I am the first of the Muslims. In the name of Allah, Allah is Greatest; O Allah, from You and to You, from Muhammad and his community."
"15087","Haddathana Yaqub, he said: And I heard him mention, meaning his father, from Muhammad ibn Ikrimah, from Abd Allah ibn Ikrimah, from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Rabiah, and from Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib, that they both came in to Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Sulami while he was praying wrapped, his cloak upon the wall of his mosque. And he prayed, then turned to us and said to us: I prayed only that you might see me; I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray thus."
"15088","Haddathana Yaqub, he said: I heard my father narrate from Muhammad ibn Ikrimah, Haddathani a man of Juhaynah, while we were with Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir, from his father Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever man of the people swears by this minbar of mine a false oath by which he takes the right of a Muslim, Allah the Mighty and Majestic shall enter him into the Fire, even for a green tooth-stick."
"15089","Haddathana Yaqub, Haddathana my father, from Ibn Ishaq, Haddathani Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir ibn Abd Allah, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, when the companions of Uhud were mentioned: By Allah, I would love to have been left with the companions of Nuhs al-jabal, meaning the foot of the mountain."
"15090","Haddathana Yaqub, Haddathana my father, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Haddathani Wahb ibn Kaysan, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: I went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the campaign of Dhat al-Riqa, mounted upon a weak camel of mine. And when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned back, the companies went on and I lagged behind, until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) caught up with me. And he said: What is with you, O Jabir? He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, this camel of mine has slowed me. He said: And make it kneel. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made his kneel, then he said: Give me this stick from your hand, or he said: Cut for me a stick from a tree. He said: And I did. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it and prodded it with prods, then he said: Ride. And I rode, and it went out, by Him who sent him with the truth, keeping pace with his she-camel. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conversed with me and said: Will you sell me this camel of yours, O Jabir? He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, rather I give it to you. He said: No, but sell it to me. He said: I said: Then price it for me. He said: I have said: I take it for a dirham. He said: I said: No, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wrong me. He said: Then for two dirhams. He said: I said: No. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept raising for me until he reached the uqiyah. He said: I said: Then I am content. He said: Are you content? I said: Yes. I said: It is yours. He said: I have taken it. He said: Then he said to me: O Jabir, have you married yet? He said: I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Previously married or virgin? He said: I said: Rather previously married. He said: Why not a young girl you play with and she plays with you? He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, my father was struck on the day of Uhud and left seven daughters of his, and I married a woman who gathers, gathering their heads and standing over them. He said: You did right, if Allah wills. He said: When we come to Sirar, we shall command a slaughter camel and it will be slaughtered, and we shall stay over it that day of ours, and she will hear of us and shake out her cushions. He said: I said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, we have no cushions. He said: There shall be; when you arrive, then act with prudence. He said: And when we came to Sirar, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded a slaughter camel and it was slaughtered, and we stayed over it that day. And when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered in the evening, he entered and we entered. He said: And I informed the woman of the hadith and of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me. She said: Then here you are; hearing and obedience. He said: And in the morning I took the head of the camel and came with it until I made it kneel at the door of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then I sat in the mosque near him. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and saw the camel and said: What is this? They said: O Messenger of Allah, this is a camel Jabir brought. He said: And where is Jabir? And I was called for him. He said: Come, O son of my brother, take the head of your camel, for it is yours. He said: And he called Bilal and said: Go with Jabir and give him an uqiyah. And I went with him and he gave me an uqiyah and added a little extra for me. He said: And by Allah, it kept growing with us, and we saw its place in our house, until it was struck yesterday in what struck the people, meaning the day of al-Harrah."
"15091","Haddathana Yaqub, Haddathana my father, from Ibn Ishaq, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: When we faced the valley of Hunayn, he said: We descended into a valley of the valleys of Tihamah, hollow, steep, we but descended in it descending. He said: And in the blindness of the morning, and the people had lain in wait for us in its ravines and its sides and its straits, having gathered and prepared and readied. He said: And by Allah, nothing startled us while descending but the squadrons charging upon us with the charge of one man, and the people fled back retreating, continuing on, none of them turning to another, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned aside to the right, then he said: To me, O people; come to me; I am the Messenger of Allah; I am Muhammad ibn Abd Allah. He said: And nothing availed; the camels bore some of them against others, and the people went off, except that with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained a group of the Emigrants and the Helpers and his household, not many. And among those who stood firm with him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were Abu Bakr and Umar, and of his household Ali ibn Abi Talib and al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib and his son al-Fadl ibn Abbas and Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith and Rabiah ibn al-Harith and Ayman ibn Ubayd, and he is the son of Umm Ayman, and Usamah ibn Zayd. He said: And a man of Hawazin upon a red camel of his, in his hand a black banner of his at the head of a long spear of his, before the people, and Hawazin behind him; when he caught up he thrust with his spear, and when the people escaped him he raised it for those behind him and they followed him."
"15092","Ibn Ishaq said: And Haddathani Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir, from his father Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: While that man of Hawazin, the bearer of the banner, upon that camel of his, doing what he did, Ali ibn Abi Talib swooped upon him, and a man of the Ansar, both intending him. He said: And Ali came to him from behind him and struck the hocks of the camel, and it fell upon its hindquarters, and the Ansari leapt upon the man and struck him a blow severing his foot with half his leg, and he toppled from his saddle. And the people fought hand to hand, and by Allah, the retreat of the people from their flight did not return until they found the captives bound before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"15093","Haddathana Yaqub, Haddathana my father, from Ibn Ishaq, Haddathani Said ibn Mina, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: We worked with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Trench. He said: And I had a small fat yearling she-goat. He said: And I said: By Allah, if we but made it for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And I commanded my wife, and she ground for us some barley and made for us bread of it, and slaughtered that sheep, and we roasted it for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And when we entered evening and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to leave the Trench, he said: And we worked in it by day, and when we entered evening we returned to our families. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have made for you a small sheep that was with us, and we made with it some of this barley bread, and I would love that you turn aside with me to my dwelling, and I intended only that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turn aside with me alone. He said: And when I said that to him, he said: Yes. Then he commanded a crier, and he cried: Turn aside with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to the house of Jabir. He said: I said: To Allah we belong and to Him we return. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, and the people came with him. He said: And he sat, and we brought it out to him. He said: And he blessed and named, then ate, and the people crowded to it; whenever a group finished they rose and people came, until the people of the Trench departed from it."
"15094","Haddathana Yaqub, Haddathana my father, from Ibn Ishaq, Haddathani Muadh ibn Rifah, from Mahmud ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn al-Jamuh, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: When Sad was buried, while we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said tasbih, and the people said tasbih with him for a long while, then he said takbir, and the people said takbir. Then they said: O Messenger of Allah, for what did you say tasbih? He said: The grave constricted upon this righteous man until Allah the Mighty and Majestic relieved him of it."
"15095","Haddathana Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi, Haddathana al-Amash, he said: It reached me from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you cook meat, increase the broth or the water, for it is more encompassing, or more reaching, for the neighbours."
"15096","Haddathana Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi, from Ibn Jurayj, Akhbarani Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever slave marries without the permission of his master is a fornicator."
"15097","Haddathana Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi, Akhbarana Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, that he heard Jabir, and he was asked about azl. He said: And he said: We used to do it in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"15098","Haddathana Rawh, Haddathana Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah, Haddathana Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: Revelation was withheld from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the beginning of his affair, and solitude was made beloved to him, and he began secluding himself in Hira. And while he was coming from Hira, behold I heard a sound from above me, and I raised my head, and behold the one who came to me in Hira above my head upon a chair. He said: And when I saw him, I fell to the ground, and when I awoke I came to my family hastening and said: Wrap me, wrap me. And Jibril (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and said: O you wrapped, rise and warn, and your Lord magnify, and your clothes purify, and defilement shun."
"15099","Haddathana Yaqub, Haddathana my father, from Salih, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Abu Salamah said: I heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah narrate that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Quraysh denied me when I was taken by night to Bayt al-Maqdis, I stood in al-Hijr, and Allah unveiled Bayt al-Maqdis for me, and I began informing them of its signs while looking at it."
"15100","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, he said: Al-Zuhri said: Akhbarani Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrating about the pause of revelation, and he said in his hadith: While I was walking, I heard a voice from the sky, and I raised my head, and behold the angel who came to me in Hira sitting upon a chair between the heaven and the earth. And I fell from him in terror, and I returned and said: Wrap me in garments, wrap me in garments. And they wrapped me, and Allah the Mighty and Majestic sent down: O you wrapped, rise and warn, and your Lord magnify, up to His saying: And defilement shun, before prayer was enjoined, and they are the idols."
"15101","Al-Zuhri said, and Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, from Jabir ibn Abdillah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I stood in the Hijr when my people denied me, and Bayt al-Maqdis was raised up for me until I began describing its signs to them."
"15102","Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Khalid, narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us, from Mamar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir who said: A man narrated to me, from Jabir ibn Abdillah who said: A young man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Do you permit me castration? He said: Fast, and ask Allah of His bounty."
"15103","Ibrahim narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us, from Mamar, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abdillah ibn Miqsam who said: I was with Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ali, and he asked Jabir ibn Abdillah about ghusl from janabah, and he said: Wet the hair and wash the skin. He said: My head has much hair. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pour three handfuls of water over his head. Hasan ibn Muhammad said: My head has much hair. He said: The head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had more hair and was better."
"15104","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Mamar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from Jabir ibn Abdillah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray voluntary prayers upon his mount wherever it turned with him while traveling, but when he wanted to pray the obligatory prayer he dismounted from his mount and faced the qiblah."
"15105","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah reporting about the Hajj of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: He commanded us, after we had performed tawaf, to exit ihram. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you intend to go to Mina, then enter ihram. So we entered ihram from al-Batha."
"15106","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr in Madinah as four rakahs and prayed Asr at Dhu al-Hulayfah as two rakahs, then spent the night at Dhu al-Hulayfah until morning. When he mounted his mount and it stood upright with him, he entered ihram."
"15107","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoning upon his mount on the Day of Sacrifice, saying: Take your rites from me, for I do not know, perhaps I will not perform Hajj after this Hajj of mine."
"15108","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, and Hajjaj from Ibn Jurayj, Ata informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: We used to eat of the sacrificial camels only for three days of Mina, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted us. He said: Eat and take provision. Hajjaj said: So we ate and took provision."
"15109","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, and Rawh, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: We shared with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Hajj and Umrah, every seven in a camel. So we slaughtered seventy camels on that day."
"15110","Muhammad ibn Bakr and Rawh narrated to us, both said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughtered a cow on behalf of Aishah in his Hajj."
"15111","Muhammad ibn Bakr and Rawh narrated to us, both said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah narrating about the Hajj of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us, when we exited ihram, to offer a sacrificial gift, and a group of us would share in a camel, and that was when he commanded them to exit ihram from their Hajj."
"15112","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade branding on the face and striking on the face."
"15113","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) provided us a bag of dates, and he would take a handful at a time for us, then a date at a time, and we would suck them and drink water over them until night. Then the sea cast out a dead whale, and Abu Ubaydah said: Fighters and hungry, so eat. So we ate, and we mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: A provision Allah brought out for you; if you have anything of it, feed us. We had some of it, so some of the people sent some of it to him, and he ate from it."
"15114","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Waqid al-Laythi narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to me, Jabir narrated to me, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Some people will come out of the Fire after they have been scorched in it, and they will be taken to a river in Paradise called the River of Life, and they will bathe in it and come out of it like small sprouts."
"15115","Al-Fadl ibn Dukayn and Abu Ahmad both said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People follow Quraysh in good and evil."
"15116","Waki narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People follow Quraysh in good and evil."
"15117","Abu Ahmad and Musa ibn Dawud both said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever intends to fast, let him take suhur with something. Musa said: Even with something."
"15118","Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Jafar, from his father, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he bathed from janabah, would pour three handfuls over his head. Hasan ibn Muhammad said to him: My hair is abundant. He said: O son of my brother, the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was more abundant than your hair and better."
"15119","Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Burd, from Ata, from Jabir who said: We used to go on expeditions with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we would come upon vessels and waterskins of the polytheists and use them, and it was not held against us."
"15120","Yazid narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that Abu Said al-Khudri entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying in a garment."
"15121","Yazid narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Ata, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on the day of Eid then deliver the sermon."
"15122","Yazid narrated to us, Sulayman, meaning al-Taymi, narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his Companions: There is no living soul among you over whom one hundred years will pass while it is alive on that day."
"15123","Yazid narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman, keeper of the water, from Jabir with the like of it, and Jabir explained it as a decrease of lifespan."
"15124","Yazid narrated to us, Hajjaj, meaning Ibn Abi Zaynab, informed us, saying: I heard Talhah ibn Nafi Abu Sufyan saying: I heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: I was in the shade of my house, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me. When I saw him I jumped to him and began walking behind him. He said: Come near. So I came near him, and he took my hand, and we went until he came to one of the chambers of his wives, Umm Salamah or Zaynab bint Jahsh, and he entered, then he gave me permission and I entered, with the curtain over her. He said: Do you have lunch? They said: Yes. Three loaves were brought and placed on a leather mat. He said: Do you have any condiment? They said: No, except some vinegar. He said: Bring it. They brought it to him. He took a loaf and placed it before him, and a loaf before me, and broke the third into two, placing half before him and half before me."
"15125","Yazid narrated to us, Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdillah who said: Nabidh would be made for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a waterskin; if there was no waterskin, it would be made for him in a brass stone pot."
"15126","Yazid narrated to us, Abd al-Malik informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdillah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade al-dubba, al-naqir, al-muzaffat, and al-hantam."
"15127","Yazid narrated to us, Sufyan, meaning al-Thawri, informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me for a need. I came while he was traveling on his mount, his face toward the east, gesturing. I spoke to him and he did not answer me. When he finished he said: I was praying."
"15128","Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, and Abu Amir from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ata, from Abd al-Malik ibn Jabir ibn Atik, from Jabir ibn Abdillah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man narrates a narration then turns, it is a trust. Abu Amir said: In his gathering, with a narration."
"15129","Yazid narrated to us, al-Hajjaj informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Regarding animals, two for one, there is no harm in it, hand to hand, but it is not valid on credit."
"15130","Yazid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, that Shurahbil ibn Sad informed him, from Jabir ibn Abdillah who said: We returned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from al-Hudaybiyah until we stopped at al-Suqya. Muadh ibn Jabal said: Who will draw water for us in our waterskins? Jabir said: I went out with a group of the Ansar until we came to the water at al-Uthayah, between them nearly twenty-three miles. We drew water in our waterskins until, after nightfall, there was a man whose camel struggled toward the trough. He said: Water it, and behold it was the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He watered, then I took the halter of his she-camel and made it kneel. He stood and prayed Isha, with Jabir, as mentioned, at his side, then prayed after it thirteen prostrations."
"15131","Yazid narrated to us, Sharik ibn Abdillah informed us, from Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir ibn Abdillah who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: A man will appear before you, or he said: A man will enter upon you, meaning a man of the people of Paradise. Then Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, came. Then he said: A youth will appear before you, or will enter upon you, meaning a man of the people of Paradise. Then Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, came. Then he said: A man of the people of Paradise will appear before you. O Allah, make him Ali. O Allah, make him Ali. Then Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, came."
"15132","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: A lizard was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he refused to eat it, saying: I do not know, perhaps it is from the early generations that were transformed."
"15133","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Amr ibn Dinar informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: A man came while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on the minbar on Friday delivering the sermon. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Have you prayed two rakahs? He said: No. He said: Then pray."
"15134","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Amr ibn Dinar informed me, saying: I heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: When the Kabah was being built, al-Abbas and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were carrying stones. Al-Abbas said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Put your waist-wrapper, Abd al-Razzaq said: upon your neck against the stones. He fell to the ground and his eyes turned toward the sky. He stood and said: My waist-wrapper, my waist-wrapper. He stood and tied it upon himself."
"15135","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, saying: Ata claimed to me, saying: I heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats this tree, meaning garlic, let him not come near us in our mosque."
"15136","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, saying: Abu al-Zubayr said: Jabir ibn Abdillah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no cutting off the hand of the plunderer, and whoever plunders a well-known plunder is not of us. And he said: There is no cutting off the hand of the traitor."
"15137","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah, and they mentioned the Ansari, saying: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon his mount praying voluntary prayers in every direction, but he would lower the two prostrations below the bowing, gesturing."
"15138","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ata informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah, and they mentioned coitus interruptus, and he said: We used to do it in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"15139","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, saying: Ata said, when Jabir ibn Abdillah came performing Umrah, we came to him in his house, and the people asked him about things, then they mentioned mutah to him, and he said: Yes, we practiced it in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar, until it was in the latter part of the caliphate of Umar, may Allah be pleased with him."
"15140","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, that the sun set for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Makkah, and he did not pray Maghrib until he came to Sarif."
"15141","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, who heard it from Jabir ibn Abdillah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Abdillah ibn Ubayy after he had been placed in his pit, and put him upon his knee, clothed him in his shirt, and blew upon him of his saliva."
"15142","Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr heard Jabir saying: My two ears heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A people will come out of the Fire and enter Paradise."
"15143","Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that an amir in Madinah called Tariq judged that umra belongs to the heir, upon the word of Jabir ibn Abdillah from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"15144","Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, who heard Jabir saying: We did not pledge to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) unto death; we only pledged to him not to flee."
"15145","Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, who heard Jabir saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the earnings of the cupper, and he said: Feed it to your camel."
"15146","Sufyan narrated to us, Ibn Aqil narrated to us, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate bread and meat, then prayed without performing ablution."
"15147","Hammad ibn Usamah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to me, Ubaydillah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi narrated to me, from Jabir ibn Abdillah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever revives a dead land, it belongs to him, and whatever wild animals eat of it is charity for him."
"15148","Yahya ibn Zakariya narrated to us, Hajjaj informed us, from Ata and from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling what is on the tops of palm trees for dates by measure."
"15149","And with it, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruits until their soundness appears, and selling for two or three years."
"15150","Yahya ibn Zakariya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ata and from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling what is on the tops of palm trees for measured dates."
"15151","Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Ata, from Jabir who said: I witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a day of Eid beginning with prayer before the sermon, without adhan or iqamah."
"15152","Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, from al-Muthanna, from Ata, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed a single tawaf."
"15153","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Jabir, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My brother has died, how shall I shroud him? He said: Shroud him well."
"15154","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Qays al-Yashkuri, from Jabir ibn Abdillah al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever encloses a wall around a land, it belongs to him."
"15155","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ali said: I said to Jabir ibn Abdillah, and Jabir ibn Abdillah said: O son of my brother, I am the most knowledgeable of people about this hadith. I was among those who stoned the man, meaning Maiz. When we stoned him and he felt the touch of the stones, he said: O people, return me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for my people killed me and deceived me about myself, saying the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will not kill you. They said: We did not desist from the man until we finished with him. When we returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we mentioned his words to him, and he said: Why did you not leave the man and bring him to me? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only intended to verify his matter."
"15156","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Wasiti, meaning al-Muzani, narrated to us, Abu Yusuf al-Hajjaj, meaning Ibn Abi Zaynab al-Sayqal, narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man while he was praying, having placed his left hand upon his right, so he pulled it away and placed the right upon the left."
"15157","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Jabir ibn Abdillah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you are in fertile land, give the mounts their share of grazing and do not pass beyond the stopping places; when you are in drought, hasten, and upon you is night travel, for the earth is folded at night. When ghouls appear to you, hasten with the adhan. Do not pray on the roads nor stop upon them, for they are shelter of snakes and beasts, nor relieve yourselves upon them, for they are cursed places."
"15158","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Wahid, from Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any slave who marries without permission, or he said: contracts marriage without permission of his masters, is a fornicator."
"15159","He said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The most fearful of what I fear for my ummah is the deed of the people of Lut."
"15160","Yazid narrated to us, al-Hajjaj informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding animals: Two for one, there is no harm in it, hand to hand, and there is no good in it on credit."
"15161","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdillah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever shares a crop partnership with his brother and wants to sell it, let him offer it to his partner, for he has more right to it for the price."
"15162","Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Maqburi, from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim, from Jabir ibn Abdillah who said: We used to pray Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then come to Banu Salimah while we could see the places where arrows landed."
"15163","Abu Qatan and Kathir ibn Hisham both said: Hisham narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in ihram for a sprain in his hip or back."
"15164","Abu Qatan narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a very hot day. He prayed with his Companions and prolonged the standing until they began falling, then bowed and prolonged, then rose and prolonged, then bowed and prolonged, then rose and prolonged, then prostrated two prostrations. Then he stood and did similar to that. So it was four bowings and four prostrations."
"15165","Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Asim, meaning al-Ahwal, narrated to us, from Amir, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade marrying a woman together with her paternal aunt or maternal aunt."
"15166","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted ruqyah for the sting of vermin for Banu Amr."
"15167","Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Ata, from Jabir who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a day of Eid beginning with prayer before the sermon, without adhan or iqamah."
"15168","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: A scorpion stung a man of us while we were sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). A man said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I treat him with ruqyah? He said: Whoever of you is able to benefit his brother, let him benefit him."
"15169","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no contagion, no safar, and no ghoul. And I heard Abu al-Zubayr mention that Jabir explained to them his saying no safar. Abu al-Zubayr said: Safar is the belly. It was said to Jabir: What is this saying? He said: Worms of the belly. He did not explain the ghoul. Abu al-Zubayr said, from himself: This ghoul is the female devil they speak of."
"15170","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The food of one suffices two, and the food of two suffices four, and the food of four suffices eight."
"15171","Rawh narrated to us, Husayn the teacher narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from a man, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, that a young man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking permission for castration. He said: Fast, and ask Allah Almighty of His bounty."
"15172","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: Some Jews greeted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Death be upon you, O Abu al-Qasim. He said: And upon you. Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, said, angered: Did you not hear what they said? He said: Yes, I heard, and I returned it upon them. We are answered against them, and they are not answered against us."
"15173","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wore a qaba of brocade gifted to him, then soon removed it and sent it to Umar ibn al-Khattab. It was said: You soon removed it, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Jibril, peace be upon him, forbade it to me. Umar came weeping, saying: O Messenger of Allah, you disliked something and gave it to me, what is for me? He said: I did not give it to you to wear; I only gave it to you to sell. So he sold it for two thousand dirhams."
"15174","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: He heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When a man enters his house and mentions Allah at his entrance and at his food, Satan says: There is no lodging nor supper here. When he enters and does not mention Allah at his entrance, Satan says: You have attained lodging and supper."
"15175","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Umar ibn al-Khattab on the Day of Conquest, while at al-Batha, to come to the Kabah and erase every image in it, and he did not enter the House until every image in it had been erased."
"15176","Rawh narrated to us, Zakariya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw in a dream that my head was cut off and rolling, and I was following it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is from Satan. When one of you sees a dream he dislikes, let him not narrate it to anyone, and let him seek refuge with Allah from Satan."
"15177","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People follow Quraysh in good and evil."
"15178","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The best of people in ignorance are the best of them in Islam when they understand."
"15179","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Ghifar, may Allah forgive it, and Aslam, may Allah grant it peace."
"15180","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I hope those who follow me of my ummah on the Day of Resurrection will be a quarter of the people of Paradise. We said takbir. He said: I hope they will be a third of the people of Paradise. We said takbir. He said: I hope you will be half."
"15181","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah asking about the coming to the water. He said: We, on the Day of Resurrection, will be upon such and such; see which of that is above the people. He said: The nations will be called with their idols and what they used to worship, the first then the first. Then our Lord will come to us after that and say: Whom are you waiting for? They will say: We are waiting for our Lord Almighty. He will say: I am your Lord. They will say: Until we look at You. He will manifest Himself to them, laughing. Jabir said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: He will go with them and they will follow Him, and every person, hypocrite or believer, will be given a light. Then they will follow Him upon the bridge of Hell, with hooks and thorns seizing whom Allah wills. Then the light of the hypocrite will be extinguished, then the believers will be saved. The first group will be saved, their faces like the moon on the night of full moon, seventy thousand not taken to account, then those after them like the brightest star in the sky, then likewise, until intercession becomes permissible, until whoever said there is no god but Allah and had in his heart good weighing a barley grain will come out of the Fire. They will be placed in the courtyard of the people of Paradise, and the people of Paradise will sprinkle water over them until they grow as a thing grows in the flood. Then he will ask until the world and ten likes of it with it will be given to him."
"15182","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: For every prophet there is a supplication he has made for his ummah, and I have hidden my supplication as intercession for my ummah on the Day of Resurrection, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"15183","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The people of Paradise eat therein and drink, and do not blow their noses, defecate, or urinate; their food becomes belching, and they are inspired with glorification and praise as they are inspired with breath."
"15184","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: Satan has despaired of being worshipped by the Muslims, but in stirring discord among them."
"15185","Rawh narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The throne of Iblis is upon the sea, then he sends his troops and they tempt people; the greatest of them in his sight is the greatest in temptation."
"15186","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah, and he did not raise it: I am your forerunner before you; if you do not find me, I am at the Hawd. The Hawd is as between Aylah to Makkah. Men and women will come and will not taste anything of it. Mawquf, and he did not raise it."
"15187","Rawh narrated to us, Zakariya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am at the Hawd watching who comes to me. Some people will be taken away from me, and I will say: O Lord, from me and from my ummah. It will be said: Do you know what they did after you? They did not cease after you turning back upon their heels. Jabir said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hawd is a month's journey, its corners equal, meaning its width like its length, its vessels like the stars of the sky, sweeter in scent than musk and whiter than milk. Whoever drinks of it will never thirst after it."
"15188","Rawh narrated to us, Zakariya narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade nabidh of the jar, muzaffat, dubba, and naqir."
"15189","And when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not find anything to make nabidh in for him, it would be made for him in a stone pot."
"15190","Rawh narrated to us, Zakariya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to clean ourselves with a bone or dung."
"15191","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Shurahbil ibn Sad, from Jabir ibn Abdillah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For one of you to withhold his hand from pebbles is better for him than to have one hundred she-camels all black-eyed. If Satan overcomes one of you, let him wipe a single wiping."
"15192","Hajjaj narrated to us, saying: Ibn Jurayj said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah claim that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade images in the house and forbade a man to make that."
"15193","Hajjaj narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I am only a human, and I have stipulated upon my Lord Almighty: any servant of the Muslims whom I curse or revile, that it be for him purification and reward."
"15194","Hajjaj narrated to me, Ibn Jurayj said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A group of my ummah will continue fighting upon truth, victorious until the Day of Resurrection. Then Isa ibn Maryam, peace be upon him, will descend, and their leader will say: Come, pray with us. He will say: No, some of you are leaders over others, as an honor of Allah Almighty to this ummah."
"15195","Hajjaj narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying, a month before he died: You ask me about the Hour; its knowledge is only with Allah. I swear by Allah, there is no living soul upon the earth today over whom one hundred years will pass."
"15196","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Said, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, Jabir ibn Abdillah narrated to me, saying: A man of the Muhajirun kicked a man of the Ansar. The Ansari said: O Ansar! The Muhajir said: O Muhajirun! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is with the call of ignorance? Leave the kick, for it is foul."
"15197","Ziyad ibn Abdillah ibn al-Tufayl narrated to us, Abdillah said: And I heard my father once saying: Ziyad ibn Abdillah ibn al-Tufayl al-Bakkai al-Amiri narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Salim, from Jabir ibn Abdillah who said: A boy was born to a man of us and he named him Muhammad. We said: We will not let you name him Muhammad with the name of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The man brought his son to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, a boy was born to me and I named him with your name, but my people refused to let me. He said: Yes, name yourselves with my name, but do not take my kunyah, for I am Qasim, I distribute among you."
"15198","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mutarrif informed us, from Asim ibn Ubaydillah ibn Asim ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab who said: I entered upon Jabir ibn Abdillah, and prayer came while some garments of his were upon the bed or rack. He stood wrapped in his garment, then prayed, then said to them when he finished: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray like this."
"15199","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, al-Fudayl, meaning Ibn Sulayman, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Yahya narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Abi Yazid, from Jabir ibn Abdillah al-Ansari, that some people came to Madinah with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while it had sickness, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade them to leave until he permitted them. They left without his permission. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Madinah is like the bellows, it expels filth as the bellows expels the filth of iron."
"15200","Hasan ibn Musa and Affan both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qays ibn Sad, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I slaughtered before stoning. He said: Stone, and no harm. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I shaved before slaughtering. He said: Slaughter, and no harm."
"15201","Ya'qub narrated to us: My father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Abdullah ibn Sahl ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl, the brother of Banu Haritha, narrated to me from Jabir ibn Abdullah al-Ansari, he said: Marhab the Jew came out from their fortress having gathered his weapons, chanting rajaz and saying: Khaybar knows that I am Marhab, fully armed, a tried hero, I stab at times and at times I strike, when the lions come forward blazing, my protection is a sanctuary not to be approached. And he was saying: Who is for single combat? So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Who is for this man? So Muhammad ibn Maslama said: I am for him, O Messenger of Allah, and I, by Allah, am the one wronged and seeking revenge, they killed my brother yesterday. He said: So stand to him, O Allah, help him against him. So when each of them drew near his fellow, there came between them an old umriyya tree of the ushar trees, and each of them began to take shelter by it from his fellow; whenever he took shelter by it from him, he cut off with his sword what was below him, until each of them emerged plainly to his fellow and it became between them like a standing man with no branches in it. Then Marhab charged upon Muhammad and struck him, so he shielded himself with the leather shield, and his sword fell into it and it gripped it and held it, and Muhammad ibn Maslama struck him until he killed him."
"15202","Hasan ibn Musa and Surayj narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us from Amr ibn Dinar from Muhammad ibn Ali from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the flesh of donkeys; Surayj said: the domestic ones, on the day of Khaybar; and he permitted the flesh of horses."
"15203","Hasan narrated to us: Zuhayr ibn Muawiya Abu Khaythama narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Hold on to your properties and do not divide them, for whoever grants a life-grant of umra, it belongs to the one to whom it was granted, alive and dead, and to his descendants; do not divide them."
"15204","Hasan narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not send out your grazing livestock and your children when the sun has set until the darkness of the evening meal has gone, for the devils roam about when the sun has set until the darkness of the evening meal has gone."
"15205","Hashim and Hasan narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray in a single garment wrapped around himself. So some of the people said to Abu al-Zubayr, while I was listening: The prescribed prayer? He said: The prescribed and other than the prescribed."
"15206","Hasan ibn Musa and Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, they said: Zuhayr narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: We ate with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the meat of the sacrificial animals, and we took provisions until we reached Medina with it."
"15207","Hasan narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir that a man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I have a slave girl, and she is our servant and our caretaker; I go to her, and I dislike that she should conceive. So he said: Practice withdrawal from her if you wish, for there shall come to her what was decreed for her. He said: So the man remained, then he came to him and said: The slave girl has become pregnant. He said: I already told you that there shall come to her what was decreed for her."
"15208","Hasan narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let no town-dweller sell for a Bedouin; leave people, Allah provides for some of them through others."
"15209","Musa ibn Dawud narrated it to us: Zuhayr narrated to us the like of it with its isnad."
"15210","Hasan narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir and Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the naqir, the muzaffat, and the dubba."
"15211","Hasan narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: Sa'd ibn Muadh was struck in his medial arm vein, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cauterized him with his hand with a mishqas. He said: Then it swelled, so he cauterized him a second time."
"15212","Hasan narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Close the doors, tie the mouths of the waterskins, cover the vessels, and extinguish the lamps, for Satan does not open a lock, nor untie a knot, nor uncover a vessel; and the little mouse sets fire to the household."
"15213","Muawiya, that is Ibn Amr, narrated to us: Abu Ishaq, that is al-Fazari, narrated to us from al-A'mash from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no Muslim man or Muslim woman, nor believing man or believing woman, who falls ill with an illness, except that Allah removes thereby some of his sins."
"15214","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us: Bakr ibn Sawada narrated to us that a freedman of Jabir ibn Abdullah informed him from Jabir ibn Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by them while they were picking arak fruit, so a man gave him some picked arak, and he said: Had I been in ablution, I would have eaten it."
"15215","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: I asked Jabir about the price of the dog and the cat, so he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, rebuke that."
"15216","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us: Jabir informed me that a woman from Banu Makhzum stole, so she sought refuge with Usama ibn Zayd, the beloved of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and she was brought to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: Had she been Fatima, I would have cut off her hand; so he cut it off."
"15217","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: I asked Jabir about a man who divorces his wife while she is menstruating, so he said: Abdullah ibn Umar divorced his wife while she was menstruating, so Umar came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him of that, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let him take her back, for she is his wife."
"15218","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: I asked Jabir: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stone? So he said: Yes, he stoned a man from Aslam, and a man from the Jews, and a woman; and he said to the Jew: We judge against you today."
"15219","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us from Jabir that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, rebuked a woman joining anything to her head."
"15220","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us from Jabir that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade a man to eat with his left hand, for Satan eats with his left hand."
"15221","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us from Jabir that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The likeness of the believer is like the ear of grain, it stands straight at times and falls down at times; and the likeness of the disbeliever is like the arz tree, it remains standing straight until it falls down without perceiving."
"15222","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: I asked Jabir: How many times did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, circuit between al-Safa and al-Marwa? So he said: One time."
"15223","Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us: Mujalid informed us from al-Sha'bi from Jabir ibn Abdullah that Umar ibn al-Khattab came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with a book he had obtained from some of the People of the Book, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, read it and became angry, and said: Are you bewildered about it, O son of al-Khattab? By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, I have brought it to you white and pure; do not ask them about anything, lest they inform you of a truth and you deny it, or of a falsehood and you believe it. By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, had Musa, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, been alive, he would have had no recourse but to follow me."
"15224","Abu Salama al-Khuza'i narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us from Ammar al-Duhni from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered Mecca on the day of the Conquest wearing a black turban."
"15225","Al-Khuza'i narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz narrated to us from Amr ibn Abi Amr from a man of the Ansar from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Eat the meat of game while you are in pilgrim sanctity, so long as you did not hunt it nor it was hunted for you."
"15226","Al-Khuza'i narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salama informed us: Abu al-Zubayr informed us from Jabir that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade at the time of Khaybar onions and leeks, then some people ate them and came to the mosque, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Did I not forbid these two foul-smelling trees? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, but hunger exhausted us. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever eats them, let him not attend our mosque, for the angels are harmed by what the sons of Adam are harmed by."
"15227","Abu Sa'id, the freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Mawal narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, he said: I entered upon Jabir ibn Abdullah while he was praying wrapped in a single garment with his cloak laid aside, so we said to him: You pray in a single garment while your cloak is laid aside? He said: So that one like you may enter upon me and see me praying in a single garment; I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying thus."
"15228","Abu Sa'id narrated to us: Za'ida narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to us from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best of the rows of men is the foremost, and the worst of them is the rearmost; and the best of the rows of women is the rearmost, and the worst of them is the foremost. O assembly of women, when the men prostrate, lower your gazes; do not see the private parts of the men because of the tightness of the waist-wrappers."
"15229","Abu Sa'id narrated to us: Za'ida narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: I walked with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to a woman of the Ansar, so she slaughtered a sheep for us, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A man of the people of Paradise shall enter; so Abu Bakr entered. Then he said: A man of the people of Paradise shall enter; so Umar entered. Then he said: A man of the people of Paradise shall enter; so he said: O Allah, if You will, make him Ali; so Ali entered. Then we were brought food and we ate, then we stood for the noon prayer, and none of us performed ablution. Then we were brought the remainder of the food, then we stood for the afternoon prayer, and none of us touched water."
"15230","Mu'ammal narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: We went out with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raising the pilgrimage call, then we came to Mecca and circumambulated the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwa, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Dissolve your pilgrim state and make it an umra, except whoever drove the sacrificial animal. He said: So the censers spread their fragrance and women became lawful. Then when it was the day of al-Tarwiya, we entered pilgrim sanctity for the Hajj. He said: Suraqa ibn Malik ibn Ju'shum said: O Messenger of Allah, is this umra of ours for this year of ours or forever? He said: No, rather forever."
"15231","Mu'ammal narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If I live, Allah willing, I shall forbid naming Baraka and Yasar."
"15232","Mu'ammal narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Ali, that is Ibn Zayd, narrated to us from Abu Nadra from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Ibn Sa'id: What do you see? He said: I see a throne upon the water, or he said: upon the sea, with snakes around it. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: That is the throne of Iblis."
"15233","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Hammad, that is Ibn Zayd, narrated to us from Kathir ibn Shinzhir from Ata ibn Abi Rabah from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me on an errand, then when I returned I greeted him and he did not return the greeting upon me; then when he finished, I said: O Messenger of Allah, I greeted you and you did not return it upon me. He said: I was praying, and he was upon his mount facing other than the qibla."
"15234","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us from Kathir ibn Shinzhir from Ata from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Cover the vessels, tie the mouths of the waterskins, shut the door, and extinguish the lamps at bedtime, for the little mouse may drag the wick and burn the house; and withhold your children in the evening, for the jinn spread out and snatch."
"15235","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us: Malik informed us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade eating the meat of the sacrificial animals after three days, then he said after that: Eat, take provisions, and store."
"15236","Ishaq narrated to us: Malik informed me from Ja'far from his father from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, run from the Black Stone until he ended at it, three circuits."
"15237","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik; and Ishaq narrated to us: Malik informed us from Ja'far ibn Muhammad from his father that Jabir ibn Abdullah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he came out of the mosque heading for al-Safa, saying: We begin with what Allah, Almighty and Majestic, began with."
"15238","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik; and Ishaq narrated to us: Malik informed us from Ja'far from his father from Jabir ibn Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he stood upon al-Safa, would declare Allah great three times and say: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things capable. And in the hadith of Abd al-Rahman: He does that three times, and supplicates, and does the like of that upon al-Marwa."
"15239","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik; and Ishaq narrated to us: Malik informed us from Ja'far from his father from Jabir ibn Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he descended from al-Safa, would walk until, when his feet poured down into the belly of the valley, he would hasten until he came out of it."
"15240","Ishaq narrated to us: Malik informed us from Ja'far from his father from Jabir ibn Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, slaughtered some of his sacrificial animals with his hand, and others were slaughtered by another."
"15241","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us from al-A'mash and Mansur from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I have a slave girl and I practice withdrawal from her. So he said to him: What is decreed shall be. It was not long before she became pregnant, so he came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Prophet of Allah, did you not see that she became pregnant? So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What Allah has decreed for a soul to come forth, it shall surely be."
"15242","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me on an errand, so I came while he was praying toward the east, gesturing upon his mount; the prostration lower than the bowing. So I greeted him and he did not return it upon me. He said: Then when he finished his prayer, he said: What did you do about such-and-such errand? I was praying."
"15243","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us; and Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Hold on to your properties and do not give them to anyone; so whoever is granted something as a life-grant, it is his."
"15244","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade dates and raisins, and fresh ripe dates and unripe dates, that is, that they be steeped together."
"15245","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us from al-A'mash from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you prostrates, let him be balanced, and let him not spread his forearms as the dog spreads them."
"15246","He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever among you fears not to wake at the end of the night, let him perform the witr at the beginning of the night, then let him sleep; and whoever among you hopes to wake at the end of the night, let him perform the witr at the end of the night, for the recitation at the end of the night is witnessed, and that is better."
"15247","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us from al-A'mash from Abu Sufyan from Jabir from al-Sulayk, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you comes to the Friday prayer while the imam is preaching, let him pray two light rak'as."
"15248","Surayj narrated to us: Hammad, that is Ibn Zayd, narrated to us from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah from Ata from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: We came with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and circumambulated the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwa; then when it was the day of sacrifice, we did not approach al-Safa and al-Marwa."
"15249","Surayj narrated to us: Hammad, that is Ibn Zayd, narrated to us from Amr from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade; so that was mentioned to Ibn Umar, and a man said: I saw the son of Jabir seeking a sharecropping land. So Ibn Umar said: Look at this one; his father narrates from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he forbade leasing land, while he seeks a land to sharecrop."
"15250","Surayj narrated to us: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us from Musa ibn Uqba from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Between a man and shirk or disbelief is the abandonment of prayer."
"15251","And I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Let no woman touch a woman in a single garment, nor let a man touch a man in a single garment. He said: So we said to Jabir: Did you count sins as shirk? He said: Allah forbid."
"15252","And I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Let no woman touch a woman in a single garment, nor let a man touch a man in a single garment. He said: So we said to Jabir: Did you count sins as shirk? He said: Allah forbid."
"15253","Surayj narrated to us: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us from Amr ibn Abi Amr: A trustworthy man of Banu Salima informed me from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The meat of game is lawful for the one in pilgrim sanctity, so long as he did not hunt it nor it was hunted for him."
"15254","Surayj narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us from Abu Bashir from Abu Sufyan from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon some of his family and said: Have you any condiment? So they said: No, except some vinegar. So he said: Bring it; and he began to dip with it, saying: Excellent is the condiment, vinegar."
"15255","Surayj narrated to us: Hushaym informed us: Ali ibn Zayd informed us from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What is between my pulpit and my chamber is a meadow of the meadows of Paradise, and my pulpit is upon a stream of the streams of Paradise."
"15256","Surayj narrated to us: Muhammad, that is Ibn Rashid, narrated to us from Sulayman ibn Musa from Ata from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: We used to obtain with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, among our spoils from the polytheists, waterskins and vessels, and he would divide them, though all of them were from dead animals."
"15257","Surayj narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz, that is Ibn Abi Salama, narrated to us from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I was shown that I entered Paradise, and there I was with al-Rumaysa, the wife of Abu Talha; and I heard a movement before me. I said: Who is this, O Jibril? He said: This is Bilal. He said: And I saw a white palace with a slave girl in its courtyard, so I said: Whose is this palace? She said: This belongs to Umar ibn al-Khattab. So I wanted to enter it to look at it, but I remembered your jealousy. So Umar said: With my father and my mother, O Messenger of Allah, would I be jealous toward you?"
"15258","Surayj narrated to us: Abu Awana narrated to us from Abu Bishr from Sulayman ibn Qays from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fought Muharib ibn Khasafa, then a man of them called Ghawrath ibn al-Harith came until he stood over the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with the sword, and said: Who prevents you from me? He said: Allah, Almighty and Majestic. So the sword fell from his hand, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took it and said: Who prevents you from me? He said: Be as the best of takers. He said: Do you testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah? He said: No, but I covenant with you that I shall not fight you nor be with a people who fight you. So he let him go. Then he came to his people and said: I have come to you from the best of people. Then when the prayer came, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed the prayer of fear: the people were two groups, a group facing the enemy and a group who prayed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So he prayed with the group who were with him two rak'as, and they left and took the place of those who were facing their enemy, and those who were facing their enemy left and prayed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, two rak'as. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had four rak'as, and the people had two rak'as each."
"15259","Surayj, that is Ibn al-Nu'man, narrated to us: Abu Awana narrated to us from Abu Bishr from Abu Sufyan from Jabir ibn Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, asked his family for condiment. They said: We have nothing but vinegar. He said: So he called for it and began to eat with it, saying: Excellent is the condiment, vinegar; excellent is the condiment, vinegar."
"15260","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Isra'il informed us from Uthman, that is Ibn al-Mughira, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to present himself to the people at the standing place, saying: Is there a man to carry me to his people? For Quraysh have prevented me from conveying the speech of my Lord, Almighty and Majestic. So a man from Hamdan came to him, and he said: From whom are you? So the man said: From Hamdan. He said: Is there protection among your people? He said: Yes. Then the man feared that his people would deem him insignificant, so he came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I shall go to them and inform them, then come to you next year. He said: Yes. So he left, and the delegation of the Ansar came in Rajab."
"15261","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us: Shu'ba narrated to us from Muharib ibn Dithar, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah al-Ansari, he said: I married, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: What did you marry? He said: I said: I married a matron. So he said: What is with you and virgins and their play?"
"15262","Shu'ba said: So I mentioned that to Amr ibn Dinar, so he said: I heard Jabir say: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Why not a young virgin whom you play with and who plays with you?"
"15263","Aswad ibn Amir, that is Shadhan, narrated to us both of them to the same meaning."
"15264","Hashim narrated to us: Shu'ba narrated to us from al-Jurayri from Abu Nadra, he said: Jabir ibn Abdullah said: We wanted to sell our houses and move near the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for the sake of prayer. He said: So I mentioned that to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: O so-and-so, to a man of the Ansar: Your dwellings, for your footsteps are recorded."
"15265","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Sa'id ibn Abi Karb from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw on the foot of a man among us a spot like a dirham that he had not washed, so he said: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"15266","Aswad narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us from Salama ibn Kuhayl from Ata from Jabir that a man granted freedom to a slave of his after his death while owing a debt, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sold him for the debt of his master."
"15267","Al-Nadr ibn Isma'il al-Qass, and he is Abu al-Mughira, narrated to us: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let none of you die except while thinking well of Allah, for some people were destroyed by their evil opinion of Allah, Almighty and Majestic: That is your opinion which you held of your Lord; it destroyed you, so you became among the losers."
"15268","Abu Muawiya narrated to us from al-A'mash from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Some people of tawhid shall be punished in the Fire until they become charred therein, then mercy shall reach them, so they shall be brought out and cast at the gate of Paradise, and the people of Paradise shall sprinkle water upon them, and they shall sprout as scum sprouts in the debris of the flood, then they shall enter Paradise."
"15269","Abu Muawiya narrated to us from al-A'mash from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, any believer whom I insulted or cursed or flogged, make it for him a purification and a reward."
"15270","Abu Muawiya narrated to us from al-A'mash from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, what are the two that necessitate? He said: Whoever dies not associating anything with Allah, Almighty and Majestic, shall enter Paradise; and whoever dies associating with Allah shall enter the Fire."
"15271","Abu Muawiya narrated to us from al-A'mash from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever plants a planting and a human or a bird or a beast or an animal eats from it, it is charity for him."
"15272","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Al-A'mash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, what are the two that necessitate? Then he mentioned the hadith."
"15273","Affan narrated to us: Abu Awana narrated to us from al-Aswad ibn Qays from Nubayh al-Anazi from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let none of you come to his family by night unexpectedly."
"15274","Affan narrated to us: Salim ibn Hayyan narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Mina narrated to us from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade muzabana, muhaqala, and mukhabara."
"15275","Affan narrated to us: Salim ibn Hayyan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: I saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying in a single garment, having crossed its two ends."
"15276","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: My father was killed on the day of Uhud, leaving two gardens, while dates were owed to a Jew upon him, and the dates of the Jew would absorb all that was in the two gardens. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Would you take some this year and defer some to next year? But he refused. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the harvest comes, inform me. He said: So I informed him, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came with Abu Bakr and Umar, and we began to harvest and it was measured out to him from beneath the palms, while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, supplicated for blessing, until we fulfilled to him all his right from the smaller of the two gardens, in Ammar's reckoning. Then we brought them fresh dates and water, and they ate and drank. Then he said: This is of the bliss about which you shall be asked."
"15277","Rawh narrated to us: Al-Thawri narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, poured forth with tranquility upon him, and he ordered them with tranquility, and he ordered them to throw with the like of the pebbles of khadhf, and he hastened in the valley of Muhassir."
"15278","Rawh narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: And I do not know with how many he stoned the jamra."
"15279","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Abu Bakr narrated to us from Ajlah from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to A'isha: Have you escorted the slave girl to her house? She said: Yes. He said: Why did you not send with them one to sing to them, saying: We came to you, we came to you, so greet us, we greet you; for the Ansar are a people in whom is amorous playfulness."
"15280","Al-Nadr ibn Isma'il Abu al-Mughira narrated to us: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, which prayer is best? He said: Lengthy standing. He said: O Messenger of Allah, and which jihad is best? He said: One whose horse is hamstrung and whose blood is shed. He said: O Messenger of Allah, and which emigration is best? He said: One who abandons what Allah, Almighty and Majestic, dislikes. He said: O Messenger of Allah, then which Muslims are best? He said: One from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. He said: O Messenger of Allah, then what are the two that necessitate? He said: Whoever dies not associating anything with Allah shall enter Paradise, and whoever dies associating anything with Allah shall enter the Fire."
"15281","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us: Abd al-Malik narrated to us from Ata from Jabir ibn Abdullah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever has land, let him cultivate it; and if he cannot cultivate it and is incapable of it, let him grant it to his Muslim brother, and let him not rent it out."
"15282","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us from Qatada from Ata ibn Abi Rabah from Jabir ibn Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The life-grant of umra is permissible for its people, or an inheritance for its people."
"15283","Affan narrated to us: Salim ibn Hayyan narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Mina narrated to us from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: My likeness and your likeness is like a man who kindled a fire, and moths and locusts began to fall into it while he wards them from it; and I am holding you by your waist-wrappers from the Fire, while you slip from my hand."
"15284","Affan narrated to us: Aban al-Attar narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, he said: I asked Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman: Which of the Quran was revealed first? He said: O you enveloped. He said: For I was told that the first sura revealed was: Read in the name of your Lord who created. Jabir said: I only narrate to you as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrated to us. He said: I stayed in seclusion in Hira, then when I finished my seclusion I descended and went into the valley, then I was called. So I looked before me and behind me and on my right and on my left, and I saw nothing. Then I was called again, so I looked before me and behind me and on my right and on my left, and I saw nothing. Then I looked above me, and there I was with him sitting upon a throne between the heaven and the earth, so I was terrified of him. Then I came to the house of Khadija and said: Wrap me, and pour cold water upon me. He said: Then there was revealed upon me: O you enveloped, arise and warn, and your Lord magnify."
"15285","Abu Sa'd al-Saghani Muhammad ibn Muyassar narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade muhaqala, muzabana, and mukhabara, and that fruit be sold until it becomes edible, except for dinars or dirhams, except the araya."
"15286","Abu Sa'd al-San'ani narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever buys food, let him not sell it until he takes full possession of it."
"15287","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us from Ibn al-Munkadir from Jabir, he said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and pledged to him upon Islam. Then he came the next day feverish and said: O Messenger of Allah, release me. But he refused. Then he came to him three consecutive days, each time saying: O Messenger of Allah, release me, while the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, refused. Then when he turned away, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Medina is like the bellows; it expels its impurity and purifies its good."
"15288","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The disbeliever eats in seven intestines, and the believer eats in one intestine."
"15289","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you is invited, let him respond; then if he wishes, let him eat, and if he wishes, let him leave."
"15290","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Al-Hasan, that is Ibn Salih, narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let no town-dweller sell for a Bedouin; leave people, Allah provides for some of them through others."
"15291","Husayn narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us from al-Ash'ath, that is Ibn Sawwar, from al-Hasan from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: After this year of ours, no polytheist shall enter this mosque of ours, except the people of the covenant and their servants."
"15292","Husayn narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us from al-Mughira from Amir from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, bought from me a camel on condition that he lend me its back for that journey of his or mine; then he gave me the camel and the price."
"15293","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Sufyan, that is Ibn Uyayna, narrated to us from Amr, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in an expedition; they think it was the expedition of Banu al-Mustaliq. Then a man of the Emigrants kicked a man of the Ansar, so the Ansari said: O Ansar, and the Emigrant said: O Emigrants. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, heard that and said: What is with the call of ignorance? So it was said: A man of the Emigrants kicked a man of the Ansar. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Leave it, for it is foul. Jabir said: And the Emigrants, when they came to Medina, were fewer than the Ansar; then the Emigrants increased. So that reached Abdullah ibn Ubayy, so he said: They have done it; by Allah, if we return to Medina, the mightiest shall surely expel the humblest from it. So Umar heard that and came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, let me strike the neck of this hypocrite. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Umar, leave him, lest people say that Muhammad kills his companions."
"15294","Husayn narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered licking the fingers and the bowl, and said: None of you knows in which of that the blessing lies."
"15295","Husayn narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to us from Zayd ibn Aslam from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever frightens the people of Medina has frightened what is between my sides."
"15296","Husayn narrated to us: Yazid ibn Ata narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Sa'id ibn Abi Karb and Abdullah ibn Marthad from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"15297","Husayn narrated to us: Abu Uways narrated to us: Shurahbil ibn Sa'd al-Ansari, the freedman of Banu Khatma, narrated to us from Jabir ibn Abdullah from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: For one of you to hold his hand from the pebbles is better for him than a hundred she-camels, all of them black-eyed; and if Satan overcomes one of you, let him wipe a single wiping."
"15298","Husayn narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us from Shurahbil from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: For one of you to hold his hand from the pebbles; then he mentioned the like of it."
"15299","Husayn narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir from Jabir ibn Abdullah that a man freed a slave of his, having no other than him, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, returned him upon him, and Nu'aym ibn al-Nahham bought him from him."
"15300","Husayn narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us from a man of Banu Salima from Jabir ibn Abdullah that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to the mosque, that is of the Confederates, and laid down his cloak and stood and raised his hands extended, supplicating against them, and he did not pray. He said: Then he came and supplicated against them and prayed."
"15301","Haddathana Hasan al-Ashyab, haddathana Shayban, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, that Jabir ibn Abd Allah informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled concerning the umra gift that it belongs to the one to whom it was given."
"15302","Haddathana Hasan, haddathana Ibn Lahi'ah, haddathana Abu al-Zubayr: I asked Jabir about tawaf of the Ka'bah, and he said: We used to circumambulate and touch the Corner at the beginning and at the end, and we would not circumambulate after the dawn prayer until the sun rose, nor after Asr until it set. And he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The sun rises upon the two horns of Satan."
"15303","Haddathana Hasan, haddathana Ibn Lahi'ah, Abu al-Zubayr informed us, he said: And Jabir informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The likeness of Madinah is like the bellows, and Ibrahim declared Makkah sacred, and I declare Madinah sacred, and it is like Makkah, sacred, what is between its two lava tracts, and its whole precinct: no tree shall be cut from it except that a man may feed from it, and the plague shall not approach it, Allah willing, nor the Dajjal, and the angels guard it at its passes and gates."
"15304","He said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: And it is not lawful for anyone to carry arms in it for fighting."
"15305","Haddathana Hasan and Musa ibn Dawud, they said: Haddathana Ibn Lahi'ah, haddathana Abu al-Zubayr, he said: I asked Jabir about ruqyah, and he said: My maternal uncle, one of the Ansar, informed me that he said: O Messenger of Allah, may I perform ruqyah for the scorpion sting? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever among you is able to benefit his brother by something, let him do so."
"15306","Haddathana Hasan, haddathana Ibn Lahi'ah, haddathana Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that Amr ibn Hazm was called for a woman in Madinah whom a snake had bitten, to perform ruqyah for her, and he refused, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed of that, so he called him, and Amr said: O Messenger of Allah, you forbid ruqas. He said: Recite it to me. So he recited it to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no harm; they are only covenants, so perform ruqyah with it."
"15307","Haddathana Hasan, haddathana Ibn Lahi'ah, haddathana Abu al-Zubayr, Jabir related to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: None of you will be admitted to Paradise by his deeds, nor will his deeds save him from the Fire. It was said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even I, except by the mercy of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"15308","Haddathana Hasan, haddathana Ibn Lahi'ah, haddathana Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you eats and his morsel falls, let him remove what he doubts from it, then let him eat it and not leave it for Satan, and let none of you wipe his hand with a cloth until he licks his hand, for a man does not know in which part of his food blessing is placed for him, for Satan lies in wait for the son of Adam at everything, even at his food."
"15309","Haddathana Hasan, haddathana Ibn Lahi'ah, haddathana Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Avoid the major sins, and be upright, and receive glad tidings."
"15310","Haddathana Hasan, haddathana Ibn Lahi'ah, haddathana Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid estimation of crops, and he said: Tell me, if the dates perish, would one of you like to consume the wealth of his brother falsely?"
"15311","Haddathana Hasan, haddathana Ibn Lahi'ah, haddathana Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The servant is with whom he loves."
"15312","Haddathana Ishaq ibn Isa, haddathana Sharik, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been commanded to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah; when they say it, they protect from me their blood and their wealth except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"15313","Haddathana Musa ibn Dawud, haddathana Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ata, from the two sons of Jabir, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the one spoken to sees the speaker glancing around, then it is a trust."
"15314","Haddathana Musa ibn Dawud, haddathana Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Ja'far, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ramal for three circuits from the Stone to the Stone, and prayed two rak'ahs, then returned to the Stone, then went to Zamzam and drank from it and poured over his head, then returned and touched the Corner, then returned to al-Safa and said: Begin with what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, began with."
"15315","Haddathana Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna and Yunus, they said: Haddathana al-Layth ibn Sa'd, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: We came with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entering ihram for Hajj alone, and Aishah came entering ihram for Umrah, until when she was at Sarif she menstruated; then when we arrived we circumambulated the Ka'bah and al-Safa and al-Marwah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded those of us who had no sacrificial animal to exit ihram. He said: So we said: What kind of exiting? He said: Complete exiting. So we had relations with women and perfumed ourselves, and between us and Arafah there were only four nights; then we entered ihram on the day of Tarwiyah. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Aishah and found her weeping. He said: What is the matter with you? She said: My matter is that I have menstruated, and people have exited ihram while I have not, and I have not circumambulated the House, and people are now going to Hajj. He said: This is a matter Allah, Mighty and Majestic, decreed for the daughters of Adam, so bathe, then enter ihram for Hajj. So she did, and she stood at all the standing places, until when she became pure she circumambulated the Ka'bah and al-Safa and al-Marwah. Then he said: You have exited from your Hajj and your Umrah together. She said: O Messenger of Allah, I feel distressed that I did not circumambulate the House until I performed Hajj. He said: Take her, O Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, and perform Umrah with her from al-Tan'im, and that was on the night of al-Hasbah."
"15316","Haddathana Musa ibn Dawud, haddathana Ibn Lahi'ah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the believer is like the ear of grain: at times it stands straight and at times it bends and straightens, and the likeness of the disbeliever is like the cedar, upright, unaware, until it falls."
"15317","Haddathana Yahya ibn Ghaylan, haddathana al-Mufaddal, from Khalid ibn Yazid, that he heard Ata, that Ibn al-Zubayr sold the fruit of land of his for three years, and Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari heard of that, so he went out to the mosque among people and said in the mosque: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to sell fruit until it ripens."
"15318","Haddathana Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi, haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: A woman who had stolen was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she sought refuge with a stepson of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah, had it been Fatimah, I would have cut off her hand. So he cut it off. Ibn Abi al-Zinad said: The stepsons of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were Salamah ibn Abi Salamah and Umar ibn Abi Salamah, and she sought refuge with one of them."
"15319","Haddathana Sulayman ibn Dawud, haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid a man to touch another man in a single garment, and a woman to touch another woman in a single garment."
"15320","And he said: When a woman pleases one of you, let him go to his wife, for that turns back something from himself."
"15321","And Jabir said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us from coming by night when we arrive from a journey."
"15322","Haddathana Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Mada'ini, Warqa informed us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The foot of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sprained, so we entered upon him, and he came out to us, or we found him in his chamber sitting before a room, and he prayed sitting while we stood behind him and prayed; when he finished the prayer he said: When I pray sitting, then pray sitting, and when I pray standing, then pray standing, and do not stand as the Persians stand for their tyrants or their kings."
"15323","Haddathana Musa ibn Dawud, haddathana Zuhayr, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling bare land for two years and three years."
"15324","Haddathana Musa and Yahya ibn Adam, they said: Haddathana Zuhayr, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not find two sandals, let him wear two leather socks, and whoever does not find a waist-wrapper, let him wear trousers."
"15325","Haddathana Musa, haddathana Zuhayr, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever plunders plunder is not of us. My father said:"
"15326","Yahya ibn Adam and Abu al-Nadr also narrated it to us:"
"15327","Haddathana Musa ibn Dawud, haddathana Zuhayr, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit until it ripens. My father said:"
"15328","Abu al-Nadr narrated it to us:"
"15329","Haddathana Musa ibn Dawud, haddathana Zuhayr, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Lock the doors, tie the waterskins, cover the vessels, and extinguish the lamps, for Satan does not open a lock, nor untie a knot, nor uncover a vessel, and the little mouse sets fire to the household; and do not send out your grazing animals and your children when the sun sets until the darkness of Isha passes, for the devils are sent out when the sun sets until the darkness of Isha passes."
"15330","Haddathana Ali ibn Ishaq, haddathana Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak, haddathana Umar ibn Salamah ibn Abi Yazid, my father related to me, he said: Jabir said to me: I said: O Messenger of Allah, my father left a debt owed to Jews. He said: I will come to you on Saturday, Allah willing, and that was in the season of dates when the palms were newly ripening. When it was Saturday morning, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me; when he entered to me at a water place of mine, he went to a spring and performed ablution, then stood toward the mosque and prayed two rak'ahs. Then I brought him to a tent of mine, and I spread for him a hair cloak and placed a cushion of hair-woven saddle padding stuffed with fiber, and he reclined upon it. I had not waited but a little until Abu Bakr appeared, and it was as if he saw what the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had done, so he performed ablution and prayed two rak'ahs. I had not waited but a little until Umar came, and he performed ablution and prayed two rak'ahs as if he had seen his two companions. Then they entered, and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, sat at his head, and Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, at his feet."
"15331","Haddathana Ali ibn Ishaq, and haddathana Abd al-Wahhab and Attab: Abd Allah informed us: Umar ibn Salamah ibn Abi Yazid al-Madini informed us: My father related to me, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah say: My father was martyred at Uhud, and my sisters sent me to him with a water-carrying camel of theirs, saying: Go and carry your father on this camel and bury him in the graveyard of Banu Salamah. He said: So I came to him with helpers of mine, and that reached the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was sitting at Uhud, so he called me and said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, he shall not be buried except with his brothers. So he was buried with his companions at Uhud."
"15332","Haddathana Sulayman ibn Dawud, haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: Al-Abbas was holding the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was making covenant with us; when we finished, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have taken and given. He said: So I asked Jabir on that day: How did you pledge to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Upon death? He said: No, but we pledged to him not to flee. I said to him: What about the day of the Tree? He said: I was holding the hand of Umar ibn al-Khattab until we pledged to him. I said: How many were you? He said: We were fourteen hundred; we all pledged to him except al-Jadd ibn Qays, who hid under the belly of a camel. And we sacrificed on that day seventy camels, a camel for every seven."
"15333","Haddathana Sulayman ibn Dawud, haddathana Abd al-Rahman, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Sulami, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is praying, let him not spit before him nor to his right, but let him spit to his left or under his feet."
"15334","Haddathana Sulayman ibn Dawud, haddathana Abd al-Rahman, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: There were images in the Ka'bah, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Umar ibn al-Khattab to erase them; Umar wetted a garment and wiped them with it, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered it with nothing of them in it."
"15335","Haddathana Sulayman ibn Dawud, haddathana Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, al-A'mash related to me, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man who witnessed Badr and al-Hudaybiyah will enter the Fire."
"15336","Haddathana Ya'mur, Abd Allah informed us, Hisham informed us, he said: I heard al-Hasan mention, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prophet has a supplication with which he supplicated, and I have stored my supplication as intercession for my nation on the Day of Resurrection."
"15337","Haddathana Attab ibn Ziyad, haddathana Abd Allah, haddathana Ibn Lahi'ah, Abu al-Zubayr related to me, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Fasting is only a shield with which the servant shields himself from the Fire; it is Mine, and I reward for it."
"15338","Haddathana Attab, haddathana Abd Allah, haddathana Asim ibn Sulayman, from al-Sha'bi, that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prolongs absence, let him not come to his family by night."
"15339","Haddathana Attab, haddathana Abd Allah, Umar ibn Salamah ibn Abi Yazid informed me, he said: My father related to me, he said: Jabir said to me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me, so I set out to slaughter a goat, and it bleated, and he heard its bleating and said: O Jabir, do not cut off milking nor offspring. I said: O Prophet of Allah, it is only a young goat I fed with unripe and ripe dates until it became fat."
"15340","Haddathana Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik, haddathana Zuhayr, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: Abu Shu'ayb had a butcher boy, and when he saw the hardship of the Messenger of Allah, he ordered his boy to prepare food sufficient for five, and he sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Come to us as the fifth of five. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, and a man followed him; when they reached his door he said: You sent to me to come to you as the fifth of five, and this man has followed us; if you permit him, he will enter, otherwise he will return. He said: I have permitted him, O Messenger of Allah. So he entered."
"15341","Haddathana Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik, haddathana Zuhayr, haddathana al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abu Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"15342","Haddathana Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik, haddathana al-Khattab ibn al-Qasim, from Khusayf, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the drop settles in the womb for forty days or forty nights, an angel is sent to it and says: O Lord, what is his provision? And it is told to him. Then he says: O Lord, what is his term? And it is told to him. Then he says: O Lord, male or female? And it is made known. Then he says: O Lord, wretched or happy? And it is made known."
"15343","Haddathana Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik, haddathana Ubayd Allah ibn Amr, from Abd al-Karim, from Ata, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An Umrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj."
"15344","Haddathana Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik, haddathana Ubayd Allah ibn Amr, from Abd al-Karim, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere except the Sacred Mosque, and a prayer in the Sacred Mosque is better than a hundred thousand prayers elsewhere."
"15345","Haddathana Musa ibn Dawud, haddathana Ibn Lahi'ah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by us coming from relieving himself, so we invited him to ajwah dates before us on a shield, and he ate from them, and he had not performed ablution before eating from them."
"15346","Haddathana Khalaf ibn al-Walid, haddathana Khalid, from Humayd al-A'raj, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us while we were reciting the Qur'an, among us the non-Arab and the Bedouin. He said: So he listened and said: Recite, for all is good; and there will come a people who will set it upright as the arrow-shaft is set upright, hastening it and not deferring it."
"15347","Haddathana Khalaf ibn al-Walid, haddathana al-Rabi', meaning Ibn Subayh, from Abu al-Zubayr al-Makki, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us from eating leek and onion."
"15348","Al-Rabi' said: So I asked Ata about that, and he said: Jabir ibn Abd Allah related to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it."
"15349","Haddathana Musa ibn Dawud, haddathana Malik, from Ja'far, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ramal from the Stone until he returned to it."
"15350","Haddathana Abd Allah ibn Muhammad, haddathana Yahya ibn Zakariya ibn Abi Za'idah, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: I have taken your camel for four dinars, and its back is yours until Madinah."
"15351","Haddathana Abd Allah ibn Muhammad, haddathana Abu Khalid al-Ahmar, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Jabir, he said: We were sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he drew a line like this before him and said: This is the path of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. And he drew two lines to its right and two lines to its left. He said: These are the paths of Satan. Then he placed his hand on the black line, then recited this verse: And that this is My path, straight, so follow it, and do not follow the paths, lest they separate you from His path; that He enjoined upon you that you may be God-fearing."
"15352","Haddathana Abd Allah ibn Muhammad, he said: Abdullah, and I heard it myself from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad: Haddathana Hafs, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to enter upon women whose husbands are absent."
"15353","Haddathana Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr, haddathana Zuhayr, haddathana Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is a partner in a dwelling or palm trees has no right to sell until he informs his partner; if he is pleased, he takes, and if he dislikes, he leaves."
"15354","Haddathana Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr, haddathana Zuhayr, haddathana Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and it rained, and he said: Whoever of you wishes, let him pray in his saddle."
"15355","Haddathana Affan, haddathana Abu Awanah, haddathana al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Nubayh al-Anazi, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out from Madinah toward the idolaters to fight them, and my father Abd Allah said to me: O Jabir, it is no harm for you to remain among the watchers of the people of Madinah until you know how our affair ends, for by Allah, were it not that I leave daughters behind me, I would love to be killed before you. He said: While I was among the watchers, my paternal aunt came with my father and my maternal uncle, balancing them upon a water-camel, and entered Madinah with them to bury them in our graveyard, when a man caught up calling: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commands you to return the slain and bury them where they fell. So we returned them and buried them where they were killed. While I was in the caliphate of Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, a man came to me and said: O Jabir ibn Abd Allah, by Allah, the work of Mu'awiyah has exposed your father, and part of him appeared. So I went to him and found him as I had buried him, unchanged except what killing leaves; so I covered him. He said: My father left a debt of dates upon him, and one of his creditors pressed me in demanding, so I came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, my father was stricken on such and such day and left a debt of dates upon me, and one of his creditors pressed me in demanding, so I would love for you to help me with him, that he may grant me respite for part of his dates until this coming harvest. He said: Yes, I will come to you, Allah willing, near midday. And he came with his two disciples, then asked permission and entered. I said to my wife: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has come to me today at midday, so let me not see you, and do not harm the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in my house with anything, nor speak to him. So he entered, and she spread for him a bedding and a pillow, and he laid his head and slept. He said: And I said to a freed slave of mine: Slaughter this young goat, a tame fat one, and be quick; finish it before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wakes, and I am with you. We kept at it until we finished it while he slept. I said to him: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wakes he will call for purification water, and I fear when he finishes he will rise, so do not finish his ablution before you place the young goat before him. When he rose he said: O Jabir, bring me purification water. He had not finished his purification before I placed the young goat before him. He looked at me and said: As if you knew our love for meat; call Abu Bakr for me. He said: Then he called his two disciples who were with him, and they entered, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck his hand and said: In the name of Allah, eat. So they ate until they were full, and much meat remained. He said: By Allah, the assembly of Banu Salamah were looking at him, and he was dearer to them than their own eyes, yet none of them approached him fearing to harm him. When he finished, he rose and his companions rose, and they went out before him, and he would say: Leave my back for the angels. And I followed them until they reached the threshold of the door. He said: And my wife brought out her chest, veiled behind a roof-shelter in the house, and said: O Messenger of Allah, pray for me and for my husband, may Allah bless you. So he said: May Allah bless you and your husband. Then he said: Call for me so-and-so, my creditor who pressed me in demanding. So he came, and he said: Grant Jabir ibn Abd Allah respite, meaning to ease, for part of your debt upon his father until this coming harvest. He said: I will not do it, and he made excuse, saying: It is only orphans wealth. He said: Where is Jabir? He said: Here I am, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Measure for him, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will fulfill him. I looked at the sky, and the sun had declined. He said: Prayer, O Abu Bakr. So they hastened to the mosque. I said: Bring your vessels near. So I measured for him from the ajwah, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, fulfilled him, and there remained for us of the dates such and such. So I came hurrying to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his mosque as if I were a spark, and I found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had prayed. I said: O Messenger of Allah, did you not see that I measured for my creditor his dates, and Allah fulfilled him, and there remained for us of the dates such and such. He said: Where is Umar ibn al-Khattab? So he came hurrying and he said: Ask Jabir ibn Abd Allah about his creditor and his dates. He said: I will not ask him; I knew that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, would fulfill him, since you informed that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, would fulfill him. He repeated this phrase to him three times, each time he said: I will not ask him; and he would not be reviewed after the third time. So he said: O Jabir, what happened with your creditor and your dates? He said: I said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, fulfilled him, and there remained for us of the dates such and such. So I returned to my wife and said: Did I not forbid you to speak to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? She said: Did you think Allah, Mighty and Majestic, would bring the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to my house and then he would leave without my asking him to pray for me and my husband before he leaves?"
"15356","Haddathana Affan, haddathana Shu'bah, haddathana Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hasan ibn Ali, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man shaded over and said: It is not righteousness to fast while traveling."
"15357","Haddathana Affan, haddathana Sulaym ibn Hayyan, haddathana Sa'id ibn Mina, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has surplus land or water, let him cultivate it or let his brother cultivate it, and do not sell it. So I asked Sa'id: What is: do not sell it? Renting? He said: Yes."
"15358","Haddathana Affan, haddathana Wuhayb, haddathana Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: He related to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ka'b ibn Ujrah, I seek refuge for you with Allah from the rule of fools. He said: And what is that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Rulers will come after me; whoever enters upon them and believes their reports and helps them in their wrongdoing, they are not of me and I am not of them, and they will not come to me at the Pond; and whoever does not enter upon them, nor believe their reports, nor help them in their wrongdoing, those are of me and I am of them, and those will come to me at the Pond. O Ka'b ibn Ujrah, prayer is devotion, and fasting is a shield, and charity extinguishes sin as water extinguishes fire. O Ka'b ibn Ujrah, none will enter Paradise whose flesh grew from unlawful earnings; the Fire is more deserving of him. O Ka'b ibn Ujrah, people are two goers: a goer who sells himself and destroys his neck, and a goer who buys himself and frees his neck."
"15359","Haddathana Affan, haddathana Shu'bah, al-Aswad ibn Qays informed me, from Nubayh al-Anazi, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you enters by night, let him not come upon his family suddenly."
"15360","Haddathana Affan, haddathana al-Mubarak, Nasr ibn Rashid related to me in the year one hundred, from one who related to him, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to plaster graves or to build over them."
"15361","Haddathana Affan, haddathana al-Mubarak, Nasr ibn Rashid related to me, from one who related to him, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, he said: A man of Banu Udhrah died in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and was buried at night, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a man be buried at night until prayer is performed over him, unless they are compelled to that."
"15362","Haddathana Ali ibn Abd Allah, haddathana Sufyan, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw as if I was brought a lump of dates, and I chewed it in my mouth and found in it a pit that hurt me, so I spat it out; then I took another and chewed it and found in it a pit, so I spat it out; then I took another and chewed it and found in it a pit, so I spat it out. Abu Bakr said: Let me interpret it. He said: He said: Interpret it. He said: It is your army which you sent; it will be safe and gain spoils, then meet a man who will invoke your protection, so they will leave him; then meet a man who will invoke your protection, so they will leave him; then meet a man who will invoke your protection, so they will leave him. He said: Likewise, said the angel."
"15363","Haddathana Affan, haddathana Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad, haddathana Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled preemption in everything undivided; when boundaries fall and roads are set, there is no preemption."
"15364","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq and Muhammad ibn Bakr, they said: Ibn Jurayj informed us: Ibn Shihab al-Zuhri informed me, from the hadith of Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, he informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled: Any man given an umra for himself and his offspring, saying: I have given it to you and your offspring as long as any of you remains, then it is, Abu Bakr said: for the one given it, and Abd al-Razzaq said: for the one given it, and it does not return to its owner, since he gave it as a gift in which inheritance applies."
"15365","Haddathana Affan, haddathana Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned the Aqabah pillar on the day of sacrifice in the forenoon, and stoned during the remaining days of Tashriq after the sun declined."
"15366","Haddathana Yazid ibn Harun, from Sa'id: Qatadah informed us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray over a brother of yours who died in other than your land. They said: Who, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Al-Najashi Ashamah. He said: So I said: So you lined up over him? He said: Yes, I was in the third row."
"15367","Haddathana Bahz, haddathana Muthanna ibn Sa'id, haddathana Talhah ibn Nafi', from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took his hand to his house; when he arrived he said: Is there any lunch or dinner, Talhah doubted. He said: So they brought out a piece of bread. He said: Is there any condiment? They said: No, except some vinegar. He said: Bring it near, for vinegar is an excellent condiment. Jabir said: I have loved vinegar ever since I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Talhah said: I have loved vinegar ever since I heard it from Jabir."
"15368","Haddathana Ali ibn Bahr, haddathana Isa ibn Yunus, haddathana al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, I am only a human; so any man of the Muslims whom I insulted, or flogged, or cursed, make it for him purification and reward."
"15369","Haddathana Ali ibn Bahr, haddathana Isa, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, similar to it, except that he said: purification and mercy."
"15370","Haddathana Ali ibn Bahr, haddathana Isa ibn Yunus, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you cleans with stones, let him clean with three."
"15371","Haddathana Ali ibn Bahr, haddathana Isa, haddathana al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No Muslim man or woman, nor believing man or woman, is afflicted by illness but Allah removes thereby some of his sins."
"15372","Haddathana Ali ibn Bahr, haddathana Hatim ibn Isma'il, recitation to us from his book, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ata, from Abd al-Malik ibn Jabir, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when his shirt was slit from its collar until he took it out from his legs. The people looked at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: I was commanded concerning my sacrificial camels which I sent forth, that they be garlanded today and marked today at such and such water, so I wore a shirt and forgot, and I could not take my shirt out from my head; and he had sent his sacrificial animals from Madinah while he remained in Madinah."
"15373","Haddathana Ali ibn Abd Allah, haddathana Abu Safwan, and he named him in other than this hadith Abd Allah ibn Sa'id ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan: Yunus ibn Yazid informed me, from Ibn Shihab: Ata related to me that Jabir ibn Abd Allah claimed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats garlic or onion, let him keep away from us, or he said: let him keep away from our mosque, and let him sit in his house. End of the Musnad of Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him."
